1
00:00:01,002 --> 00:00:03,738
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:03,772 --> 00:00:06,775
♪ WAY DOWN IN DEEP 13 ♪

3
00:00:06,808 --> 00:00:09,810
♪ DR. FORRESTER
AND TV'S FRANK ♪

4
00:00:09,843 --> 00:00:13,013
♪ WERE HATCHING
AN EVIL SCHEME ♪

5
00:00:13,047 --> 00:00:16,083
♪ THEY HIRED A TEMP
BY THE NAME OF MIKE ♪

6
00:00:16,117 --> 00:00:19,220
♪ JUST A REGULAR JOE
THEY DIDN'T LIKE ♪

7
00:00:19,253 --> 00:00:22,323
♪ THEIR EXPERIMENT
NEEDED A GOOD TEST CASE ♪

8
00:00:22,357 --> 00:00:23,892
♪ SO THEY CONKED HIM
ON THE NOGGIN ♪

9
00:00:23,925 --> 00:00:25,993
♪ AND THEY SHOT HIM INTO SPACE ♪

10
00:00:26,027 --> 00:00:28,530
GET ME DOWN!

11
00:00:28,563 --> 00:00:31,867
♪ WE'LL SEND HIM
CHEESY MOVIES ♪

12
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:34,835
♪ THE WORST WE CAN FIND
LA-LA-LA ♪

13
00:00:34,868 --> 00:00:37,838
♪ HE'LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

14
00:00:37,872 --> 00:00:41,275
♪ AND WE'LL MONITOR HIS MIND
LA-LA-LA ♪

15
00:00:41,308 --> 00:00:44,212
♪ NOW KEEP IN MIND
MIKE CAN'T CONTROL ♪

16
00:00:44,245 --> 00:00:47,282
♪ WHERE THE MOVIES BEGIN OR END
LA-LA-LA ♪

17
00:00:47,315 --> 00:00:50,352
♪ HE'LL TRY
TO KEEP HIS SANITY ♪

18
00:00:50,385 --> 00:00:55,423
♪ WITH THE HELP
OF HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

19
00:00:55,457 --> 00:00:56,992
♪ ROBOT ROLL CALL ♪

20
00:00:57,025 --> 00:00:58,358
- CAMBOT!
- SHOW YOURSELF!

21
00:00:58,392 --> 00:00:59,627
- GYPSY!
- I'M NOT READY!

22
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,528
- TOM SERVO!
- HELLO THERE!

23
00:01:01,562 --> 00:01:03,197
- CROW!
- THAT'S ONE "O"!

24
00:01:03,230 --> 00:01:06,033
♪ IF YOU'RE WONDERING
HOW HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

25
00:01:06,067 --> 00:01:09,203
♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS
LA-LA-LA ♪

26
00:01:09,237 --> 00:01:12,240
♪ JUST REPEAT TO YOURSELF,
"IT'S JUST A SHOW ♪

27
00:01:12,273 --> 00:01:15,177
♪ "I SHOULD
REALLY JUST RELAX ♪

28
00:01:15,210 --> 00:01:20,047
♪ FOR MYSTERY SCIENCE
THEATER 3000!" ♪

29
00:01:33,528 --> 00:01:35,397
- OKAY, YOU GUYS READY?
- YES.

30
00:01:35,430 --> 00:01:38,833
♪ OH, THE YELLOW ROSE
OF TEXAS ♪

31
00:01:38,867 --> 00:01:40,568
HI, EVERYONE. WELCOME TO
THE SATELLITE OF LOVE.

32
00:01:40,602 --> 00:01:43,505
I'M MIKE, THIS IS TOM SERVO,
AND THIS IS CROW T. ROBOT.

33
00:01:43,538 --> 00:01:44,838
AND WE'RE JUST WORKING ON
ONE OF THOSE

34
00:01:44,872 --> 00:01:46,307
BELOVED OLD STANDARDS.

35
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:47,775
YOU KNOW, THESE ARE
THE KIND OF SONGS

36
00:01:47,808 --> 00:01:49,110
- EVERYONE CAN ENJOY--
- HEY, HEY, HEY, MIKE!

37
00:01:49,143 --> 00:01:50,945
THERE'S SOMETHING COMING IN
ON THE HEXFIELD.

38
00:01:50,978 --> 00:01:52,247
- HUH?
- WHOA.

39
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:54,882
- HELLO? YES?
- YEAH, HELLO, ARNIE.

40
00:01:54,915 --> 00:01:56,550
UH, ARNIE?

41
00:01:56,583 --> 00:01:57,885
ARNIE, YOU SOUND WEIRD.

42
00:01:57,918 --> 00:02:00,788
LOOK, YOU GOTTA GET OVER HERE
AND SIGN THESE PAPERS.

43
00:02:00,822 --> 00:02:02,790
I KNOW YOU'RE NOT THRILLED
TO HEAR FROM ME.

44
00:02:02,823 --> 00:02:04,758
UH, MA'AM, I THINK
YOU MAY HAVE THE WRONG NUMBER.

45
00:02:04,792 --> 00:02:08,362
THERE'S NO ARNIE HERE.

46
00:02:08,395 --> 00:02:11,665
WOW. THAT WAS WEIRD.
WELL, LET'S GO.

47
00:02:11,698 --> 00:02:15,303
♪ OH, THE YELLOW ROSE
OF TEXAS ♪

48
00:02:15,337 --> 00:02:18,072
MIKE, THE HEXFIELD AGAIN.

49
00:02:18,105 --> 00:02:19,440
LOOK, I KNOW ARNIE'S THERE.

50
00:02:19,473 --> 00:02:21,775
YOU DON'T GOTTA
COVER FOR HIM, CHOPPER.

51
00:02:21,808 --> 00:02:23,310
CHOPPER, THIS IS YOU, RIGHT?

52
00:02:23,343 --> 00:02:25,313
LOOK, YOU DON'T HAVE TO COVER
FOR HIM,

53
00:02:25,347 --> 00:02:28,148
HE JUST HAS TO GET OVER HERE
AND SIGN THESE PAPERS.

54
00:02:28,182 --> 00:02:29,750
- LADY, UH--
- HOLD ON. WHAT?

55
00:02:29,783 --> 00:02:31,252
- WHAT'S FOR SUPPER?
- EGGS.

56
00:02:31,285 --> 00:02:32,620
- AGAIN?
- YES, AGAIN!

57
00:02:32,653 --> 00:02:34,955
SO, IS ARNIE STAYING THERE
WITH YOU, CHOPPER?

58
00:02:34,988 --> 00:02:37,225
UH, THIS MAY TAKE A WHILE.
WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK.

59
00:02:37,258 --> 00:02:40,127
LOOK, CHOP, DO NOT LET HIM
TAKE ADVANTAGE OF YOU.

60
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:43,665
HE'S A SWEET GUY,
BUT HE TAKES, TAKES, TAKES.

61
00:02:43,698 --> 00:02:47,502
MOMMY'S ON THE PHONE!

62
00:02:47,535 --> 00:02:49,470
♪♪

63
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:57,145
OF COURSE, I WAS ONLY ABOUT 16
WHEN ME AND ARNIE GOT HOOKED UP.

64
00:02:57,178 --> 00:03:01,348
MAN, HE WAS SO GOOD LOOKING...
BACK THEN.

65
00:03:01,382 --> 00:03:04,152
NOWADAYS, IT'S JUST
HIS WHISKEY BREATH,

66
00:03:04,185 --> 00:03:07,655
THIS DUMP, AND 4:00AM CALLS
FROM THE POLICE.

67
00:03:07,688 --> 00:03:09,890
OH, HOLD ON,
MY BACON'S ON FIRE.

68
00:03:09,923 --> 00:03:13,060
NOW. NOW!

69
00:03:13,093 --> 00:03:14,628
WOW.

70
00:03:14,662 --> 00:03:17,598
WELL, YOU KNOW, SHE DID HAVE
A CERTAIN JE NE SAIS QUOI

71
00:03:17,632 --> 00:03:18,933
ABOUT HER, DIDN'T SHE?

72
00:03:18,967 --> 00:03:20,133
NO.

73
00:03:20,167 --> 00:03:22,037
LET'S SEE
WHAT BENNY AND JUNE ARE DOING.

74
00:03:22,070 --> 00:03:24,972
HELLO, MURRAY, AUTOMATA.

75
00:03:25,005 --> 00:03:27,142
SAY, WHAT'S ONE OF
THE MOST POPULAR

76
00:03:27,175 --> 00:03:29,843
FORMS OF EXERCISE
THIS MONTH? HMM?

77
00:03:29,877 --> 00:03:33,080
HMM? WELL, THAT'S RIGHT.
THE RECUMBENT BIKE.

78
00:03:33,113 --> 00:03:35,417
AS I SEE IT,
RECUMBENT CREATORS WERE AFRAID

79
00:03:35,450 --> 00:03:37,485
TO MAKE THEM
TOO COMFORTABLE.

80
00:03:37,518 --> 00:03:39,787
WELL, I'M NOT AFRAID. TA-DA!

81
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:42,123
THE RECOMFY BIKE!
[CHUCKLES]

82
00:03:42,157 --> 00:03:45,460
DOCTOR F., COULD YOU TUCK ME IN
BEFORE MY RIDE?

83
00:03:45,493 --> 00:03:48,228
OF COURSE, FRANKLIN.
THERE YOU GO.

84
00:03:48,262 --> 00:03:49,930
CHECK OUT THE READING LAMP,
NIGHT-STAND,

85
00:03:49,963 --> 00:03:52,800
AND GOOSE-DOWN COMFORTER.

86
00:03:52,833 --> 00:03:55,102
OF COURSE, WE MAY HAVE TO DITCH
THE WHEELS AND THE PEDALS

87
00:03:55,135 --> 00:03:58,072
TO MAKE ROOM FOR THE ICE MACHINE
AND ESPRESSO BAR, BUT--

88
00:03:58,105 --> 00:04:01,675
UH, DOCTOR,
I CAN'T GET IT TO GO.

89
00:04:01,708 --> 00:04:03,410
WELL, TRY HARDER, YOU LOAD.

90
00:04:03,443 --> 00:04:06,447
BUT THERE'S KIND OF
A LOT OF STUFF HERE.

91
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:08,917
"THERE'S KIND OF
A LOT OF STUFF HERE."

92
00:04:08,950 --> 00:04:11,118
NAPPY TIME,
DON'T YOU THINK, FRANK?

93
00:04:11,152 --> 00:04:12,720
BACK UP TO YOU, MARGO.

94
00:04:12,753 --> 00:04:14,822
[SNORING]

95
00:04:14,855 --> 00:04:17,525
WELL, THAT IS REALLY,
REALLY USELESS.

96
00:04:17,558 --> 00:04:19,527
[LAUGHTER]

97
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:21,562
ANYWAY, OUR INVENTION
PUMPS NEW LIFE

98
00:04:21,595 --> 00:04:23,665
INTO THAT AGE OLD DECK
OF PLAYING CARDS.

99
00:04:23,698 --> 00:04:25,367
LET'S FACE IT,
WITH ONLY 52 CARDS,

100
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:26,900
THERE'S ONLY SO MUCH
YOU CAN DO.

101
00:04:26,933 --> 00:04:29,670
A JACK, QUEEN, KING,
GIVE ME A BREAK!

102
00:04:29,703 --> 00:04:31,972
AAH, THAT'S WHY WE EACH CAME UP
WITH OUR OWN NEW CARDS.

103
00:04:32,005 --> 00:04:33,908
TO SORT OF
SPICE THINGS UP A BIT.

104
00:04:33,942 --> 00:04:36,077
MINE IS THE EIGHT
OF CHRIS LEMMON.

105
00:04:36,110 --> 00:04:38,312
SON OF THE VERY TALENTED
JACK LEMMON.

106
00:04:38,345 --> 00:04:39,613
CHRIS LEMMON?

107
00:04:39,647 --> 00:04:41,415
YEAH, I JUST LOVED HIM
IN DUET.

108
00:04:41,448 --> 00:04:44,918
HUH, WELL, MY CARD IS TODD.

109
00:04:44,952 --> 00:04:47,022
JUST TODD.
TODD IS HELPFUL.

110
00:04:47,055 --> 00:04:48,355
AND TODD IS THERE FOR YOU.

111
00:04:48,388 --> 00:04:50,425
- TODD? TODD?
- YEAH.

112
00:04:50,458 --> 00:04:51,958
WELL, IS HE--
WHAT VALUE IS HE?

113
00:04:51,992 --> 00:04:53,460
IS HE ROYALTY OR WHAT?

114
00:04:53,493 --> 00:04:55,830
WELL, TODD DOESN'T LIKE
TO BE PIGEONHOLED.

115
00:04:55,863 --> 00:04:58,598
HE SAYS THE TERM "ROYALTY"
PUTS LIMITATIONS
ON YOUR DREAMS.

116
00:04:58,632 --> 00:05:00,502
WELL, OKAY, WHAT HAPPENS
IF I LAY DOWN AN EIGHT

117
00:05:00,535 --> 00:05:01,902
OF CHRIS LEMMONS?
WHO WINS?

118
00:05:01,935 --> 00:05:04,372
AH, NO. TODD SAYS, IN AMERICA,
VALUES ARE MEANINGLESS.

119
00:05:04,405 --> 00:05:06,207
AND HE DOESN'T
LIKE COMPETITION.

120
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:07,742
ACTUALLY, NOW THAT
YOU BRING IT UP,

121
00:05:07,775 --> 00:05:09,810
TODD SAYS YOUR CHRIS LEMMON
CARD HAS ISSUES

122
00:05:09,843 --> 00:05:11,345
HE NEEDS TO WORK THROUGH.

123
00:05:11,378 --> 00:05:14,215
WELL, IF IT'S OKAY WITH TODD,
WHY DOESN'T CROW GO NEXT?

124
00:05:14,248 --> 00:05:15,450
- WHAT DO YOU GOT, BUDDY?
- OH, YES, YES!

125
00:05:15,483 --> 00:05:16,817
MY CARD IS THE...

126
00:05:16,850 --> 00:05:18,887
[TRUMPET SOUND]
CROW OF DIAMONDS!

127
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,287
WOO! CROW OF DIAMONDS.

128
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:21,622
CROW, I THINK YOU MISSED
THE WHOLE POINT

129
00:05:21,655 --> 00:05:22,857
OF THIS EXERCISE.

130
00:05:22,890 --> 00:05:24,258
WELL, TODD THINKS IT'S OKAY.

131
00:05:24,292 --> 00:05:26,127
TODD...

132
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:28,195
[SNORING]

133
00:05:28,228 --> 00:05:32,067
[LAUGHS]

134
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:35,035
ENOUGH OF YOUR
TOUCHY-FEELY CRAP, NELSON.

135
00:05:35,068 --> 00:05:36,903
TODAY'S MOVIE
REALLY GETS GOING

136
00:05:36,937 --> 00:05:39,340
ABOUT TWO MINUTES
BEFORE THE CLOSING CREDITS.

137
00:05:39,373 --> 00:05:41,542
IT'S ANOTHER
BERT I. GORDON PAIN PARADE

138
00:05:41,575 --> 00:05:44,478
CALLED
THE BEGINNING OF THE END.

139
00:05:44,512 --> 00:05:47,382
AND I HOPE YOU HAVE
HEALTH INSURANCE.

140
00:05:47,415 --> 00:05:50,383
[GIGGLES]

141
00:05:50,417 --> 00:05:53,153
ON YOUR LIFE!

142
00:05:53,187 --> 00:05:55,490
AND THEN LATER ON,
TODD'S GONNA SHOW ME

143
00:05:55,523 --> 00:05:57,625
THIS REALLY GREAT
MASSAGE TECHNIQUE,

144
00:05:57,658 --> 00:06:00,027
AND PHOTOS FROM HIS WEEKEND
WITH ROBERT FULGHUM, AND--

145
00:06:00,060 --> 00:06:02,028
[BUZZER SOUNDS]
AH, MOVIE SIREN, DOG GONE IT.

146
00:06:02,062 --> 00:06:04,132
OH, WE GOT A MOVIE SIREN.
COME ON, MOVIE SIREN!

147
00:06:17,378 --> 00:06:19,947
HEY, YOU KNOW, I'VE GOT
A GOOD PLACE FOR TODD.

148
00:06:19,980 --> 00:06:21,815
- YEE!
- OH, THAT'S FINE.

149
00:06:21,848 --> 00:06:24,352
- BOY, YOU'RE FICKLE.
- I'LL DEAL WITH IT.

150
00:06:24,385 --> 00:06:26,920
LOOKS LIKE THIS IS WHERE
ICHABOD CRANE TAKES HIS DATES.

151
00:06:26,953 --> 00:06:29,057
OOH, AND YOU KNOW, IT'D BE SEXY
UNTIL YOU THINK,

152
00:06:29,090 --> 00:06:30,925
"IT MIGHT BE MY PARENTS!
OH, MY GOD!"

153
00:06:30,958 --> 00:06:31,958
NO!

154
00:06:31,992 --> 00:06:33,560
♪ ASK ME WHY ♪

155
00:06:33,593 --> 00:06:36,763
HEY, HOW DOES HE SING
WHILE HE'S KISSING HER?

156
00:06:36,797 --> 00:06:38,498
♪ NEVER BE AFRAID ♪

157
00:06:38,532 --> 00:06:44,338
YOU TASTE LIKE VINYL.

158
00:06:44,372 --> 00:06:46,007
BET YOU ANYTHING
THERE'S GONNA BE A CLAW

159
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:50,043
HANGING FROM
THEIR DOOR HANDLE.

160
00:06:50,077 --> 00:06:54,415
OOH, NO, NOT THERE.
YEAH, THAT'S IT. OH, YEAH. OH.

161
00:06:54,448 --> 00:06:56,983
[SCREAMS]
DON'T GIVE ME A HICKEY!

162
00:06:57,017 --> 00:06:58,652
WHAT-- WHAT?

163
00:06:58,685 --> 00:07:01,388
HUH. OH. WHAT?

164
00:07:01,422 --> 00:07:03,557
THE BEGINNING
OF THE END ALREADY?

165
00:07:03,590 --> 00:07:08,930
- I DON'T...
- IT JUST STARTED!

166
00:07:08,963 --> 00:07:12,767
AND THE JUNE TAYLOR DANCERS!

167
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:15,870
IS THIS A FLASHBACK
TO PREVIOUS CREDITS?

168
00:07:15,903 --> 00:07:18,305
I WONDER WHAT THAT LADY SAW
WHEN SHE SCREAMED THERE.

169
00:07:18,338 --> 00:07:20,273
LOU FERRIGNO?

170
00:07:20,307 --> 00:07:21,675
MAYBE.

171
00:07:21,708 --> 00:07:24,345
OH, STOP IT.
I'M GETTING NAUSEATED.

172
00:07:24,378 --> 00:07:26,947
- MAYBE SHE SAW BIGFOOT.
- BIGFOOT PIZZA?

173
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:30,618
- NO, I... MAYBE.
- I DON'T...

174
00:07:30,652 --> 00:07:34,122
OH, COULD I GET SOME DRAMAMINE
FOR THIS CREDIT SEQUENCE?

175
00:07:34,155 --> 00:07:36,023
- YOU OKAY, BUDDY?
- YEAH, I THINK SO.

176
00:07:36,057 --> 00:07:41,428
PLEASE WELCOME YOUR NEW RICHMOND
HIGH-SCHOOL MARCHING BAND.

177
00:07:41,462 --> 00:07:44,332
- HONEY.
- MIKE, I THINK I NEED A BUCKET.

178
00:07:44,365 --> 00:07:46,167
[VOMITING]
CREDIT SICK, THERE.

179
00:07:46,200 --> 00:07:48,802
HANG IN THERE.

180
00:07:48,835 --> 00:07:50,203
AH, I'M OKAY.

181
00:07:50,237 --> 00:07:51,705
PUT YOUR HEAD
BETWEEN YOUR KNEES.

182
00:07:51,738 --> 00:07:52,907
OKAY.

183
00:07:52,940 --> 00:07:54,842
- DON'T SLIP IN IT.
- DOES THAT FEEL BETTER?

184
00:07:54,875 --> 00:07:56,810
- YEAH.
- NOW.

185
00:07:56,843 --> 00:07:59,247
- WOW.
- UGH.

186
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:00,748
SO THIS IS LIKE
BEGINNING OF THE END

187
00:08:00,782 --> 00:08:03,417
BOLD, CONDENSED FONT
HERE, HUH?

188
00:08:03,450 --> 00:08:05,753
OH, NO.
[VOMITING]

189
00:08:05,787 --> 00:08:07,087
HONEY, DO YOU THINK
YOU COULD KEEP DOWN

190
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:09,157
SOME 7-UP AND SODA CRACKERS?

191
00:08:09,190 --> 00:08:11,892
- UH, NO.
- SOME LUKE WARM PORK?

192
00:08:11,925 --> 00:08:14,695
[VOMITING]
I'M SORRY, I'M SORRY!

193
00:08:14,728 --> 00:08:17,965
ONE MORE TIME!

194
00:08:17,998 --> 00:08:22,803
[HUMMING THEME]

195
00:08:22,837 --> 00:08:24,205
THERE'S TOO MANY NOTES.

196
00:08:24,238 --> 00:08:25,940
SO IS SOMETHING GOING TO HAPPEN?

197
00:08:25,973 --> 00:08:28,042
I DON'T KNOW.

198
00:08:29,343 --> 00:08:31,212
- HUH?
- [MICHAEL] HUMS.

199
00:08:31,245 --> 00:08:35,448
FOLKS, WE'LL START THE MOVIE
AS SOON AS OUR RIDE
GETS HERE.

200
00:08:35,482 --> 00:08:39,353
MAN, THAT CAR RADIO
IS LOUD, HUH?

201
00:08:39,387 --> 00:08:44,425
YOU KNOW, BIRD EYE SURE DOESN'T
SKIMP ON THE OPENING.

202
00:08:44,458 --> 00:08:46,227
THIS IS 2-5-4
ON THE LUDLOW SWING--

203
00:08:46,260 --> 00:08:49,930
AND WE'RE HOPELESSLY LOST.

204
00:08:49,963 --> 00:08:52,467
WE'LL BE CHECKING-IN
IN 45 MINUTES.

205
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:56,170
[DISPATCHER]
10-4, CAR 2-5-4.
KLP 6-4-6.

206
00:08:56,203 --> 00:08:58,105
YOU WANT TO SAY HI
TO HEADQUARTERS?

207
00:08:58,138 --> 00:09:00,307
PULL OVER.
I SAW SOMETHING.

208
00:09:00,340 --> 00:09:02,008
IF THEY HAD TO PULL OVER
EVERY TIME YOU SEE SOMETHING,

209
00:09:02,042 --> 00:09:05,345
IT'S GOING TO BE A LONG RIDE.

210
00:09:05,378 --> 00:09:06,947
RANTOUL IS ONLY
FIVE MILES AWAY.

211
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:08,382
YESTERDAY,
IT WAS 10 MILES AWAY!

212
00:09:08,415 --> 00:09:11,552
SOMEONE'S MOVING THE SIGN.

213
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:16,957
- WHOA!
- SOMETHING HAPPENED
OFF SCREEN HERE.

214
00:09:16,990 --> 00:09:18,858
UH, MS. MANSFIELD?

215
00:09:18,892 --> 00:09:21,328
I'LL REPORT IN.

216
00:09:21,362 --> 00:09:24,698
YOU KNOW, THESE THINGS JUST
DON'T DO ANYTHING TO ME
EMOTIONALLY ANYMORE.

217
00:09:24,732 --> 00:09:27,668
I'M DRAINED.

218
00:09:27,702 --> 00:09:29,170
HI. ME AGAIN.

219
00:09:29,203 --> 00:09:32,072
CAR 2-5-4 TO CHAMPAGNE URBANA.

220
00:09:32,105 --> 00:09:34,242
[DISPATCHER]
URBANA TO 2-5-4, GO AHEAD.

221
00:09:34,275 --> 00:09:38,012
CAR 2-5-4 TO URBANA,
WE'RE INVESTIGATING AN ACCIDENT

222
00:09:38,045 --> 00:09:40,948
AT JUNCTION 45
AND LUDLOW CUTOFF.

223
00:09:40,982 --> 00:09:44,785
- FOUL PLAY SUSPECTED.
- NO DUH.

224
00:09:44,818 --> 00:09:47,253
UH, HOLD ON,
I'M GONNA READ YOU A POEM.

225
00:09:47,287 --> 00:09:50,658
OH YEAH, THE DRIVER MAY
HAVE BEEN WILLIAM SUMMERFIELD.

226
00:09:50,692 --> 00:09:54,495
177 DECATUR STREET,
LUDLOW, ILLINOIS.

227
00:09:54,528 --> 00:09:55,830
OINK BADA-BOOM.

228
00:09:55,863 --> 00:09:57,765
[DISPATCHER]
ONE OF YOU STAY ON THE SCENE,

229
00:09:57,798 --> 00:09:59,667
THE OTHER INVESTIGATE
THE LUDLOW ADDRESS. 10-4.

230
00:09:59,700 --> 00:10:02,803
CAR 2-5-4.
KLP 6-4-6.

231
00:10:02,837 --> 00:10:06,373
MAN, HE'S GOOD.

232
00:10:06,407 --> 00:10:09,010
WHELP, THIS IS IT, I GUESS.

233
00:10:09,043 --> 00:10:10,912
I DON'T KNOW WHAT TO SAY, CARL.

234
00:10:10,945 --> 00:10:12,847
I'LL NEVER FORGET YOU.

235
00:10:12,880 --> 00:10:14,915
- BUT--
- NO, JUST GO.

236
00:10:18,485 --> 00:10:19,620
LOOKS LIKE A GIRL'S SWEATER.

237
00:10:19,653 --> 00:10:22,690
THE CAR WAS ATTACKED
BY A SWEATER!

238
00:10:22,723 --> 00:10:26,293
SO WHY IS WALTER WINCHELL
IN THIS SCENE?

239
00:10:26,327 --> 00:10:27,962
HEY, IT'S MY SIZE!

240
00:10:27,995 --> 00:10:29,597
[DISPATCHER]
COME IN CAR 88.

241
00:10:29,630 --> 00:10:31,465
UH, EXCUSE ME. THAT'S FOR ME.
I'M THE MAN.

242
00:10:33,267 --> 00:10:36,403
♪ ANGELS OF THE MORNING ♪

243
00:10:36,437 --> 00:10:38,005
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS]

244
00:10:38,038 --> 00:10:41,042
- YELLO!
- CAR 88 TO CHAMPAIGN, URBANA.
McKENNIZE HERE, GO AHEAD.

245
00:10:41,075 --> 00:10:43,643
[DISPATCHER]
CAR 2-5-4 HAS FAILED TO REPORT.

246
00:10:43,677 --> 00:10:45,078
IS THAT CAR IN YOUR AREA?

247
00:10:45,112 --> 00:10:47,815
- I BEG YOUR PARDON!
- NO, NOT HERE.

248
00:10:47,848 --> 00:10:52,587
10-4 CAR 88.
THIS IS KLP 6-4-6 URBANA,

249
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:54,988
CALLING CAR 2-5-4,
COME IN CAR 2-5-4.

250
00:10:55,022 --> 00:10:57,357
McKENNZIE? McKENNZIE!
YOU'RE BREAKING EVERY RULE
IN THE BOOK!

251
00:10:57,390 --> 00:11:00,828
URBANA TO CAR 2-5-4,
COME IN CAR 2-5-4.

252
00:11:00,862 --> 00:11:02,563
UH, HOUSTON WE GOT A PROBLEM.

253
00:11:02,597 --> 00:11:06,967
[DISPATCHER]
URBANA TO CAR 2-5-4,
COME IN CAR 2-5-4.

254
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,570
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACH]

255
00:11:09,603 --> 00:11:12,372
I WAS THE FIRST ONE HERE!

256
00:11:12,405 --> 00:11:14,642
- HELLO, I'M AT LUDLOW!
- IT'S REALLY DARK!

257
00:11:14,675 --> 00:11:16,777
- THE WHOLE TOWN'S DESTROYED!
- IT'S REALLY NEAT.

258
00:11:16,810 --> 00:11:19,113
- EVERYBODY'S GONE!
- I'M LONELY.

259
00:11:19,147 --> 00:11:22,015
YOU GOT TO DO SOMETHING.
YOU WON'T BELIEVE THIS.

260
00:11:22,048 --> 00:11:24,152
SEND HELP!
LOTS OF HELP, QUICK!

261
00:11:24,185 --> 00:11:26,220
OH, FORGET IT.

262
00:11:27,655 --> 00:11:29,457
EXECUTIVE PRODUCER
STEVEN BOCHCO.

263
00:11:30,858 --> 00:11:33,827
YEAH, BASICALLY I RUN
THE ARMY, YEP.

264
00:11:33,860 --> 00:11:35,195
HOW YOU GUYS DOING OVER THERE?

265
00:11:35,228 --> 00:11:38,398
I DON'T FEEL VERY FUN TODAY.
COME ON. JUST COME ON.

266
00:11:38,432 --> 00:11:42,937
THE DIRECTOR'S BROTHER-IN-LAW,
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN.

267
00:11:42,970 --> 00:11:45,138
WHAT THE-- HEY!

268
00:11:45,172 --> 00:11:47,207
YOU KNOW, BIRD EYE DID THIS ALL
IN ONE TAKE.

269
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:50,010
- AMAZING.
- ♪♪ [MICHAEL HUMS]

270
00:11:50,043 --> 00:11:51,745
YOU KNOW, WHEN I WAS A BOY
WE DIDN'T HAVE FAST MOVIES.

271
00:11:51,778 --> 00:11:53,447
SOMETIMES WE HAD TO WAIT
THREE OR FOUR HOURS

272
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:54,748
FOR SOMETHING TO HAPPEN.

273
00:11:54,782 --> 00:11:57,350
I LOVE THAT STORY.

274
00:11:57,383 --> 00:11:59,420
ANYONE NEED TO GO
TO THE BATHROOM, GO NOW!

275
00:11:59,453 --> 00:12:05,292
[SERVO]
♪ HOW WILL YOU MAKE IT
ON YOUR OWN? ♪

276
00:12:07,427 --> 00:12:10,363
SHE'S GOT A RADIO TUNED
TO THE MARCHING BAND STATION.

277
00:12:10,397 --> 00:12:13,267
ALL SOUSA, ALL THE TIME.

278
00:12:13,300 --> 00:12:16,570
HMM. MUST GET VIVARIN.

279
00:12:16,603 --> 00:12:18,538
[SERVO SNORES]

280
00:12:18,572 --> 00:12:22,442
NOW, THIS IS AN IMPROV
THAT REALLY WENT NOWHERE.

281
00:12:22,475 --> 00:12:23,543
[SERVO AND CROW LAUGH]

282
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:28,948
OKAY, MEN, PRIVATE REESE
IS FEELING VULNERABLE TODAY.

283
00:12:28,982 --> 00:12:30,317
IT'S UP TO US TO CHEER HIM UP.

284
00:12:30,350 --> 00:12:34,722
YOUR HOVER BUICK
WILL GET YOU THERE IN STYLE.

285
00:12:34,755 --> 00:12:36,557
HOVER BUICK.

286
00:12:36,590 --> 00:12:38,425
SERVICEMEN, GREAT.

287
00:12:41,762 --> 00:12:43,963
[CROW MIMICS TIRES SCREECHING]

288
00:12:46,833 --> 00:12:48,868
ALL RIGHT, LADY,
JUST FOLLOW THE ARROWS.

289
00:12:48,902 --> 00:12:50,637
- ANY CHANCE
OF GETTING THROUGH?
- NOPE.

290
00:12:50,670 --> 00:12:51,838
WHAT HAPPENED?

291
00:12:51,872 --> 00:12:55,142
LOOK, LADY, JUST DETOUR.
WILL YOU, PLEASE?

292
00:12:55,175 --> 00:12:57,077
DON'T MAKE ME PULL YOU
FROM YOUR CAR

293
00:12:57,110 --> 00:13:00,713
AND BEAT YOU
WITH MY NIGHTSTICK.

294
00:13:00,747 --> 00:13:05,585
MMM, QUIET.
SMOOTH RIDE.

295
00:13:05,618 --> 00:13:07,220
OH, NOW THEY'RE
GONNA HAVE TO TURN

296
00:13:07,253 --> 00:13:11,958
THE REAR PROJECTION SCREEN
AROUND, TOO.

297
00:13:11,992 --> 00:13:14,562
GUYS, THIS IS SO NOT ILLINOIS.

298
00:13:14,595 --> 00:13:16,263
[CROW GIGGLES]

299
00:13:19,198 --> 00:13:23,003
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS]

300
00:13:23,037 --> 00:13:26,140
MMM. I WONDER WHAT THEY'RE
DOING HERE. WELL--

301
00:13:26,173 --> 00:13:28,308
GEE, MARTIAL LAW IS FUN.

302
00:13:28,342 --> 00:13:31,812
♪♪ [SERVO VOCALIZES]

303
00:13:31,845 --> 00:13:36,217
WHOA,
THAT IS A TEXAS STYLE CAMERA.

304
00:13:36,250 --> 00:13:37,985
TELL HIM TO TAKE
THAT DETAIL OUT OF THERE.

305
00:13:38,018 --> 00:13:39,653
THE OLD MAN IS SENDING
A REPLACEMENT.

306
00:13:39,687 --> 00:13:41,822
THAT'S MY LINE!
FINALLY REMEMBERED.

307
00:13:41,855 --> 00:13:43,823
I'M SORRY, SOLDIER,
I SHOULD'VE EXPLAINED.

308
00:13:43,857 --> 00:13:46,660
I'M AUDREY AIMS,
NATIONAL WIRE SERVICE.

309
00:13:46,693 --> 00:13:48,628
- YES, MA'AM.
- HOW DO I GET THERE?

310
00:13:48,662 --> 00:13:50,998
SORRY, MY ORDERS ARE
TO LET NO ONE THROUGH.

311
00:13:51,032 --> 00:13:53,267
WELL, THAT SURELY DOESN'T
INCLUDE THE PRESS.

312
00:13:53,300 --> 00:13:56,403
I'M SORRY, MA'AM.
BUT NO ONE--

313
00:13:56,437 --> 00:13:58,272
GOOD JOB TODAY, LANCE.
CARRY ON.

314
00:13:58,305 --> 00:14:00,473
WELL, WAS IT VERY BAD?

315
00:14:00,507 --> 00:14:02,375
- SO ASHAMED.
- MANY GET HURT?

316
00:14:02,408 --> 00:14:04,612
LOOK, LADY, YOU'RE NOT GOING
TO FISH ANY INFORMATION
OUT OF ME.

317
00:14:04,645 --> 00:14:08,915
NOW, WHY DON'T YOU GET BACK
ON THE MAIN ROAD?
IT'S A ABOUT MILE SOUTH.

318
00:14:08,948 --> 00:14:10,850
HEAR THAT, GUYS?
I REALLY TOLD HER OFF.

319
00:14:10,883 --> 00:14:13,353
MILE SOUTH, HA!

320
00:14:14,788 --> 00:14:17,892
HE LIKES ME.
I THINK WE'RE DATING.

321
00:14:17,925 --> 00:14:22,428
OH, I LOCKED
MY KEYS IN THE CAR-- OH!

322
00:14:26,067 --> 00:14:29,035
HEY! THE CAR STARTED
WITHOUT HER EVEN DOING ANYTHING.

323
00:14:29,068 --> 00:14:33,073
[ALL MIMIC
MARCHING BAND MUSIC]

324
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:42,650
JIMMY JAM DOES HIS THING.

325
00:14:42,683 --> 00:14:44,918
- [DISPATCHER]
UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE--
- I'M PAUL FREES.

326
00:14:44,952 --> 00:14:47,788
A TRAFFIC WILL CONTINUE
TO BE ROUTED AROUND
THE LUDLOW AREA

327
00:14:47,822 --> 00:14:48,955
ACCORDING TO SPECIAL ORDERS--

328
00:14:48,988 --> 00:14:51,392
- GOOD MORNING.
- I'M TURNING MYSELF IN.

329
00:14:51,425 --> 00:14:53,060
I'D LIKE TO SEE
YOUR COMMANDING OFFICER.

330
00:14:53,093 --> 00:14:54,495
HERE'S A LITTLE SOMETHING
FOR YOU.

331
00:14:54,528 --> 00:14:56,063
WELL, I'M SORRY
BUT THE COLONEL'S BUSY.

332
00:14:56,097 --> 00:14:57,330
TOO BUSY FOR THESE?

333
00:14:57,363 --> 00:14:59,433
PERHAPS CAPTAIN BARTON
CAN HELP YOU.

334
00:15:02,302 --> 00:15:04,505
"I AM DEAF.
PLEASE GIVE ME MONEY." HM.

335
00:15:04,538 --> 00:15:06,873
- SEND HER IN.
- MA'AM.

336
00:15:06,907 --> 00:15:09,208
FILE ON DALTON TRUMBO, SIR.

337
00:15:09,242 --> 00:15:11,312
THANKS, LIEUTENANT.

338
00:15:11,345 --> 00:15:12,312
SIT DOWN, PLEASE.

339
00:15:12,345 --> 00:15:14,482
NOW, GET UP AGAIN.
[CHUCKLES]

340
00:15:14,515 --> 00:15:17,383
AREN'T YOU THE AUDREY AIMES
WHO COVERED KOREA
FOR THAT PICTURE MAGAZINE?

341
00:15:17,417 --> 00:15:19,018
- THAT'S RIGHT.
- WELL, I HATED IT.

342
00:15:19,052 --> 00:15:21,288
I READ THE BOOK YOU WROTE
AFTER THE WAR.
LIKED IT VERY MUCH.

343
00:15:21,322 --> 00:15:22,790
WHY, THANK YOU.

344
00:15:22,823 --> 00:15:25,158
YOU'RE WITH NATIONAL WIRE
SERVICE NOW.

345
00:15:25,192 --> 00:15:27,093
I WAS ON MY WAY
TO CHANUTE FIELD

346
00:15:27,127 --> 00:15:29,830
TO DO A PICTURE STORY
ON A NEW JET PLANE
THEY'RE UNVEILING,

347
00:15:29,863 --> 00:15:32,265
AND I RAN INTO A ROAD BLOCK.

348
00:15:32,298 --> 00:15:34,568
- SO?
- YEAH, YOU'RE RIGHT.
WHAT WAS I THINKING ABOUT?

349
00:15:34,602 --> 00:15:36,637
THERE WAS A TOWN
BEYOND THAT ROAD BLOCK,

350
00:15:36,670 --> 00:15:39,172
A TOWN THAT ISN'T THERE
ANYMORE.

351
00:15:39,205 --> 00:15:41,308
UNTIL WE FIND OUT
EXACTLY WHAT HAPPENED,

352
00:15:41,342 --> 00:15:42,810
WE'D LIKE TO AVOID PUBLICITY.

353
00:15:42,843 --> 00:15:45,512
DO YOU HAVE ANY IDEA
WHAT HAPPENED?

354
00:15:45,545 --> 00:15:47,147
I'M SORRY, MISS AIMES.

355
00:15:47,180 --> 00:15:49,550
MAYBE AFTER
THIS WHOLE COVER-UP,
WE CAN HAVE COFFEE SOMETIME?

356
00:15:49,583 --> 00:15:51,552
YOU CAN'T SUPPRESS
A STORY LIKE THIS.

357
00:15:51,585 --> 00:15:53,220
WE'RE NOT TRYING TO,
MISS AIMES,

358
00:15:53,253 --> 00:15:54,755
BUT UNTIL WE HAVE
MORE FACTS...

359
00:15:54,788 --> 00:15:57,357
♪ THIS IS THE ARMY,
AUDREY AIMES ♪

360
00:15:57,390 --> 00:15:59,125
WILL YOU GIVE US YOUR WORD YOU
WON'T RELEASE A STORY

361
00:15:59,158 --> 00:16:00,393
UNTIL WE GIVE THE GO-AHEAD?

362
00:16:00,427 --> 00:16:01,928
YOU HAVE MY WORD.

363
00:16:01,962 --> 00:16:03,597
GOD, YOUR HAIR
SMELLS WONDERFUL.

364
00:16:03,630 --> 00:16:05,032
SOMETIME DURING THE NIGHT,

365
00:16:05,065 --> 00:16:07,333
THE TOWN OF LUDLOW
WAS COMPLETELY DEMOLISHED.

366
00:16:07,367 --> 00:16:08,968
- AND?
- TOWN'S POPULATION,

367
00:16:09,002 --> 00:16:10,970
ABOUT A HUNDRED AND FIFTY
PEOPLE, VANISHED.

368
00:16:11,003 --> 00:16:12,672
VANISHED?

369
00:16:12,705 --> 00:16:14,408
NO BODIES, NOTHING.

370
00:16:14,442 --> 00:16:15,875
IT WAS
SOME DAVID COPPERFIELD STUNT.

371
00:16:15,908 --> 00:16:17,143
THERE MUST BE SOME TRACE.

372
00:16:17,177 --> 00:16:18,912
I KNOW IT'S HARD TO BELIEVE,
MISS AIMES...

373
00:16:18,945 --> 00:16:20,313
BUT I'M KOKO TAYLOR.

374
00:16:20,347 --> 00:16:22,048
WE'VE A SPECIAL DETAIL GOING
THROUGH THE WRECKAGE

375
00:16:22,082 --> 00:16:24,017
FOR TWO SOLID HOURS
AND COULDN'T FIND A THING.

376
00:16:24,050 --> 00:16:25,218
TWO SOLID HOURS?

377
00:16:25,252 --> 00:16:26,553
WE DON'T KNOW.

378
00:16:26,587 --> 00:16:28,855
ON ACCOUNT OF THE FACT
WE'RE NOT VERY SMART.

379
00:16:28,888 --> 00:16:32,192
150 PEOPLE JUST DON'T VANISH
INTO THIN AIR.

380
00:16:32,225 --> 00:16:35,162
WE'RE STILL TRYING TO FIND OUT
WHAT HAPPENED,

381
00:16:35,195 --> 00:16:37,097
IF YOU'D LIKE TO SIT IN.

382
00:16:37,130 --> 00:16:38,465
YES, THANK YOU.
I WOULD.

383
00:16:38,498 --> 00:16:40,167
I'VE GOT A CLARINET IN MY CAR.

384
00:16:42,235 --> 00:16:45,338
HEY...
[IMITATING ARNOLD ZIFFEL'S
FROM GREEN ACRES]

385
00:16:45,372 --> 00:16:48,975
DAVE, WHAT TIME DID YOU LEAVE
LUDLOW LAST NIGHT?

386
00:16:49,008 --> 00:16:50,877
MUST'VE BEEN AFTER 11:00.

387
00:16:50,910 --> 00:16:52,278
ARNOLD ZIFFEL'S FATHER.

388
00:16:52,312 --> 00:16:54,448
MY SON-IN-LAW WAS WATCHING
THE TELEVISION NEWS AT 10:30,

389
00:16:54,482 --> 00:16:55,882
SO I SAT DOWN
AND WATCHED THAT.

390
00:16:55,915 --> 00:16:57,283
THEN I CAUGHT LETTERMAN.

391
00:16:57,317 --> 00:17:00,020
AND MY DAUGHTER WANTED ME
TO SIT THERE AND TALK A WHILE.

392
00:17:00,053 --> 00:17:02,655
THEN I GOT TO THINKING
THAT I HAD TO GET UP EARLY.

393
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:05,258
- YOUR POINT, PLEASE?
- SO I HAD TO GO.

394
00:17:05,292 --> 00:17:07,828
- DID YOU NOTICE ANYTHING
STRANGE...
- HOIMAN!

395
00:17:07,862 --> 00:17:10,263
...ABOUT THE HOUSE OR ABOUT
THE WAY THE FAMILY ACTED?

396
00:17:10,297 --> 00:17:13,600
OTHER THAN WANTING MY SON-IN-LAW
TO DIAPER ME, NOPE.

397
00:17:13,633 --> 00:17:16,137
- WHEN YOU'RE DRIVING
OUT OF TOWN...
- HM, NICE LIKENESS.

398
00:17:16,170 --> 00:17:18,705
NOTHING OUT OF WAY
IN THE STREET, THE BUILDING,
OR THE SKY?

399
00:17:18,738 --> 00:17:21,275
NO UNUSUAL LIGHT,
SOME SOUND OR MOVEMENT?

400
00:17:21,308 --> 00:17:23,277
OBJECTION, YOUR HON-- OH.

401
00:17:23,310 --> 00:17:25,345
WELL, I HEARD SOMETHING
SOUND LIKE THUNDER.

402
00:17:25,378 --> 00:17:27,413
COULDN'T SEE IT SO GOOD
'CAUSE OF THE RAIN.

403
00:17:27,447 --> 00:17:28,448
...A PLANE WENT OVER.

404
00:17:28,482 --> 00:17:30,350
YOU ARE SO HIGH.

405
00:17:30,383 --> 00:17:32,953
ALL RIGHT, DAVE.
I CAN CALL YOU AGAIN
IF I NEED YOU?

406
00:17:32,987 --> 00:17:36,590
- OH, YES, YES.
- YOU KNOW YOU CAN CALL ME DAD.

407
00:17:36,623 --> 00:17:40,193
MY NEXT GUEST, ROSE MARIE!
[IMITATES CHEERING]

408
00:17:40,227 --> 00:17:41,995
THE TELEPHONE COMPANY'S
OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPTS?

409
00:17:42,028 --> 00:17:43,963
IT WAS A MISTAKE.
I DIDN'T MEAN TO--

410
00:17:43,997 --> 00:17:47,200
THE LAST CALL FROM LUDLOW
AT 11:59 P.M.

411
00:17:47,233 --> 00:17:49,837
WHEN DID YOU FIRST NOTICE
ANYTHING WRONG WITH
THE LUDLOW CONNECTION?

412
00:17:49,870 --> 00:17:52,907
- ANDREW JACKSON?
- OLD HICKORY.

413
00:17:52,940 --> 00:17:54,942
I PHONED THE COMPANY LINESMAN
TO GO OUT THERE RIGHT AWAY.

414
00:17:54,975 --> 00:17:57,677
SO THE TELEPHONE LINES
COULD'VE GONE DOWN

415
00:17:57,710 --> 00:18:00,413
ANYWHERE BETWEEN
11:59 AND 4:45.

416
00:18:00,447 --> 00:18:01,682
YES, YES,
IS THAT WHAT YOU WANT?

417
00:18:01,715 --> 00:18:03,017
ALL RIGHT, THANKS.

418
00:18:03,050 --> 00:18:04,752
YOU'VE BEEN VERY HELPFUL.

419
00:18:04,785 --> 00:18:06,687
MAN, SHE'S A TOUGH OLD BIRD.

420
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:07,988
[WHISTLES]
OKAY, BYE.

421
00:18:08,022 --> 00:18:09,355
OH, COLONEL STURGEON,

422
00:18:09,388 --> 00:18:10,890
MISS AIMES,
NATIONAL WIRE SERVICE.

423
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:12,158
HOW DO YOU DO?

424
00:18:12,192 --> 00:18:13,260
AUDREY AIMES?

425
00:18:13,293 --> 00:18:14,695
I'VE READ A LOT OF YOUR STUFF,

426
00:18:14,728 --> 00:18:15,895
SEEN A LOT
OF YOUR PHOTOGRAPHS.

427
00:18:15,928 --> 00:18:17,263
READING YOUR CLEAVAGE NOW.

428
00:18:17,297 --> 00:18:18,832
- YELLO!
- YES?

429
00:18:18,865 --> 00:18:20,367
[MAN ON PHONE]
SET TO GO SIR,
WHENEVER YOU'RE READY.

430
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:21,802
I'LL BE RIGHT THERE.

431
00:18:21,835 --> 00:18:23,403
ALL RIGHT, I'VE GOT TO PICK UP
PHIL AT PLAY PRACTICE.

432
00:18:23,437 --> 00:18:24,705
I HOPE YOU UNDERSTAND
OUR PROBLEM,

433
00:18:24,738 --> 00:18:26,138
OUR NEED TO KEEP THIS QUIET.

434
00:18:26,172 --> 00:18:27,473
YES, CAPTAIN'S BRIEFED ME.

435
00:18:27,507 --> 00:18:29,008
THEN HE PANTSED ME.

436
00:18:29,042 --> 00:18:31,778
IF ANYONE WANTS ME,
I CAN BE REACHED
IN LUDLOW BY RADIO.

437
00:18:31,812 --> 00:18:33,380
HOW'S CHANCES
OF ME GOING ALONG?

438
00:18:33,413 --> 00:18:35,982
- NOT THIS TRIP.
MAYBE LATER.
- MAYBE LATER?

439
00:18:36,015 --> 00:18:37,483
IN ANY CASE, NOT UNTIL WE
KNOW WHAT'S OUT THERE.

440
00:18:37,517 --> 00:18:38,552
OH, BY THE WAY, COLONEL,

441
00:18:38,585 --> 00:18:39,987
MY CAMERA WAS TAKEN FROM ME

442
00:18:40,020 --> 00:18:41,288
AT THE ROAD BLOCK,
BY ONE OF YOUR MEN.

443
00:18:41,322 --> 00:18:43,690
I'LL GIVE ORDERS
TO HAVE IT RELEASED.

444
00:18:43,723 --> 00:18:45,658
I'LL TAKE THE LONG WAY
OUT OF HERE.

445
00:18:45,692 --> 00:18:47,327
BERT I. GORDON FILM AFTER ALL.

446
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:48,328
SEE YA.

447
00:18:48,362 --> 00:18:49,630
WHAT A LOSER.

448
00:18:49,663 --> 00:18:52,432
THERE HAS TO BE A LOGICAL
EXPLANATION FOR THIS.

449
00:18:52,465 --> 00:18:56,270
A TOWN OF 150 PEOPLE
JUST DOESN'T DISAPPEAR.

450
00:18:56,303 --> 00:18:57,537
THIS ONE DID.

451
00:18:57,570 --> 00:18:59,940
YES, BUT IN GENERAL
THEY DON'T DISAPPEAR.

452
00:18:59,973 --> 00:19:01,408
THAT'S MY POINT.

453
00:19:04,912 --> 00:19:08,982
HEY, NOW SHE'S ON
THE ABBOTT AND COSTELLO
SHOW SET.

454
00:19:09,015 --> 00:19:10,983
OH, MAN,
I SHOULD'VE TAKEN HOME EC

455
00:19:11,017 --> 00:19:13,820
OR GONE INTO TEACHING
OR NURSING LIKE
ALL THE OTHER GIRLS.

456
00:19:13,853 --> 00:19:16,188
GOSH, I'M 21
AND I'M STILL NOT MARRIED.

457
00:19:16,222 --> 00:19:17,857
YELLO!

458
00:19:17,890 --> 00:19:20,127
[WOMAN ON PHONE]
CHICAGO MOBILE SERVICE
OPERATOR.

459
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:22,362
I'D LIKE TO PLACE
A PERSON-TO-PERSON CALL,
PLEASE,

460
00:19:22,395 --> 00:19:24,397
TO MR. NORMAN TAGGART.

461
00:19:24,430 --> 00:19:27,467
- ME BEING
ONE OF THE PERSONS OF COURSE.
- ...NATIONAL WIRE SERVICE.

462
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:30,703
THE NUMBER
IS MURRAY HILL 4, 4836.

463
00:19:30,737 --> 00:19:34,407
- MAN, I MISS THOSE KIND
OF PHONE NUMBERS.
- NEW YORK.

464
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:35,775
[IMITATING FRANK NELSON]
EEEEYEEESSSS?

465
00:19:35,808 --> 00:19:37,978
LINED UP THAT JET PLANE STORY
ALREADY?

466
00:19:38,012 --> 00:19:39,880
I'M NOT ON THE JET STORY.
NORM, LISTEN.

467
00:19:39,913 --> 00:19:41,782
I'M ONTO SOMETHING
I THINK CAN BE REAL BIG.

468
00:19:41,815 --> 00:19:43,483
ME.

469
00:19:43,517 --> 00:19:45,085
OH, HE'S RIGHT HANDED.

470
00:19:45,118 --> 00:19:48,522
WHERE?

471
00:19:48,555 --> 00:19:49,957
SCRIBBLE, SCRIBBLE.

472
00:19:49,990 --> 00:19:51,925
SCRIBBLE, SCRIBBLE
AS THOUGH I'M WRITING SOMETHING.

473
00:19:51,958 --> 00:19:53,960
WHAT DO YOU MEAN
WE CAN'T PRINT IT?

474
00:19:53,993 --> 00:19:56,763
I'VE GIVEN MY WORD
TO HOLD OFF FOR A WHILE.

475
00:19:56,797 --> 00:19:58,432
- NOW, LISTEN, NORM.
- YOU'RE FIRED.

476
00:19:58,465 --> 00:20:00,600
A PLANE FLEW OVER LUDLOW
LAST NIGHT ABOUT MIDNIGHT,

477
00:20:00,633 --> 00:20:02,937
JUST ABOUT THE TIME
THE LID BLEW OFF.
CHECK ON IT.

478
00:20:02,970 --> 00:20:04,337
AND CHECK WASHINGTON.

479
00:20:04,370 --> 00:20:07,173
SEE IF THEY HAD AN ATOMIC
INSTALLATION IN THE LUDLOW AREA.

480
00:20:07,207 --> 00:20:08,408
OKAY.

481
00:20:08,442 --> 00:20:09,777
WHO AM I, YOUR STRINGER?

482
00:20:09,810 --> 00:20:12,178
CALL ME BACK AS SOON AS YOU
HAVE ANYTHING, RIGHT?

483
00:20:12,212 --> 00:20:13,313
GOOD-BYE.

484
00:20:13,347 --> 00:20:15,982
- JEEZ, HER GUY FRIDAY.
- COOL.

485
00:20:18,952 --> 00:20:23,090
♪♪ [HUMMING]

486
00:20:25,358 --> 00:20:27,860
HEY, WE FOUND THE 150 PEOPLE.
YOU WERE RIGHT.

487
00:20:27,893 --> 00:20:30,263
SORRY, MISS, YOU CAN'T--
OH, IT'S YOU AGAIN.

488
00:20:30,297 --> 00:20:31,665
I KNOW I CAN'T

489
00:20:31,698 --> 00:20:33,333
BUT I'D LIKE TO HAVE MY CAMERA
BACK, PLEASE.

490
00:20:33,367 --> 00:20:36,235
COLONEL STURGEON SAID HE WAS
GOING TO SPEAK TO SOMEBODY.

491
00:20:36,268 --> 00:20:42,142
HEY, CORPORAL, MATHIAS,
SHE WANTS HER CAMERA BACK.

492
00:20:42,175 --> 00:20:43,543
[PHONE RINGS]

493
00:20:43,577 --> 00:20:45,578
I'LL GET IT.
IT'S PROBABLY FOR ME.

494
00:20:45,612 --> 00:20:46,680
YELLO.

495
00:20:46,713 --> 00:20:48,848
OH, DO YOU KNOW OUR JACKPOT
TODAY?

496
00:20:48,882 --> 00:20:50,083
WHAT'S THE SCORE?

497
00:20:50,117 --> 00:20:52,052
WRONG TRACK, BABY.

498
00:20:52,085 --> 00:20:54,988
THE AIRLINES CONFIRM
A COMMERCIAL LINER
OVER LUDLOW

499
00:20:55,022 --> 00:20:57,323
AT 12:03 LAST NIGHT.

500
00:20:57,357 --> 00:20:58,992
AND THERE ARE NO
ATOMIC INSTALLATIONS,

501
00:20:59,025 --> 00:21:02,028
SECRET OR OTHERWISE,
WITHIN 75 MILES OF LUDLOW.

502
00:21:02,062 --> 00:21:04,497
WELL, IT WAS A POSSIBILITY.

503
00:21:04,530 --> 00:21:06,298
THE ONLY
WHO'VE BEEN PLAYING AROUND

504
00:21:06,332 --> 00:21:08,668
WITH RADIOACTIVE MATERIALS
IN YOUR VICINITY

505
00:21:08,702 --> 00:21:10,337
IS THE U.S. DEPARTMENT
OF AGRICULTURE.

506
00:21:10,370 --> 00:21:12,605
- ANYTHING THERE?
- DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE?

507
00:21:12,638 --> 00:21:14,942
YEAH, THEY'VE GOT
AN EXPERIMENTAL PROJECT,

508
00:21:14,975 --> 00:21:16,377
JUST OUTSIDE PAXTON.

509
00:21:16,410 --> 00:21:18,378
U.S. DEPARTMENT
OF AGRICULTURE,

510
00:21:18,412 --> 00:21:20,580
ILLINOIS EXPERIMENTAL STATION.

511
00:21:20,613 --> 00:21:22,415
OKAY, I'VE GOT THAT.
I'LL KEEP IN TOUCH.

512
00:21:22,448 --> 00:21:25,685
I'VE GOTTA GO.
I'VE GOT SOMEONE IN MY OFFICE.

513
00:21:25,718 --> 00:21:27,020
♪♪ [HUMMING]

514
00:21:27,053 --> 00:21:29,857
I HAVE A CITY IDEA-- CHICAGO.
I THINK IT MIGHT WORK.

515
00:21:29,890 --> 00:21:31,958
[CHUCKLES]
LET'S GET OUT OF HERE.

516
00:21:31,992 --> 00:21:33,893
♪♪ [WHISTLES]

517
00:21:49,442 --> 00:21:51,845
- [WHISTLES]
- WOW, I DON'T KNOW ABOUT
THIS MOVIE, YOU GUYS.

518
00:21:51,878 --> 00:21:52,978
NOTHING'S HAPPENING.

519
00:21:53,012 --> 00:21:54,848
I THINK MAYBE WE SHOULD CALL
THE MADS.

520
00:21:54,882 --> 00:21:55,948
WE CAN DO THAT, RIGHT?

521
00:21:55,982 --> 00:21:57,950
WELL, I GUESS,

522
00:21:57,983 --> 00:21:59,485
BUT I WOULDN'T ADVISE IT.

523
00:21:59,518 --> 00:22:01,822
YEAH, I MEAN, WHY GET THEM
INVOLVED?

524
00:22:01,855 --> 00:22:04,223
I MEAN, I JUST THINK
WE SHOULD CALL THE MADS.

525
00:22:04,257 --> 00:22:05,492
WHY DON'T WE CALL THE MADS?

526
00:22:05,525 --> 00:22:06,593
- NO.
- NO.

527
00:22:06,627 --> 00:22:10,863
♪ MY BABY TAKES
THE MORNING TRAIN ♪

528
00:22:10,897 --> 00:22:13,100
♪ SHE WORKS TILL 9:00-- ♪

529
00:22:13,133 --> 00:22:17,737
FRANK? I COULD NOT STOP PICKING
AT THAT PAN OF LEMON BARS.

530
00:22:17,770 --> 00:22:19,973
I ATE HALF THE PAN.

531
00:22:20,007 --> 00:22:23,243
YOU'RE SO LUCKY YOU COULD EAT
ANYTHING AND NOT WORRY.

532
00:22:23,277 --> 00:22:26,847
OH, PSHAW, I'D GIVE ANYTHING
TO HAVE THAT COMPLEXION
OF YOURS.

533
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:28,882
OH, FRANK.

534
00:22:28,915 --> 00:22:35,820
HEY, WOW, V.I.C.I. IS ON.

535
00:22:38,892 --> 00:22:42,762
YOU KNOW, FRANK,
THIS IS EXACTLY WHAT
I WANTED TO DO TODAY,

536
00:22:42,795 --> 00:22:44,932
JUST HAVE THE WHOLE DAY
TO OURSELVES.

537
00:22:44,965 --> 00:22:47,800
I'M DECLARING THIS
NATIONAL OUR DAY.

538
00:22:47,833 --> 00:22:49,002
[LAUGHS]

539
00:22:49,035 --> 00:22:50,970
PLEASE, DO NOT LET ME EAT
ALL OF THIS.

540
00:22:51,003 --> 00:22:53,005
WELL, I SHOULDN'T.

541
00:22:59,913 --> 00:23:03,283
OH, MY GOD, FRANK.
SWITCH ON A GAME.
SWITCH ON A GAME.

542
00:23:03,317 --> 00:23:05,852
[CHEERING,
COACH WHISTLE ON TV]

543
00:23:05,885 --> 00:23:09,688
[GRUNTING]

544
00:23:09,722 --> 00:23:12,358
SO, I GUESS WE CAN CALL
THE MADS, HUH?

545
00:23:12,392 --> 00:23:13,527
- YEAH.
- YEAH.

546
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:14,962
BUT YOU KNOW WHAT?

547
00:23:14,995 --> 00:23:16,797
I DON'T THINK I'M GOING TO DO
THAT FOR A WHILE.

548
00:23:16,830 --> 00:23:18,532
NO, I DON'T THINK SO.

549
00:23:18,565 --> 00:23:19,665
WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK.

550
00:23:27,907 --> 00:23:31,143
STRANGER FELLERS.

551
00:23:31,177 --> 00:23:33,213
COME ON IN.
JUST WORKING ON PLUTONIUM.

552
00:23:33,247 --> 00:23:36,817
HERMAN BADILLO.

553
00:23:36,850 --> 00:23:40,820
I'M LOOKING
FOR THE FARNSTEIN WEDDING.

554
00:23:40,853 --> 00:23:43,723
TOMATOES LIKE BRAHMS.

555
00:23:43,757 --> 00:23:45,425
WOW, SUDDENLY SALAD.

556
00:23:45,458 --> 00:23:48,093
EXCUSE ME.

557
00:23:48,127 --> 00:23:49,897
MAN, THOSE ARE CHERRY TOMATOES.

558
00:23:49,930 --> 00:23:51,030
I BEG YOUR PARDON.

559
00:23:51,063 --> 00:23:52,765
I NEVER PROMISED YOU
A ROSE GARDEN.

560
00:23:56,168 --> 00:23:58,372
HEY, THIS IS THE PRODUCE
DEPARTMENT, ISN'T IT?

561
00:23:58,405 --> 00:23:59,738
I BEG YOUR PARDON.

562
00:23:59,772 --> 00:24:03,643
WE'RE WORKING OVERTIME
TO KEEP DOM DELUISE FED.

563
00:24:03,677 --> 00:24:07,480
THE MORE HE IGNORES ME,
THE MORE I'M ATTRACTED TO HIM.

564
00:24:07,513 --> 00:24:08,582
OH!

565
00:24:08,615 --> 00:24:10,117
- HELLO.
- I'M PETER GRAVES.

566
00:24:10,150 --> 00:24:14,420
HELLO.
I SPOKE TO HIM, BUT I GUESS
HE DIDN'T HEAR ME.

567
00:24:14,453 --> 00:24:16,388
OH, HE'S A DEAF MUTE.

568
00:24:16,422 --> 00:24:17,723
YOU INSENSITIVE LITTLE...

569
00:24:17,757 --> 00:24:18,725
WORKING WITH RADIATION
CAN BE DANGEROUS.

570
00:24:18,758 --> 00:24:19,792
I SMELLED THAT.

571
00:24:19,825 --> 00:24:20,793
AN ACCIDENT LAST YEAR

572
00:24:20,827 --> 00:24:21,895
COST HIM HIS SPEECH
AND HIS HEARING.

573
00:24:21,928 --> 00:24:23,095
AND 600 BUCKS.

574
00:24:23,128 --> 00:24:24,797
OH, I'M SORRY.

575
00:24:24,830 --> 00:24:26,867
I'M LOOKING
FOR THE PROJECT DIRECTOR.

576
00:24:26,900 --> 00:24:28,335
I'M THE PROJECT DIRECTOR.

577
00:24:28,368 --> 00:24:29,335
MY NAME'S ED WAINWRIGHT.

578
00:24:29,368 --> 00:24:31,905
WHAT CAN I DO FOR YOU?

579
00:24:31,938 --> 00:24:35,008
OH, EXCUSE ME A MINUTE.

580
00:24:35,042 --> 00:24:36,710
KIND OF A VAGUE SIGN LANGUAGE.

581
00:24:36,743 --> 00:24:38,445
I'M SORRY, FRANK.

582
00:24:38,478 --> 00:24:40,813
OH, WE DROPPED
HIS CHOCOLATE SAMPLER.

583
00:24:40,847 --> 00:24:43,717
NOTHING TO WORRY ABOUT.
JUST A SLIGHT CATASTROPHE.

584
00:24:43,750 --> 00:24:45,818
YOU HAVE THESE CATASTROPHES
VERY OFTEN?

585
00:24:45,852 --> 00:24:47,987
WELL, AS OFTEN AS WE HAVE
GOVERNMENT COVER-UPS.

586
00:24:48,020 --> 00:24:50,290
ALL THE TIME.
IT'S HARD TO KEEP THESE THINGS
FROM GETTING IN.

587
00:24:50,323 --> 00:24:51,925
THESE ARE SNAILS.

588
00:24:51,958 --> 00:24:53,760
LAST SUMMER
IT WAS CATERPILLARS,

589
00:24:53,793 --> 00:24:56,663
AND AFTER THAT IT WAS
GRASSHOPPERS BY THE DROVE.

590
00:24:56,697 --> 00:24:57,663
THIS GUY EATS ANYTHING.

591
00:24:57,697 --> 00:24:59,165
AND JUST LAST WEEK
IT WAS BEETLES.

592
00:24:59,198 --> 00:25:00,867
NOW IT'S BAGEL DOGS.

593
00:25:00,900 --> 00:25:02,202
WHAT CAN I DO FOR YOU?

594
00:25:02,235 --> 00:25:04,203
MR. WAINWRIGHT,
I'M AUDREY AIMES.

595
00:25:04,237 --> 00:25:06,372
I'M WITH NATIONAL
WIRE SERVICE.

596
00:25:06,405 --> 00:25:09,175
I SUPPOSE YOU HEARD ABOUT
WHAT HAPPENED IN LUDLOW.

597
00:25:09,208 --> 00:25:10,910
- YES.
- I'D LIKE TO KISS YOU
FULL ON THE MOUTH.

598
00:25:10,943 --> 00:25:12,478
I'M TRYING TO FIND OUT
WHAT WAS RESPONSIBLE,

599
00:25:12,512 --> 00:25:13,747
AND IT OCCURRED TO ME

600
00:25:13,780 --> 00:25:15,148
THAT RADIATION OF SOME SORT

601
00:25:15,182 --> 00:25:17,317
MIGHT'VE CAUSED
THE DESTRUCTION OUT THERE.

602
00:25:17,350 --> 00:25:18,985
NO, I DON'T THINK SO.
HERE.

603
00:25:19,018 --> 00:25:21,822
LET ME SHOW YOU
A GIANT CROUTON
WE'RE WORKING ON.

604
00:25:21,855 --> 00:25:25,425
WE'RE THE ONLY PEOPLE
AROUND HERE USING
RADIOACTIVE MATERIALS.

605
00:25:25,458 --> 00:25:27,727
MAYBE I SHOULDN'T BE KEEPING
MY LUNCH IN HERE.
I DON'T KNOW.

606
00:25:27,760 --> 00:25:28,962
AND ISOTOPES AREN'T EXPLOSIVE.

607
00:25:28,995 --> 00:25:30,297
AND THEY'RE PACKED
WITH VITAMINS.

608
00:25:30,330 --> 00:25:32,032
I'M AFRAID YOUR ANSWER
ISN'T HERE.

609
00:25:32,065 --> 00:25:33,098
OH, I SEE.

610
00:25:33,132 --> 00:25:34,567
THE BIG BRUSH OFF.

611
00:25:34,600 --> 00:25:37,103
TELL ME, IS THIS THING
REALLY A STRAWBERRY?

612
00:25:37,137 --> 00:25:39,005
YES, AND THESE ARE TOMATOES.

613
00:25:39,038 --> 00:25:40,507
AND THOSE ARE TURKEY FRANKS.

614
00:25:40,540 --> 00:25:42,742
THIS WE HOPE IS THE FUTURE
OF THE AMERICAN FARMER.

615
00:25:42,775 --> 00:25:45,945
AND FOR THAT MATTER,
ALL FARMERS EVERYWHERE.

616
00:25:45,978 --> 00:25:47,880
- CAN YOU EAT THEM?
- NO, NOT YET.

617
00:25:47,913 --> 00:25:49,015
I DON'T EVEN LIKE TOMATOES.

618
00:25:49,048 --> 00:25:50,217
WE HOPE TO DEVELOPED
ONE DAY A HYBRID

619
00:25:50,250 --> 00:25:52,152
THAT CAN BE EATEN.

620
00:25:52,185 --> 00:25:54,453
HOW IS IT THERE HASN'T BEEN
ANY PUBLICITY ON THIS?

621
00:25:54,487 --> 00:25:57,190
OH, THERE HAVE BEEN A FEW
STORIES IN FARM JOURNALS,

622
00:25:57,223 --> 00:25:58,758
BUT TO MOST OF THE PUBLIC,

623
00:25:58,792 --> 00:26:01,027
THESE GIANTS
ARE JUST FREAKS OF NATURE.

624
00:26:01,060 --> 00:26:02,328
NO PRACTICAL VALUE.

625
00:26:02,362 --> 00:26:05,132
- GET THIS THING OFF ME.
- HOW DID THEY GET SO BIG?

626
00:26:05,165 --> 00:26:07,733
RADIATION
CAUSES PHOTOSYNTHESIS,

627
00:26:07,767 --> 00:26:09,035
THAT IS THE GROWING PROCESS,

628
00:26:09,068 --> 00:26:10,470
TO CONTINUE NIGHT AND DAY.

629
00:26:10,503 --> 00:26:13,005
RADIO ISOTOPES ACT AS
A SORT OF ARTIFICIAL SUN.

630
00:26:13,038 --> 00:26:15,842
THAT'S IT, REAL HER IN, BOSS.

631
00:26:15,875 --> 00:26:17,010
FASCINATING.

632
00:26:17,043 --> 00:26:18,912
TELL ME, WHAT'S HE DOING?

633
00:26:18,945 --> 00:26:20,413
WELL, THAT'S PLANT FOOD,
ESSENTIAL MINERALS.

634
00:26:20,447 --> 00:26:21,748
AND HE'S EATING IT.

635
00:26:21,782 --> 00:26:23,215
KEEPS THE PLANTS
FROM BURNING THEMSELVES UP.

636
00:26:23,248 --> 00:26:24,783
THEY HAVE TO BE FED
CONSTANTLY.

637
00:26:24,817 --> 00:26:27,153
ACTUALLY THE FRUIT
WOULD GROW MUCH LARGER

638
00:26:27,187 --> 00:26:28,988
IF WE DIDN'T LIMIT
THE STIMULATION.

639
00:26:29,022 --> 00:26:30,423
SPEAKING OF STIMULATION.

640
00:26:30,457 --> 00:26:32,058
MAYBE YOU'D LIKE TO DO
A STORY ON US.

641
00:26:32,092 --> 00:26:33,760
I'D BE GLAD TO TELL YOU
MORE ABOUT THE WORK.

642
00:26:33,793 --> 00:26:35,128
OOH, SCHMOOZE OVERDRIVE.

643
00:26:35,162 --> 00:26:36,963
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.
I'D BE VERY INTERESTED,

644
00:26:36,997 --> 00:26:39,465
BUT RIGHT NOW I'M WORKING
ON THIS LUDLOW STORY.

645
00:26:39,498 --> 00:26:43,235
IF YOU COULD SEE MY HANDS RIGHT
NOW, YOU'D BE HORRIFIED.

646
00:26:43,268 --> 00:26:45,238
- GOOD-BYE.
- BYE.

647
00:26:47,140 --> 00:26:49,375
DON'T START.

648
00:26:49,408 --> 00:26:50,943
♪ THAT'S MY MOTHER DEAR ♪

649
00:26:50,977 --> 00:26:55,082
♪ SHE HELPS ME THROUGH
EVERYTHING I DO ♪

650
00:26:55,115 --> 00:26:57,317
THREE JERKS AND A JILL.

651
00:26:57,350 --> 00:26:59,852
COLONEL.

652
00:26:59,885 --> 00:27:01,153
YOU HERE?

653
00:27:01,187 --> 00:27:02,655
THEY WOULDN'T LET ME INSIDE,
SO--

654
00:27:02,688 --> 00:27:05,325
COLONEL, SPRINGFIELD
IS ON THE LINE.

655
00:27:05,358 --> 00:27:06,827
COLONEL, YOU JUST GOT BACK
FROM LUDLOW.

656
00:27:06,860 --> 00:27:08,327
YOU SAID, AFTER YOU GOT BACK,
I COULD GO.

657
00:27:08,360 --> 00:27:10,197
- I SAID MAYBE.
- WELL, HOW ABOUT IT?

658
00:27:10,230 --> 00:27:11,597
NOTHING WILL BE OPEN
TO THE PRESS.

659
00:27:11,630 --> 00:27:12,632
OH, COLONEL, BE FAIR.

660
00:27:12,665 --> 00:27:14,167
I PLAYED BALL WITH YOU.

661
00:27:14,200 --> 00:27:16,502
GIVE ME THE JUMP ON THE OTHER
REPORTERS THAT'LL BE IN HERE.

662
00:27:16,535 --> 00:27:18,738
AT LEAST LET ME TAKE
SOME PICTURES IN LUDLOW.

663
00:27:18,772 --> 00:27:20,940
I PROMISE I WON'T PUT THEM
ON THE WIRE UNTIL TOMORROW.

664
00:27:20,973 --> 00:27:22,542
WELL, I GUESS
YOU RATE THAT.

665
00:27:22,575 --> 00:27:24,377
FOR EFFORT ANYWAY.

666
00:27:24,410 --> 00:27:25,812
BRATTON, TAKE MISS AIMS
TO LUDLOW.

667
00:27:25,845 --> 00:27:26,947
YES, SIR.

668
00:27:26,980 --> 00:27:28,515
AND I HOPE YOU HAVE
A STRONG STOMACH.

669
00:27:28,548 --> 00:27:31,250
GABE KAPLAN'S PERFORMING.

670
00:27:31,283 --> 00:27:33,352
HE'S NICE.

671
00:27:33,385 --> 00:27:35,822
WE'RE GOING TO TAKE
SOME PICTURES IN LUDLOW.

672
00:27:35,855 --> 00:27:37,457
IF WE'RE NOT BACK
IN 15 MINUTES,

673
00:27:37,490 --> 00:27:39,758
BETTER COME IN AFTER US.

674
00:27:39,792 --> 00:27:45,732
- YES, SIR. LET 'EM THROUGH.
- LOOK AT THAT GUY OVER THERE.
HE'S TAKEN A FEW IN THE HEAD.

675
00:27:45,765 --> 00:27:48,535
THAT WOULDN'T STOP A KID
ON A BIG WHEEL.

676
00:27:48,568 --> 00:27:52,305
TOUGHEST JOB YOU'LL EVER LOVE.

677
00:27:52,338 --> 00:27:54,673
ALL RIGHT, CAPTAIN.
WAY TO GO. WHOO!

678
00:27:57,210 --> 00:28:00,680
HUH? SUDDENLY IT'S TURNED
INTO TOPPER.

679
00:28:03,115 --> 00:28:06,718
SOMEBODY TURN DOWN
THE ALBERT GLASSER MUSIC!
I CAN'T CONCENTRATE!

680
00:28:06,752 --> 00:28:09,422
I WISH THE LARSONS WOULD TAKE
BETTER CARE OF THEIR YARD.

681
00:28:09,455 --> 00:28:11,323
- OH, IT'S A DISGRACE.
- OH, LOOK AT THAT.

682
00:28:11,357 --> 00:28:13,760
MY GOODNESS.

683
00:28:13,793 --> 00:28:15,195
WANNA STOP AND LOOT?

684
00:28:16,830 --> 00:28:18,330
HEY, IT'S A STAR CITY.

685
00:28:20,500 --> 00:28:24,103
LOOK. THERE'S
A PERFECTLY GOOD 2 X 4.

686
00:28:24,137 --> 00:28:25,838
THIS WAS NO BOATING ACCIDENT.

687
00:28:29,175 --> 00:28:30,777
♪♪ [HUMMING]

688
00:28:32,078 --> 00:28:33,245
I'VE HAD ENOUGH.

689
00:28:33,278 --> 00:28:35,948
I CAN'T STAND REALITY.

690
00:28:35,982 --> 00:28:39,218
- WHOA-HO, COLONEL.
- SOME USE CALENDARS
TO TELL AGE.

691
00:28:39,252 --> 00:28:41,187
I COULD USE RUINS
TO COUNT MINE.

692
00:28:41,220 --> 00:28:42,988
OH, AM I HERE, TOO?

693
00:28:43,022 --> 00:28:45,692
I WAS 25 WHEN I WENT THROUGH
SEOUL AFTER THE SHELLS.

694
00:28:45,725 --> 00:28:46,993
I'M WEARING PANTIES RIGHT NOW.

695
00:28:47,027 --> 00:28:49,395
I WAS 20 WHEN I TOOK MY CAMERA
INTO COLOGNE AND BERLIN

696
00:28:49,428 --> 00:28:50,497
AFTER WORLD WAR II.

697
00:28:50,530 --> 00:28:52,198
24 WHEN I SAW DYLAN
AT THE BITTER END.

698
00:28:52,232 --> 00:28:55,535
MUST BE USED TO IT BY NOW.

699
00:28:55,568 --> 00:28:58,003
CAPTAIN, THERE'S SOME THINGS
YOU NEVER GET USED TO.

700
00:28:58,037 --> 00:28:59,338
LIKE UNDERARM ODOR.

701
00:29:03,008 --> 00:29:05,678
THANKS.
HOW ABOUT MY KISS?

702
00:29:05,712 --> 00:29:08,380
HOW ABOUT A DRINK
TO WIPE AWAY SOME MEMORIES?

703
00:29:08,413 --> 00:29:09,815
GOOD WAY TO GET RID
OF THE JITTERS.

704
00:29:09,848 --> 00:29:11,250
I KNOW A LITTLE PLACE--

705
00:29:11,283 --> 00:29:13,787
HOW DO A HUNDRED
AND FIFTY PEOPLE VANISH
INTO THIN AIR?

706
00:29:13,820 --> 00:29:15,020
YEAH, TERRIBLE.
MARTINIS?

707
00:29:15,053 --> 00:29:16,155
AROUND THIS PART OF THE COUNTRY,

708
00:29:16,188 --> 00:29:18,257
THINGS SEEM TO HAVE
A WAY OF VANISHING.

709
00:29:18,290 --> 00:29:20,560
ONLY A COUPLE OF MONTHS AGO
IT WAS A WAREHOUSE.

710
00:29:20,593 --> 00:29:21,862
KIND OF FELL APART OVER NIGHT,

711
00:29:21,895 --> 00:29:23,095
JUST LIKE LUDLOW.

712
00:29:23,128 --> 00:29:24,230
GOOD-BYE, CAPTAIN.

713
00:29:24,263 --> 00:29:25,498
WHA-- HELLO?

714
00:29:25,532 --> 00:29:27,700
OKAY, OKAY,
YOU CAN HAVE YOUR RAISE.

715
00:29:30,237 --> 00:29:32,205
HEY, HE SAW
AND HEARD SOMETHING.

716
00:29:36,108 --> 00:29:38,778
WOMEN ON THE VERGE
OF AN ATOMIC BREAKDOWN.

717
00:29:38,812 --> 00:29:40,980
SHE WANTS ME SO BAD.

718
00:29:43,583 --> 00:29:44,950
LET'S GET ON
WITH THE HARASSMENT

719
00:29:44,983 --> 00:29:46,352
SO WE CAN GET SOME WORK DONE.

720
00:29:46,385 --> 00:29:49,455
HI. DID YOU DECIDE TO COME
BACK AND DO A STORY ON US?

721
00:29:49,488 --> 00:29:50,823
NO, AS A MATTER OF FACT,

722
00:29:50,857 --> 00:29:52,092
I CAME BACK FOR SOME HELP.

723
00:29:52,125 --> 00:29:54,027
I'D LIKE YOU TO DO ME A FAVOR.

724
00:29:54,060 --> 00:29:55,295
- OH, YES.
- ANYTHING I CAN.

725
00:29:55,328 --> 00:29:56,897
DOES IT INVOLVE TAKING
MY PANTS OFF?

726
00:29:56,930 --> 00:30:00,165
REMEMBER THE WAREHOUSE
THAT WAS DESTROYED
ABOUT THREE MONTHS AGO?

727
00:30:00,198 --> 00:30:01,667
I WANT YOU TO TAKE ME
TO SEE IT.

728
00:30:01,700 --> 00:30:03,002
THEN TO DINNER AND A MOVIE.

729
00:30:03,035 --> 00:30:05,137
OH, I'D LIKE TO,

730
00:30:05,170 --> 00:30:06,907
BUT I'VE GOT TOO MUCH WORK
ON MY HANDS RIGHT NOW.

731
00:30:06,940 --> 00:30:08,642
HOW ABOUT TOMORROW?

732
00:30:08,675 --> 00:30:12,245
THREE MONTHS AGO A WAREHOUSE
WAS DESTROYED,

733
00:30:12,278 --> 00:30:14,847
AND ONE PERSON IN IT VANISHED.

734
00:30:14,880 --> 00:30:17,150
THIS MORNING LUDLOW
WAS DESTROYED.

735
00:30:17,183 --> 00:30:18,618
ALL THE PEOPLE IN IT VANISHED.

736
00:30:18,652 --> 00:30:19,718
COINCIDENCE? READ THE BOOK.

737
00:30:19,752 --> 00:30:20,887
DON'T YOU SEE
A POSSIBLE TIE UP?

738
00:30:20,920 --> 00:30:23,422
LOOK, LAY OFF. LAY OFF!

739
00:30:23,455 --> 00:30:24,790
IT'S POSSIBLE, I SUPPOSE.

740
00:30:24,823 --> 00:30:26,425
WHAT DO YOU WANT ME TO DO?

741
00:30:26,458 --> 00:30:29,862
JUST RIDE OUT THERE WITH ME
AND TAKE A LOOK AT IT.

742
00:30:29,895 --> 00:30:31,563
I DON'T UNDERSTAND
WHAT GOOD THAT'LL DO.

743
00:30:31,597 --> 00:30:33,532
THE AUTHORITIES
INVESTIGATED IT THOROUGHLY.

744
00:30:33,565 --> 00:30:35,802
LOOK, I'M COMING ON TO YOU.
DON'T YOU GET IT?

745
00:30:35,835 --> 00:30:37,903
THE SHERIFF THINKS IN TERMS
OF CRIME AND PUBLICITY.

746
00:30:37,937 --> 00:30:39,505
YOU'RE A SCIENTIST.

747
00:30:39,538 --> 00:30:41,908
YOU THINK IN TERMS
OF CAUSE AND EFFECT.

748
00:30:41,942 --> 00:30:44,477
MAYBE YOU'LL SEE SOMETHING
THAT THE SHERIFF MISSED.

749
00:30:44,510 --> 00:30:47,147
THAT SHOULDN'T BE
TOO DIFFICULT.

750
00:30:47,180 --> 00:30:49,048
STILL, I-- I DON'T KNOW.

751
00:30:49,082 --> 00:30:50,148
HM?

752
00:30:51,250 --> 00:30:52,585
FRANK, THAT'S FILTHY.

753
00:30:52,618 --> 00:30:55,187
I SHOULD WASH
YOUR HANDS OUT WITH SOAP.

754
00:30:55,220 --> 00:30:56,722
WHAT'S HE SAYING?

755
00:30:56,755 --> 00:30:59,625
HE SAYS THAT YOUR LIPS
ARE EASY TO READ,

756
00:30:59,658 --> 00:31:02,462
THAT YOUR THEORY MAKES YOU
A VERY BRIGHT GIRL IN HIS BOOK,

757
00:31:02,495 --> 00:31:03,697
AND HE'D LIKE TO GO ALONG
WITH US.

758
00:31:03,730 --> 00:31:05,265
AND HE'S BEING HELD HERE
AGAINST HIS WILL.

759
00:31:05,298 --> 00:31:07,467
EH-- OOPS.

760
00:31:07,500 --> 00:31:10,068
- PETER, NO!
- OH, NO! GOD!

761
00:31:10,102 --> 00:31:11,703
WHEN YOU BARGE
INTO PEOPLE'S LIVES

762
00:31:11,737 --> 00:31:13,973
AND DRAG THEM OFF TO PLACES
THEY DON'T REALLY WANT TO GO,

763
00:31:14,007 --> 00:31:16,775
AREN'T YOU SORT OF IN DANGER
OF BECOMING UNPOPULAR?

764
00:31:16,808 --> 00:31:18,812
SLUG BUG.
OW.

765
00:31:18,845 --> 00:31:19,978
OH, I THOUGH YOU...

766
00:31:20,012 --> 00:31:21,880
HOW'D YOU PICK
SUCH AN OCCUPATION?

767
00:31:21,913 --> 00:31:25,117
WAIT, THIS ISN'T A STICK SHIFT.

768
00:31:25,150 --> 00:31:27,653
I GUESS I WAS JUST BORN
INQUISITIVE.

769
00:31:27,687 --> 00:31:28,822
EVER SINCE I CAN REMEMBER,

770
00:31:28,855 --> 00:31:30,757
I WANTED TO KNOW
THE WHY AND WHEREFORE

771
00:31:30,790 --> 00:31:33,627
OF JUST ABOUT
EVERYTHING I SAW.

772
00:31:33,660 --> 00:31:36,295
I INHERITED MY KNACK
FOR THE CAMERA FROM DAD.

773
00:31:36,328 --> 00:31:37,863
YOUR DAD, AS A MATTER OF FACT.

774
00:31:37,897 --> 00:31:39,665
MY CURIOSITY SUPPLIED
THE NOSE FOR NEWS,

775
00:31:39,698 --> 00:31:42,335
AND THE CAMERA SUPPLIED
THE MEMORY.

776
00:31:42,368 --> 00:31:44,603
SO THERE YOU HAVE IT.

777
00:31:44,637 --> 00:31:45,772
WHAT ABOUT YOU?

778
00:31:45,805 --> 00:31:48,473
HAVE YOU ALWAYS BEEN
INTERESTED IN SCIENCE?

779
00:31:48,507 --> 00:31:50,743
WELL, AFTER
MY GERMAN DANCEHALL DAYS...

780
00:31:50,777 --> 00:31:52,378
I GUESS I ALWAYS HAVE BEEN
ONE WAY OR ANOTHER.

781
00:31:52,412 --> 00:31:53,947
I USED TO FOOL AROUND
WITH RADIOS

782
00:31:53,980 --> 00:31:56,315
AND ANYTHING ELECTRICAL
WHEN I WAS A KID.

783
00:31:56,348 --> 00:31:58,183
I WAS A RADAR OFFICER
DURING THE WAR,

784
00:31:58,217 --> 00:32:00,420
AND THEN I WENT INTO THIS
WHEN I GOT OUT.

785
00:32:00,453 --> 00:32:02,988
LOOK. LET'S JUST PLAY
THE RADIO FOR A WHILE. HM?

786
00:32:03,022 --> 00:32:04,790
OH, YES, I REMEMBER NOW,

787
00:32:04,823 --> 00:32:06,692
THAT EVERY TIME I READ
ONE OF YOUR ARTICLES,

788
00:32:06,725 --> 00:32:10,897
IT WAS DATELINED FROM SOME AREA
OF FLOOD OR FAMINE OR WAR.

789
00:32:10,930 --> 00:32:14,167
MADE ME REALIZE
WHAT A SHELTERED LIFE
WE SCIENTISTS REALLY LEAD.

790
00:32:14,200 --> 00:32:17,503
- WHAT DO YOU THINK OF THAT?
HUH?
- SHELTERED?

791
00:32:17,537 --> 00:32:18,905
LOOK WHAT HAPPENED TO FRANK.

792
00:32:18,938 --> 00:32:21,573
YEAH, WATCH THIS.
HEY, FRANK!

793
00:32:21,607 --> 00:32:23,542
[LAUGHS]

794
00:32:35,955 --> 00:32:40,258
GEEZ, FRANK, YOU SHOULD'VE
THOUGHT ABOUT THAT
BEFORE WE LEFT.

795
00:32:40,292 --> 00:32:41,393
DOESN'T LOOK THAT GREAT,

796
00:32:41,427 --> 00:32:43,062
BUT THEY GOT GREAT
UNION RINGS HERE.

797
00:32:45,363 --> 00:32:46,698
HUH? WHAT?

798
00:32:46,732 --> 00:32:48,267
- WHAT THE?
- WHAT THE?

799
00:32:48,300 --> 00:32:50,068
HEY, THIS IS EVEN WORSE
THAN THAT OTHER STUFF

800
00:32:50,102 --> 00:32:51,403
THAT WE DIDN'T KNOW
WHAT IT WAS.

801
00:32:55,173 --> 00:32:57,477
WELL, IT'S A FIXER UPPER.
THAT'S FOR SURE.

802
00:33:01,880 --> 00:33:03,582
LOOKS TO ME AS THOUGH
SOME FORCE

803
00:33:03,615 --> 00:33:05,818
HAD TO PUSH THESE WALLS OUT
FROM THE INSIDE.

804
00:33:05,852 --> 00:33:08,420
THINK IT WAS AN EXPLOSION?

805
00:33:08,453 --> 00:33:09,922
IT COULDN'T HAVE BEEN.

806
00:33:09,955 --> 00:33:12,125
ANY EXPLOSION BIG ENOUGH
TO DESTROY THIS WAREHOUSE

807
00:33:12,158 --> 00:33:13,592
COULD CERTAINLY
HAVE BEEN HEARD IN LUDLOW.

808
00:33:13,625 --> 00:33:15,027
AT LEAST WE SAVED THIS HAT.

809
00:33:15,060 --> 00:33:16,962
WHAT WAS IT THAT THEY KEPT
STORED HERE?

810
00:33:16,995 --> 00:33:19,498
WHEAT.
ALMOST A MILLION BUSHELS.

811
00:33:19,532 --> 00:33:21,133
THAT'S A LOT OF WHEAT.

812
00:33:21,167 --> 00:33:24,037
IT WAS SURPLUS
TO KEEP THE MARKET
FROM BEING OVERSUPPLIED.

813
00:33:24,070 --> 00:33:26,005
- I HATE WHEAT.
- DOESN'T IT STRIKE YOU
AS A LITTLE STRANGE

814
00:33:26,038 --> 00:33:27,107
THAT OUT OF ALL THAT WHEAT

815
00:33:27,140 --> 00:33:28,707
THERE'S NOT
A GRAIN LEFT ANYWHERE?

816
00:33:28,740 --> 00:33:30,777
NO, THAT'S NATURE'S WAY,
AUDREY.

817
00:33:30,810 --> 00:33:33,012
BIRDS PROBABLY CLEANED UP
THE LEAVINGS.

818
00:33:33,045 --> 00:33:36,315
HE'S NOT DEAF.
THEY'RE TALKING
ABOUT WHEAT OVER HERE.

819
00:33:36,348 --> 00:33:39,018
THAT'S FRANK'S WAY OF YELLING.

820
00:33:42,122 --> 00:33:44,223
WHA-WHAT?

821
00:33:44,257 --> 00:33:47,193
WOW, THAT'S
A WHOLE LOT OF SKIRT.

822
00:33:47,227 --> 00:33:48,627
I SEE WHAT YOU MEAN, FRANK.

823
00:33:48,660 --> 00:33:49,995
WHAT IS IT?

824
00:33:50,028 --> 00:33:51,197
WHAT-WHAT DID HE SAY?

825
00:33:51,230 --> 00:33:55,535
YOU SEE HOW BARREN
THIS GROUND IS?

826
00:33:55,568 --> 00:33:58,337
I DON'T KNOW.
I'VE SEEN HORSES LEAVE IT
LIKE THIS.

827
00:33:58,370 --> 00:34:00,005
THIS IS DEEPER THAN HORSES GO

828
00:34:00,038 --> 00:34:01,007
AND MUCH MORE THOROUGH.

829
00:34:01,040 --> 00:34:02,007
AND MUCH MORE FUN.

830
00:34:02,040 --> 00:34:03,542
PRACTICALLY DOWN TO THE ROOTS.

831
00:34:03,575 --> 00:34:05,812
NOW, HORSES PICK AND CHOOSE.
THEY LEAVE PATCHES.

832
00:34:05,845 --> 00:34:07,280
I WAS IN FURY,
SO I KNOW THAT.

833
00:34:07,313 --> 00:34:08,347
THIS IS BARREN.

834
00:34:08,380 --> 00:34:09,815
PLEASE DON'T SAY THAT WORD.

835
00:34:09,848 --> 00:34:11,183
I'M VERY SENSITIVE RIGHT NOW.

836
00:34:15,053 --> 00:34:18,590
LEAVE IT TO OLD FRANK.
HE'LL MAKE A BOTANIST
OUT OF ME YET.

837
00:34:18,623 --> 00:34:19,925
YOU'RE HEAD
OF A GOVERNMENT LAB,

838
00:34:19,958 --> 00:34:21,193
AND YOU NEED LESSONS
IN BOTANY?

839
00:34:21,227 --> 00:34:22,328
WELL, JUST LAY OFF.

840
00:34:22,362 --> 00:34:24,063
I TRY TO TEACH HIM
WHAT I CAN

841
00:34:24,097 --> 00:34:25,263
ABOUT MY FIELD OF STUDY.

842
00:34:25,297 --> 00:34:27,400
HE TRIES TO TEACH ME
WHAT HE CAN ABOUT HIS.

843
00:34:27,433 --> 00:34:28,802
AREN'T YOU A BOTANIST?

844
00:34:28,835 --> 00:34:30,737
NO. NO, I'M AN ENTOMOLOGIST--

845
00:34:30,770 --> 00:34:32,272
THE STUDY OF INSECTS.

846
00:34:32,305 --> 00:34:33,405
OH, FASCINATING.

847
00:34:33,438 --> 00:34:34,807
HOW COME YOU'RE WORKING
WITH PLANTS?

848
00:34:34,840 --> 00:34:36,408
GOD, YOU'RE RIGHT.

849
00:34:36,442 --> 00:34:38,912
WELL, THE EXISTENCE
AND DEVELOPMENT OF PLANTS
AND INSECTS

850
00:34:38,945 --> 00:34:40,278
ARE VERY CLOSELY RELATED.

851
00:34:40,312 --> 00:34:42,248
THEY'RE HIGHLY DEPENDENT
ON ONE ANOTHER.

852
00:34:42,282 --> 00:34:44,817
AS A PLAIN MATTER OF FACT,
ONE COULDN'T LIVE
WITHOUT THE OTHER.

853
00:34:44,850 --> 00:34:45,885
- MM-HM.
- BOGUS.

854
00:34:45,918 --> 00:34:47,320
THAT'S WHY I CAN'T UNDERSTAND.

855
00:34:47,353 --> 00:34:50,923
GROUND LIKE THIS IS USUALLY
TEEMING WITH INSECTS.

856
00:34:50,957 --> 00:34:52,758
THIS AREA'S COMPLETELY
DEVOID OF IT.

857
00:34:52,792 --> 00:34:54,460
HM, YOU LIKE FIDDLE FADDLE?

858
00:34:54,493 --> 00:34:55,995
I THINK I'D LIKE TO GET
SOME SHOTS OF THIS.

859
00:34:56,028 --> 00:34:57,730
I'M GOING BACK TO THE CAR
FOR MY CAMERA.

860
00:34:57,763 --> 00:35:00,332
I'D REALLY LIKE TO SEE YOU RUB
YOUR FOREARMS TOGETHER.

861
00:35:04,303 --> 00:35:07,207
HEY, AN INDIAN HEAD PENNY.

862
00:35:07,240 --> 00:35:08,942
- HERE, LET ME HELP YOU.
- [CHIRPING]

863
00:35:08,975 --> 00:35:11,343
[GRUNTS]

864
00:35:11,377 --> 00:35:12,945
WHAT WAS THAT?

865
00:35:12,978 --> 00:35:14,047
- [CHIRPING GETS LOUDER]
- I DON'T KNOW.

866
00:35:16,182 --> 00:35:19,352
IT MIGHT BE COMING
FROM BEHIND THAT RATHER LARGE
GRASSHOPPER.

867
00:35:19,385 --> 00:35:21,053
I THINK.

868
00:35:22,455 --> 00:35:24,857
LUCKILY THE GRASSHOPPER'S
CLOSED CAPTIONED.

869
00:35:24,890 --> 00:35:27,593
FRANK, WOULD YOU QUIT CLOWNING
WITH THAT GIANT GRASSHOPPER?

870
00:35:27,627 --> 00:35:29,862
OH, NO, STOP!

871
00:35:29,895 --> 00:35:32,332
HE'S SIGNING "AAH!"

872
00:35:32,365 --> 00:35:33,398
OH, NO.

873
00:35:33,432 --> 00:35:34,433
YOU CAN'T SAVE HIM.

874
00:35:34,467 --> 00:35:35,702
GET IN THE CAR.

875
00:35:35,735 --> 00:35:37,703
QUICKLY, GET A REALLY BIG
APPLESAUCE JAR

876
00:35:37,737 --> 00:35:40,438
WITH HOLES POKED IN THE LID.

877
00:35:40,472 --> 00:35:41,840
HEY, DIANE ARBUS,

878
00:35:41,873 --> 00:35:43,608
WHY DON'T YOU TAKE A PICTURE?

879
00:35:43,642 --> 00:35:45,010
YOU'VE GOT A CAMERA.

880
00:35:45,043 --> 00:35:46,812
WE'LL SEND HELP.
B-B-BYE.

881
00:35:49,315 --> 00:35:51,817
SO FEEL LIKE CHINESE?

882
00:35:51,850 --> 00:35:54,753
THE GEIGER COUNTERS
SHOW NO RADIOACTIVITY
TO SPEAK OF, SIR.

883
00:35:54,787 --> 00:35:56,122
ONLY BACKGROUND.

884
00:35:56,155 --> 00:35:58,090
THERE'S GOT TO BE
AN EXPLANATION SOMEWHERE.

885
00:35:58,123 --> 00:35:59,725
I'VE GOT YOUR EXPLANATION
FOR YOU, TOM.

886
00:35:59,758 --> 00:36:01,327
- WE'VE GOT BUGS.
- NOW, LISTEN.

887
00:36:01,360 --> 00:36:03,562
YOU'VE KNOWN ME EVER
SINCE I CAME TO PAXTON.

888
00:36:03,595 --> 00:36:04,997
YOU KNOW I'M NOT GIVEN
TO HYSTERIA,

889
00:36:05,030 --> 00:36:07,300
AND YOU'VE GOT TO LISTEN
TO ME WITH AN OPEN MIND.

890
00:36:07,333 --> 00:36:09,302
[WHIMPERING GIBBERISH]

891
00:36:09,335 --> 00:36:10,435
WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

892
00:36:10,468 --> 00:36:11,937
I'M TALKING
ABOUT GIANT LOCUSTS.

893
00:36:11,970 --> 00:36:14,407
GIANT LOCUSTS ARE RESPONSIBLE
FOR ALL OF THIS.

894
00:36:14,440 --> 00:36:15,742
I LOVE IT.

895
00:36:15,775 --> 00:36:17,910
NO EVIDENCE OF ANY EXPLOSION,
COLONEL.

896
00:36:17,943 --> 00:36:20,512
THE BUILDINGS LOOK
MORE LIKE THEY WERE HIT
WITH A BATTERING RAM.

897
00:36:20,545 --> 00:36:22,715
WE FOUND THESE GUNS
AT THE SCENE,

898
00:36:22,748 --> 00:36:24,583
THE KIND PEOPLE KEEP
IN THEIR HOME.

899
00:36:24,617 --> 00:36:25,718
THEY'VE BEEN FIRED.

900
00:36:25,752 --> 00:36:27,218
- CAN I GO HOME NOW?
- OKAY. LIEUTENANT.

901
00:36:27,252 --> 00:36:28,453
NOW, LISTEN, TOM.

902
00:36:28,487 --> 00:36:30,188
THESE ARE EIGHT FEET TALL,
SOME EVEN BIGGER.

903
00:36:30,222 --> 00:36:31,690
THEY'RE VICIOUS,
MERCILESS KILLERS.

904
00:36:31,723 --> 00:36:32,825
NOW, ED.

905
00:36:32,858 --> 00:36:34,693
STOPS THEM COLD
WITH THAT "NOW, ED" EVERY TIME.

906
00:36:34,727 --> 00:36:37,297
LIEUTENANT, TELEPHONE
SPRINGFIELD AGAIN.

907
00:36:37,330 --> 00:36:38,897
TELL THEM I'M STILL WAITING
FOR THOSE SPECIALISTS.

908
00:36:38,930 --> 00:36:41,033
- YES, SIR.
- FRANK JOHNSON IS DEAD.

909
00:36:41,067 --> 00:36:42,502
HE WAS KILLED
NOT HALF AN HOUR AGO.

910
00:36:42,535 --> 00:36:43,768
IT WAS HORRIBLE.

911
00:36:43,802 --> 00:36:45,270
OBVIOUSLY YOU'RE BOTH
UNDER STRAIN--

912
00:36:45,303 --> 00:36:46,438
WHY WON'T YOU LISTEN?

913
00:36:46,472 --> 00:36:48,040
YOU'VE GOT TO GET
SOME SOLDIERS OUT THERE

914
00:36:48,073 --> 00:36:49,542
BEFORE MORE PEOPLE
ARE KILLED.

915
00:36:49,575 --> 00:36:51,910
MISS AIMES, THE GOVERNOR ASKED
ME TO EXERCISE DIGRESSION

916
00:36:51,943 --> 00:36:53,245
IN DEALING WITH YOU.

917
00:36:53,278 --> 00:36:54,747
PLEASE DON'T MAKE IT ANY HARDER
FOR ME THAN IT IS.

918
00:36:54,780 --> 00:36:56,582
YOU HAVE TO BELIEVE US.

919
00:36:56,615 --> 00:36:59,452
LISTEN, YOU'VE SEEN THE GIANT
PLANTS OUT AT THE LAB.

920
00:36:59,485 --> 00:37:01,820
ARE YOU TRYING TO TELL ME
YOU BRED THESE THINGS?

921
00:37:01,853 --> 00:37:03,288
YEP, THEN I DEEP FRY THEM.

922
00:37:03,322 --> 00:37:04,757
IN A SENSE I DID, YES.

923
00:37:04,790 --> 00:37:06,692
HEY, IT'S IKE.
SAY HI TO IKE, EVERYONE.

924
00:37:06,725 --> 00:37:07,927
- THE LOCUSTS MUST'VE GOTTEN
INTO THE LAB.

925
00:37:07,960 --> 00:37:08,995
- HI, IKE.
- I LIKE IKE.

926
00:37:09,028 --> 00:37:10,128
AND THEY ATE SOME
OF THE PLANTS

927
00:37:10,162 --> 00:37:11,330
OR SOME OF THE RADIOACTIVE
PLANT FOOD.

928
00:37:11,363 --> 00:37:12,965
THEIR CELL DIVISION
ACCELERATED IMMEDIATELY.

929
00:37:12,998 --> 00:37:14,733
THAT IS THEY STARTED
TO GROW ABNORMALLY FAST.

930
00:37:14,767 --> 00:37:16,235
SO IT'S YOUR FAULT.

931
00:37:16,268 --> 00:37:18,470
THEY HAVE
A CONSTANT FOOD SUPPLY
TO SUSTAIN THIS GROWTH.

932
00:37:18,503 --> 00:37:19,972
SO A COUPLE OF MONTHS AGO

933
00:37:20,005 --> 00:37:22,342
THEY WANDERED INTO THE GRAIN
ELEVATOR OUTSIDE OF TOWN.

934
00:37:22,375 --> 00:37:23,708
WHEN THEY GREW
TO THIS GIANT SIZE,

935
00:37:23,742 --> 00:37:24,843
THEY PUSHED THEIR WAY OUT.

936
00:37:24,877 --> 00:37:26,845
OH, THEY JUST PUSHED
THE BUILDING DOWN.

937
00:37:26,878 --> 00:37:28,613
- YES.
- OKAY, OKAY, FORGET LOCUSTS.

938
00:37:28,647 --> 00:37:29,948
GIANT PANDA BEARS
AND THEY FLY.

939
00:37:29,982 --> 00:37:31,417
ONE OF THEM HAS THE STRENGTH
OF 10 MEN.

940
00:37:31,450 --> 00:37:33,152
THERE ARE PROBABLY
2 OR 300 OF THEM.

941
00:37:33,185 --> 00:37:35,420
SO LAST NIGHT, NOT SATISFIED
WITH EATING THE GRAIN,

942
00:37:35,453 --> 00:37:36,522
THEY CAME TO LUDLOW.

943
00:37:36,555 --> 00:37:37,790
- YES.
- [CHUCKLES]

944
00:37:37,823 --> 00:37:39,758
EVEN IF I WENT FOR YOUR STORY
ABOUT THE SIZE,

945
00:37:39,792 --> 00:37:41,427
IT'D BE HARD TO BELIEVE
THEY'D ATTACK PEOPLE.

946
00:37:41,460 --> 00:37:43,095
- SERGEANT.
- HAVE THESE PEOPLE KILLED.

947
00:37:43,128 --> 00:37:44,530
THAT REPORT COME IN
FROM THE CHEMISTS?

948
00:37:44,563 --> 00:37:45,563
NO, NOT YET, SIR.

949
00:37:45,597 --> 00:37:46,665
WHY WON'T YOU LISTEN?

950
00:37:46,698 --> 00:37:48,000
I AM LISTENING.

951
00:37:48,033 --> 00:37:51,003
WE SAW FRANK JOHNSON KILLED
BY A GIANT LOCUST.

952
00:37:51,037 --> 00:37:52,372
SURE, AND THERE ARE
RELIABLE PEOPLE

953
00:37:52,405 --> 00:37:53,572
WHO'VE ALSO SEEN
FLYING SAUCERS

954
00:37:53,605 --> 00:37:54,940
AND WEIRD LITTLE MEN
FROM MARS.

955
00:37:54,973 --> 00:37:56,775
TAKE ANOTHER LOOK
AT THAT TOWN OUT THERE.

956
00:37:56,808 --> 00:37:58,577
OR HAVE YOU FOUND THE ANSWER?

957
00:37:58,610 --> 00:38:00,312
GOD, I WANT PORK RIGHT NOW.

958
00:38:00,345 --> 00:38:01,647
LIEUTENANT.

959
00:38:01,680 --> 00:38:03,148
YES, SIR.

960
00:38:03,182 --> 00:38:04,950
I'M TAKING A DETAIL OUT
FOR A LOOK AROUND.

961
00:38:04,983 --> 00:38:07,152
YOU'RE TO KEEP RADIO CONTACT.
I WANT 10 MEN.

962
00:38:07,185 --> 00:38:08,987
- GET THEM ON THE TRUCK.
- YES, SIR.

963
00:38:09,020 --> 00:38:11,090
- ALL RIGHT, ED?
- STRAP THIS ON.

964
00:38:11,123 --> 00:38:14,260
YOU CAN SHOW ME THE EXACT SPOT
WHERE YOU SAW

965
00:38:14,293 --> 00:38:16,028
WELL, WHATEVER IT WAS YOU SAW.

966
00:38:16,062 --> 00:38:17,530
NO.

967
00:38:17,563 --> 00:38:20,465
WELL, AFTER ALL,
IT'S HIS GRASSHOPPER.

968
00:38:20,498 --> 00:38:23,435
THESE RIBBINGS ARE SO MUCH LESS
GENTLE THAN PLEATS.

969
00:38:23,468 --> 00:38:26,305
IT'S A GOOD THING THEY'RE NOT
HUGE EYEBROW MITES.

970
00:38:31,943 --> 00:38:33,578
THE JOADS ARE ARMED
TO THE TEETH.

971
00:38:36,315 --> 00:38:38,983
"CALIFORNEE."

972
00:38:39,017 --> 00:38:41,353
♪ WE'RE NOT AFRAID
OF BIG OLD BUGS ♪

973
00:38:41,387 --> 00:38:46,425
♪ ARMY GUYS LIKE GENTLE HUGS ♪

974
00:38:46,458 --> 00:38:48,393
THAT TOO WINDY BACK THERE
FOR YOU GUYS?

975
00:38:51,830 --> 00:38:54,633
IS THE TRUCK
JUST GOING TO DUMP THEM?

976
00:38:54,667 --> 00:38:56,702
IS THIS A SNIPE HUNT?

977
00:38:59,037 --> 00:39:02,542
[IMITATING BEEPING]

978
00:39:05,677 --> 00:39:07,212
- ALL RIGHT.
- ALL RIGHT!

979
00:39:07,245 --> 00:39:08,580
ALL RIGHT, ALL RIGHT.
[GRUNTING]

980
00:39:10,615 --> 00:39:12,685
BIG PILES OF POTATOES.

981
00:39:12,718 --> 00:39:15,620
DEFENDING COUNTRIES...

982
00:39:15,653 --> 00:39:17,957
MEN, WE'RE GONNA GET US
SOME CRAZY GRASSHOPPERS.

983
00:39:17,990 --> 00:39:20,658
WHY DIDN'T THEY GIVE US NETS
INSTEAD OF RIFLES?

984
00:39:20,692 --> 00:39:21,860
MM-HM.

985
00:39:21,893 --> 00:39:23,262
OBSERVATIONAL HUMOR.

986
00:39:23,295 --> 00:39:24,997
ALL RIGHT, MEN.
PAIR OUT.

987
00:39:25,030 --> 00:39:27,567
THAT'S ONE OF MY FAVORITE
MOUNTAINS IN ILLINOIS
BACK THERE.

988
00:39:30,368 --> 00:39:33,305
HEY, SOMEBODY STRUNG OUT
NICE ROOFING MATERIAL HERE.

989
00:39:33,338 --> 00:39:34,473
HERE'S THE SPOT, TOM.

990
00:39:34,507 --> 00:39:36,075
HE WET 'EM HERE.

991
00:39:36,108 --> 00:39:38,310
WHERE'S THE BODY?

992
00:39:38,343 --> 00:39:39,912
THERE ISN'T ANY BODY.

993
00:39:39,945 --> 00:39:42,047
I DON'T THINK I'VE IMPLIED
THERE WOULD BE A BODY.

994
00:39:42,080 --> 00:39:43,515
THERE ISN'T ANY BODY.

995
00:39:43,548 --> 00:39:45,918
ALL RIGHT, MEN,
INTO THE WOODS.

996
00:39:56,062 --> 00:39:57,997
I DON'T KNOW, CROW,
IT'S PROBABLY JUST ME,

997
00:39:58,030 --> 00:39:59,898
BUT THE WHOLE IDEA
OF A SCREENPLAY

998
00:39:59,932 --> 00:40:02,468
BASED AROUND THE LIFE
OF PETER GRAVES

999
00:40:02,502 --> 00:40:04,537
JUST SPELLS BOX-OFFICE POISON.

1000
00:40:04,570 --> 00:40:06,872
AND THEN TO GO AND NARROW
THE FOCUS SO MUCH.

1001
00:40:06,905 --> 00:40:09,275
HERE, LET ME SIZZLE IT
FOR YOU, MIKE.

1002
00:40:09,308 --> 00:40:12,443
PETER GRAVES WENT TO THE
UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA, RIGHT?

1003
00:40:12,477 --> 00:40:14,680
- I GUESS.
- "I GUESS" NOTHING.

1004
00:40:14,713 --> 00:40:16,615
THE MAN WENT TO THE U OF M,

1005
00:40:16,648 --> 00:40:19,050
AND THAT'S EXACTLY
WHAT MY SCREENPLAY EXPLOITS.

1006
00:40:19,083 --> 00:40:20,887
WELL, CAN WE JUST GET ON
WITH THIS, PLEASE?

1007
00:40:20,920 --> 00:40:22,153
YES.
[CLEARS THROAT]

1008
00:40:22,187 --> 00:40:23,388
HERE WE GO.

1009
00:40:23,422 --> 00:40:26,292
JUST PLAIN PETER.
THE U OF M YEARS.

1010
00:40:26,325 --> 00:40:28,827
OR PETER GRAVES GOES
TO COLLEGE

1011
00:40:28,860 --> 00:40:31,363
AT THE UNIVERSITY
OF MINNESOTA.

1012
00:40:31,397 --> 00:40:33,265
A SCREENPLAY
BY CROW T. ROBOT.

1013
00:40:33,298 --> 00:40:35,067
OKAY, OKAY, LET'S GO.

1014
00:40:35,100 --> 00:40:37,368
I'M ONLY DOING THIS BECAUSE I
NEED THE STAGE TIME, PIN BEAK.

1015
00:40:37,402 --> 00:40:38,437
OKAY, SERVO.

1016
00:40:38,470 --> 00:40:39,872
OKAY, OKAY.

1017
00:40:39,905 --> 00:40:42,975
ACT I-- PETER GRAVES ENROLLS
AT THE UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA.

1018
00:40:43,008 --> 00:40:45,277
- OKAY, OKAY, HERE WE GO.
- ♪♪ [HUMMING]

1019
00:40:45,310 --> 00:40:47,680
HI, I'M THE REGISTRAR.
MAY I HELP YOU?

1020
00:40:47,713 --> 00:40:49,348
YES, I'M PETER GRAVES,

1021
00:40:49,382 --> 00:40:54,253
AND I'D LIKE TO ENROLL
AT THE UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA.

1022
00:40:54,287 --> 00:40:56,288
THAT'S-- THAT'S IT.

1023
00:40:56,322 --> 00:40:57,657
ACT II.

1024
00:40:57,690 --> 00:40:58,690
MIKE, YOU'VE GOT TO HELP ME
WITH THE CHARACTER

1025
00:40:58,723 --> 00:40:59,992
BECAUSE I DON'T HAVE...

1026
00:41:00,025 --> 00:41:01,160
THANK YOU.

1027
00:41:01,193 --> 00:41:04,563
ACT II-- PETER GRAVES
ATTENDS HIS FIRST CLASS.

1028
00:41:04,597 --> 00:41:06,532
HI, I'M PETER GRAVES.

1029
00:41:06,565 --> 00:41:09,000
IS THIS BIOLOGY 101?

1030
00:41:09,033 --> 00:41:10,502
- YES.
- GOOD.

1031
00:41:10,535 --> 00:41:13,905
I'M PETER GRAVES,
AND I'M IN THE RIGHT CLASS.

1032
00:41:13,938 --> 00:41:17,508
HUH. UM, ACT III.

1033
00:41:17,542 --> 00:41:20,812
ACT III-- PETER GRAVES
ENJOYS DORM LIFE.

1034
00:41:20,845 --> 00:41:23,082
OKAY. THINK FAST.

1035
00:41:23,115 --> 00:41:25,350
AHA, I'M PETER GRAVES,

1036
00:41:25,383 --> 00:41:27,385
AND I'M ENJOYING
SOME GOOD NATURED RIBBING

1037
00:41:27,418 --> 00:41:29,322
WITH ONE OF MY MANY NEW PALS

1038
00:41:29,355 --> 00:41:32,490
HERE AT THE UNIVERSITY
OF MINNESOTA.

1039
00:41:32,523 --> 00:41:36,295
ACT IV-- EXTRACURRICULAR
ACTIVITIES.

1040
00:41:36,328 --> 00:41:38,663
OH, THIS IS GREAT, THIS ONE.

1041
00:41:38,697 --> 00:41:39,732
I'M PETER GRAVES,

1042
00:41:39,765 --> 00:41:40,900
AND I WAS WONDERING

1043
00:41:40,933 --> 00:41:42,868
IF YOU COULD DIRECT ME
TO THE NATATORIUM,

1044
00:41:42,902 --> 00:41:44,537
AS I'M ATTENDING A SWIM MEET.

1045
00:41:44,570 --> 00:41:45,803
IT'S THAT WAY.

1046
00:41:45,837 --> 00:41:48,873
THANK YOU.
I'M PETER GRAVES.

1047
00:41:48,907 --> 00:41:54,347
OKAY. UH, ACT V--
PETER FINDS HIS CALLING.

1048
00:41:54,380 --> 00:41:57,115
I'M PETER GRAVES,
AND I'M BEGINNING
TO TAKE AN INTEREST

1049
00:41:57,148 --> 00:41:59,618
IN THE THEATER ARTS
AND SPEECH COMMUNICATIONS

1050
00:41:59,652 --> 00:42:00,752
HERE AT THE UNIVERSITY OF--

1051
00:42:00,785 --> 00:42:02,722
- CROW, HOW MANY ACTS ARE THERE?
- WHAT?

1052
00:42:02,755 --> 00:42:04,423
UH, 15.

1053
00:42:04,457 --> 00:42:05,857
- UH, CROW?
- YEAH.

1054
00:42:05,890 --> 00:42:07,158
NOT CRITICIZING HERE,

1055
00:42:07,192 --> 00:42:09,962
BUT WERE YOU WORRIED
ABOUT THE REDUNDANCY FACTOR

1056
00:42:09,995 --> 00:42:11,630
OR NOT OR...?

1057
00:42:11,663 --> 00:42:14,098
WELL, I FELT MY POINT WAS
IMPORTANT ENOUGH TO RISK THAT,

1058
00:42:14,132 --> 00:42:15,300
BUT LET'S DO THE CLIMAX.

1059
00:42:15,333 --> 00:42:16,635
I THINK YOU'LL REALLY LIKE IT.

1060
00:42:16,668 --> 00:42:18,070
- OH, YEAH.
- LET'S GET TO THE CLIMAX.

1061
00:42:18,103 --> 00:42:19,905
ALL THE CARDS OVER NOW.

1062
00:42:19,938 --> 00:42:22,808
ACT 15, GRADUATION.

1063
00:42:22,842 --> 00:42:24,175
I'M PETER GRAVES.

1064
00:42:24,208 --> 00:42:25,610
THANK YOU FOR THE OPPORTUNITY

1065
00:42:25,643 --> 00:42:28,047
OF LEARNING
AT THIS FINE INSTITUTION.

1066
00:42:28,080 --> 00:42:29,213
AS I LOOK BACK,

1067
00:42:29,247 --> 00:42:31,883
I REMEMBER FONDLY
MY ENROLLMENT PROCESS

1068
00:42:31,917 --> 00:42:33,718
WHERE, HAD YOU BEEN THERE,

1069
00:42:33,752 --> 00:42:35,420
YOU MIGHT'VE HEARD ME SAY,

1070
00:42:35,453 --> 00:42:37,122
"HI, I'M PETER GRAVES,

1071
00:42:37,155 --> 00:42:40,792
AND I'D LIKE TO ENROLL AT
THE UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA"

1072
00:42:40,825 --> 00:42:42,193
OR THE TIME WHEN I--

1073
00:42:42,227 --> 00:42:44,663
THAT'S IT!
CROW, YOU ARE WAY OUT THERE!

1074
00:42:44,697 --> 00:42:47,232
- HEY.
- WAY OUT!

1075
00:42:47,265 --> 00:42:48,833
GEE, UH, OH...

1076
00:42:48,867 --> 00:42:50,568
I GOTTA AGREE WITH HIM, CROW.

1077
00:42:50,602 --> 00:42:52,337
NO, BUT, MIKE,

1078
00:42:52,370 --> 00:42:56,108
NO MATTER WHAT YOU OR SERVO
MAY THINK OF MY LITTLE
SCREENPLAY,

1079
00:42:56,142 --> 00:42:58,777
IF IT'S CONVINCED
JUST ONE PERSON OUT THERE

1080
00:42:58,810 --> 00:43:03,148
THAT PETER GRAVES WENT
TO THE UNIVERSITY OF MINNESOTA,

1081
00:43:03,182 --> 00:43:04,450
THEN I'VE DONE MY JOB.

1082
00:43:04,483 --> 00:43:06,285
- [ALARM BUZZING]
- I'M PETER GRAVES,

1083
00:43:06,318 --> 00:43:08,820
AND WE'VE GOT MOVIE SIGN
ON A&E.

1084
00:43:20,698 --> 00:43:21,867
[GASPS, MUTTERS]

1085
00:43:21,900 --> 00:43:23,668
- OH.
- THAT'S ENOUGH.

1086
00:43:23,702 --> 00:43:25,603
ALL RIGHT.

1087
00:43:25,637 --> 00:43:27,172
♪♪ [HUMMING]

1088
00:43:36,648 --> 00:43:38,517
- HEY, FRANK.
- HOW WAS THAT BROTHEL
LAST NIGHT?

1089
00:43:38,550 --> 00:43:41,987
MAYBE WE CAN TRAIN
ONE OF THESE GIANT CRICKETS
TO PULL A PLOW, HUH?

1090
00:43:42,020 --> 00:43:44,188
EVERYTHING'S NOT A JOKE, TED.

1091
00:43:44,222 --> 00:43:46,792
- I DON'T LIKE THIS THING.
- OH, TAKE IT EASY.

1092
00:43:46,825 --> 00:43:48,393
MAYBE THEY WERE BIG ANTS.

1093
00:43:48,427 --> 00:43:51,697
DIDN'T SEE THEM REAL GOOD,
DID YOU?

1094
00:43:51,730 --> 00:43:53,565
GRASSHOPPERS ARE GOOD EATING.

1095
00:43:53,598 --> 00:43:56,235
YEAH? MUSTARD OR KETCHUP?

1096
00:43:56,268 --> 00:43:58,470
SHOULDN'T THEY ALL BE
DIFFERENT ETHNIC TYPES?

1097
00:44:02,607 --> 00:44:03,742
NO. NO KIDDING.

1098
00:44:03,775 --> 00:44:05,277
ATE THEM ONCE DOWN IN MEXICO.

1099
00:44:05,310 --> 00:44:07,578
YOU BETTER WATCH YOUR STEP.
THEY LIABLE TO GET EVEN.

1100
00:44:07,612 --> 00:44:09,180
WE'RE HAVING A LIGHTHEARTED
CONVERSATION

1101
00:44:09,213 --> 00:44:11,317
IN THE MIDST
OF UNBEARABLE TENSION.

1102
00:44:14,185 --> 00:44:16,222
WELL, AT LEAST IT'S A NICE DAY
TO BE OUT, EH?

1103
00:44:16,255 --> 00:44:18,223
YOU MUST'VE SEEN SOMETHING.

1104
00:44:18,257 --> 00:44:20,392
MR. WAINWRIGHT'S A SCIENTIST.
HE'S TRAINED TO SEE THINGS
RIGHT.

1105
00:44:20,425 --> 00:44:22,527
THESE DAYS THEY BLAME
THE ATOM FOR EVERYTHING.

1106
00:44:22,560 --> 00:44:25,097
BAD HEALTH, BAD CROPS,
BAD WEATHER.

1107
00:44:25,130 --> 00:44:26,898
- BAD LIEUTENANT.
- NOW IT'S GRASSHOPPERS.

1108
00:44:26,932 --> 00:44:29,367
THEY COULDN'T HAVE JUST DREAMED
UP THIS GUY FRANK
BEING KNOCKED OFF.

1109
00:44:29,400 --> 00:44:32,337
- AH.
- [MOCKING] AH.

1110
00:44:32,370 --> 00:44:34,305
NOW, WERE YOUR GLASSES
IN THE CASE,

1111
00:44:34,338 --> 00:44:37,408
OR DID THEY JUST DROP
OUT OF YOUR POCKET?

1112
00:44:37,442 --> 00:44:39,412
- [CHIRPING]
- OH! OH, MR. KOT-TARE!

1113
00:44:44,082 --> 00:44:46,118
WHAT WOULD MITCHELL DO RIGHT
NOW, HUH?

1114
00:44:47,552 --> 00:44:49,755
GLADYS, QUIT BUGGING
THE STEVENS!

1115
00:44:54,025 --> 00:44:55,760
IT'S BERNARD HERRMANN MUSIC
OUT THERE.

1116
00:44:57,495 --> 00:45:00,165
THEY SENSE I'M PETER GRAVES.

1117
00:45:00,198 --> 00:45:03,602
THEY'RE ALL TOO EMBARRASSED
TO ADMIT THEY HEAR ANYTHING.

1118
00:45:05,037 --> 00:45:06,938
HEY, IS THIS
WHAT WE'RE LOOKING FOR?

1119
00:45:06,972 --> 00:45:08,507
- HUH?
- YOW.

1120
00:45:10,675 --> 00:45:13,612
SIT. STAY.

1121
00:45:13,645 --> 00:45:14,780
[SCREAMING]

1122
00:45:14,813 --> 00:45:18,317
JUST GET A GIANT SCREEN DOOR!

1123
00:45:18,350 --> 00:45:21,787
HEY, LET'S PULL ONE LEG OFF
AND WATCH IT TRY TO WALK.

1124
00:45:25,023 --> 00:45:29,462
I THINK WE SHOULD'VE WAITED
FOR THE SANCTIONS
TO TAKE EFFECT.

1125
00:45:29,495 --> 00:45:32,998
YOU SEE, IF YOU'RE GOING
TO HAVE A WAR,
YOU SHOULD WAIT FIRST.

1126
00:45:38,670 --> 00:45:40,572
[IMITATING GUN FIRE]

1127
00:45:43,775 --> 00:45:46,043
JUST RUN
IN THAT GENERAL DIRECTION.

1128
00:45:49,480 --> 00:45:51,617
WE'RE GOING TO GET
A LOT OF RAID, RIGHT?

1129
00:45:51,650 --> 00:45:55,753
WE'RE GOING TO GET A WHOLE LOT
OF RAIN, RIGHT?

1130
00:45:55,787 --> 00:45:57,957
EXTERMINATE
WITH EXTREME PREJUDICE.

1131
00:46:00,658 --> 00:46:02,627
OH, THIS IS A BUG HUNT, MAN.

1132
00:46:06,198 --> 00:46:09,535
♪ WHEN YOU WISH UPON A STAR ♪

1133
00:46:09,568 --> 00:46:13,805
SOMETIMES YOU CAN'T HEAR THE
PINCER WITH YOUR NAME ON IT.

1134
00:46:13,838 --> 00:46:16,908
HEY, YOU GUYS KNOW
WHERE WE CAN GET SOME DECENT
WEED AROUND HERE?

1135
00:46:19,043 --> 00:46:23,582
BETTER GET THE PLACE READY.
YEAH.

1136
00:46:25,217 --> 00:46:30,655
AMERICA RESPONDS TO THE NEW
ROBERT URICH/FAYE DUNAWAY
SITCOM!

1137
00:46:30,688 --> 00:46:33,025
AL BUNDY TAKES COMMAND!

1138
00:46:34,292 --> 00:46:35,793
CAN I GET A RIDE
WITH YOU GUYS?

1139
00:46:35,827 --> 00:46:37,162
HELP YOURSELF TO A GUN, PETER.

1140
00:46:44,168 --> 00:46:46,705
♪ JOHN JACOB
JINGLEHEIMER SCHMIDT ♪

1141
00:46:46,738 --> 00:46:48,240
OH, MY GOD!

1142
00:46:48,273 --> 00:46:49,808
INSECTS TRAINED
BY RUSS WEATHERWAX.

1143
00:46:49,842 --> 00:46:52,310
ONE WEEKEND A MONTH, MY ASS!

1144
00:46:53,912 --> 00:46:57,248
WELL, THAT WENT WELL.

1145
00:46:57,282 --> 00:46:58,583
AND EVERY AVAILABLE MAN.

1146
00:46:58,617 --> 00:47:00,152
I'M THROWING A PARTY.

1147
00:47:00,185 --> 00:47:01,653
ALSO GET SOME AIR SUPPORT.

1148
00:47:01,687 --> 00:47:03,122
WE'LL BOMB THEM
OUT OF THAT FOREST.

1149
00:47:03,155 --> 00:47:04,557
YEAH, THAT OUGHT TO HOLD
THE LITTLE...

1150
00:47:04,590 --> 00:47:05,757
WHAT ARE YOU GOING TO DO?

1151
00:47:05,790 --> 00:47:07,625
GOING IN THERE AND WIPE OUT
EVERY LAST ONE.

1152
00:47:07,658 --> 00:47:09,293
- THEY'LL SLAUGHTER YOU.
- NOT THIS TIME.

1153
00:47:09,327 --> 00:47:10,595
DIG THIS.

1154
00:47:10,628 --> 00:47:12,030
I WANT LIGHT AUXILIARY
BROUGHT UP WITH COMPANY H.

1155
00:47:12,063 --> 00:47:13,765
YOU DON'T HAVE ENOUGH MEN.

1156
00:47:13,798 --> 00:47:16,167
THERE WILL BE THREE REGIMENTS
OUT THERE TOMORROW BY 03:00.

1157
00:47:16,200 --> 00:47:18,070
YOU DON'T UNDERSTAND.
YOU STILL DON'T HAVE ENOUGH MEN.

1158
00:47:18,103 --> 00:47:19,337
NOT ENOUGH MEN FOR
A COUPLE HUNDRED LOCUSTS?

1159
00:47:19,370 --> 00:47:20,938
THERE ARE MORE
THAN A COUPLE HUNDRED.

1160
00:47:20,972 --> 00:47:23,342
- BUT YOU SAID BEFORE--
- THAT WAS BEFORE I HEARD THEM
SCREECH.

1161
00:47:23,375 --> 00:47:24,677
THE NOISE THEY MAKE CONVINCES
ME THERE ARE MORE.

1162
00:47:24,710 --> 00:47:26,010
HOW MANY ARE THERE?

1163
00:47:26,043 --> 00:47:27,445
I DON'T KNOW.
THERE COULD BE COUNTLESS
NUMBERS.

1164
00:47:27,478 --> 00:47:29,447
I THINK YOU BETTER CALL
IN THE REGULAR ARMY, TOM.

1165
00:47:29,480 --> 00:47:31,048
WHERE WOULD I GET OFF CALLING
THE REGULAR ARMY

1166
00:47:31,082 --> 00:47:32,417
TO HANDLE SOME OVERSIZED
GRASSHOPPERS?

1167
00:47:32,450 --> 00:47:33,852
BOYS, BOYS, DON'T FIGHT.

1168
00:47:33,885 --> 00:47:35,487
WHY, THEY'D SECTION EIGHT ME
RIGHT OUT OF THE SERVICE.

1169
00:47:35,520 --> 00:47:36,922
[PHONE RINGS]

1170
00:47:36,955 --> 00:47:39,390
LIEUTENANT, TAKE CHARGE
OF THE EAST SECTOR.

1171
00:47:39,423 --> 00:47:42,293
[GRUNTS]

1172
00:47:42,327 --> 00:47:45,197
HI, ANYONE FOR NUTTER-BUTTERS?

1173
00:47:45,230 --> 00:47:48,233
EXCUSE ME.
BUM LEG.

1174
00:47:48,267 --> 00:47:50,768
I'M AFRAID HE DOESN'T
UNDERSTAND HOW SERIOUS THIS IS.

1175
00:47:50,802 --> 00:47:53,538
AFTER ALL, HE KNOWS WHAT
THE MILITARY IS CAPABLE OF.

1176
00:47:53,572 --> 00:47:55,107
OH, JUST JUMP ON ME, TOO.

1177
00:47:55,140 --> 00:47:56,875
HE HAS FAITH IN REGIMENTAL
FIRE POWER

1178
00:47:56,908 --> 00:47:57,943
BECAUSE HE'S SEEN IT WORK.

1179
00:47:57,977 --> 00:47:59,410
♪ FAITH, FAITH, FAITH, BABY-- ♪

1180
00:47:59,443 --> 00:48:01,447
HE'S NEVER COME UP WITH
ANYTHING LIKE THIS BEFORE.

1181
00:48:01,480 --> 00:48:02,647
YOU'VE DONE ALL YOU CAN.

1182
00:48:02,680 --> 00:48:04,148
NO, NO, I HAVEN'T.

1183
00:48:04,182 --> 00:48:05,283
IN A WAY I FEEL RESPONSIBLE.

1184
00:48:05,317 --> 00:48:07,018
IN A WAY?

1185
00:48:07,052 --> 00:48:10,522
HE'S IN DEADLY DANGER
IF THOSE LOCUSTS BREAK OUT
OF THE FOREST.

1186
00:48:10,555 --> 00:48:11,923
WELL, BACK TO THE SALT MINE.

1187
00:48:11,957 --> 00:48:13,492
WHAT ARE YOU GOING TO DO?

1188
00:48:13,525 --> 00:48:14,760
I'M GOING TO WASHINGTON.

1189
00:48:14,793 --> 00:48:16,728
MAYBE THE ARMY PEOPLE
WILL LISTEN TO ME.

1190
00:48:16,762 --> 00:48:18,330
I'LL GO WITH YOU.
MAYBE I CAN HELP.

1191
00:48:18,363 --> 00:48:20,032
I SAW THEM, TOO.

1192
00:48:20,065 --> 00:48:21,500
- ALL RIGHT.
- MIND IF I CATCH A RIDE?

1193
00:48:21,533 --> 00:48:22,900
WE'VE GOT TO CONVINCE THEM,
AUDREY.

1194
00:48:22,933 --> 00:48:24,770
WE MAY BE WITNESSING
THE BEGINNING OF AN ERA

1195
00:48:24,803 --> 00:48:26,772
THAT'LL MEAN THE COMPLETE
ANNIHILATION OF MAN.

1196
00:48:26,805 --> 00:48:28,773
- HM.
- ANNIHILATION?

1197
00:48:28,807 --> 00:48:31,075
- WHAT WILL I WEAR?
- ANNIHILATION.

1198
00:48:31,108 --> 00:48:32,810
THE BEGINNING OF THE END.

1199
00:48:32,843 --> 00:48:36,147
UH, REAL GOOD, THEN.
BYE-BYE.

1200
00:48:36,180 --> 00:48:37,815
AND GUESTS OF
THE BEGINNING OF THE END

1201
00:48:37,848 --> 00:48:39,583
STAYED AT
THE BEAUTIFUL CAPITAL DOME.

1202
00:48:39,617 --> 00:48:40,918
INFERIOR GUESTS

1203
00:48:40,952 --> 00:48:44,923
STAY AT THE DEFENSE DEPARTMENT
ANNEX.

1204
00:48:44,957 --> 00:48:46,023
THIS, GENTLEMEN, IS THE ENEMY.

1205
00:48:46,057 --> 00:48:47,392
MOVING PICTURES.

1206
00:48:47,425 --> 00:48:49,828
THIS LOCUST, MORE COMMONLY
KNOWN AS THE GRASSHOPPER,

1207
00:48:49,862 --> 00:48:52,697
IS ALMOST IDENTICAL
TO THE GIANT LOCUSTS OF LUDLOW

1208
00:48:52,730 --> 00:48:54,432
EXCEPT FOR ITS SIZE

1209
00:48:54,465 --> 00:48:57,268
AND THE FACT THAT THE GIANTS'
WINGS FAILED TO DEVELOP.

1210
00:48:57,302 --> 00:48:58,503
THEY CANNOT FLY.

1211
00:48:58,537 --> 00:49:00,072
NOW I'LL GET COMFORTABLE.

1212
00:49:00,105 --> 00:49:02,273
THE LOCUST IS INTELLIGENT
BUT STRONG.

1213
00:49:02,307 --> 00:49:03,708
HE IS ARMED.

1214
00:49:03,742 --> 00:49:05,877
- LOCUSTS FOLLOW A LEADER.
- HIS NAME'S LARRY.

1215
00:49:05,910 --> 00:49:08,380
LIKE THE BEE AND THE ANT,
THEY'RE ABLE TO COMMUNICATE
WITH EACH OTHER.

1216
00:49:08,413 --> 00:49:10,582
- AUNT BEE?
- THIS COMMUNICATION, OR CALL,

1217
00:49:10,615 --> 00:49:12,083
IS PRODUCED BY THE HIND LEGS.

1218
00:49:12,117 --> 00:49:13,485
LET ME DEMONSTRATE.

1219
00:49:13,518 --> 00:49:16,488
THIS IS THE 1956 AUSTRALIAN
LOCUST PLAGUE.

1220
00:49:16,522 --> 00:49:18,190
AND THIS IS THE 1910
FRUITGUM COMPANY.

1221
00:49:18,223 --> 00:49:21,793
- COVERING AN AREA
OF 400 SQUARE MILES.
- SEEN IT.

1222
00:49:21,827 --> 00:49:24,930
- WE'VE BEEN PLAGUED BY LOCUSTS
SINCE BIBLICAL TIMES.
- YOU'RE NOT FUNNY.

1223
00:49:24,963 --> 00:49:26,498
- THERE ARE VARIOUS FORMS
OF COMBATING THEM.
- SIT DOWN.

1224
00:49:26,532 --> 00:49:28,167
AS A MATTER OF FACT,
IN OUR OWN COUNTRY,

1225
00:49:28,200 --> 00:49:30,735
THE EARLY SETTLERS OF THE
MASSACHUSETTS BAY COLONY...

1226
00:49:30,768 --> 00:49:33,472
- ARMED THEMSELVES
WITH BUNDLES OF BRUSH...
- OW, OW, OW...

1227
00:49:33,505 --> 00:49:36,273
AND DROVE MILLIONS OF LOCUSTS
INTO THE SEA.

1228
00:49:36,307 --> 00:49:41,447
TODAY, DESPITE THE FACT
THAT WE'VE DEVELOPED POWERFUL
INSECTICIDES...

1229
00:49:41,480 --> 00:49:42,647
I HAVEN'T GOT A SERIES.

1230
00:49:42,680 --> 00:49:44,015
...THE LOCUST
STILL INFLICTS DAMAGES

1231
00:49:44,048 --> 00:49:45,817
TO THE TUNE OF $25 MILLION

1232
00:49:45,850 --> 00:49:47,985
IN THE UNITED STATES ALONE--

1233
00:49:48,018 --> 00:49:50,755
CALIFORNIA, COLORADO, TEXAS.

1234
00:49:50,788 --> 00:49:52,323
UH, CONNECTICUT.

1235
00:49:52,357 --> 00:49:55,127
- EVEN THIS SMALL LOCUST
WILL ATTACK A MAN.
- LITTLE BASTARD.

1236
00:49:55,160 --> 00:49:56,495
IT HAS TWO POWERFUL JAWS

1237
00:49:56,528 --> 00:49:57,862
WITH A RIDGE FULL
OF SHARP TEETH.

1238
00:49:57,895 --> 00:49:59,363
AND THEY'RE VICIOUS GOSSIPS.

1239
00:49:59,397 --> 00:50:00,765
AND THEY'LL KILL OTHER INSECTS
AND DEVOUR THEM.

1240
00:50:00,798 --> 00:50:03,135
IF NO OTHER INSECTS
ARE AVAILABLE,

1241
00:50:03,168 --> 00:50:04,502
IT BECOMES A CANNIBAL,

1242
00:50:04,535 --> 00:50:06,037
TURNING ON ITS OWN KIND.

1243
00:50:06,070 --> 00:50:07,472
SHE WANTS ME.

1244
00:50:07,505 --> 00:50:11,142
WHAT IN THE GOOD GOD
ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

1245
00:50:11,175 --> 00:50:13,778
NOW, YOU'VE SEEN
WHAT THE LOCUSTS CAN DO
IN ITS NORMAL SIZE,

1246
00:50:13,812 --> 00:50:15,180
SMALLER THAN YOUR THUMB.

1247
00:50:15,213 --> 00:50:16,615
IMAGINE, IF YOU WILL,

1248
00:50:16,648 --> 00:50:18,250
A LOCUST THAT'S GROWN
BIGGER THAN A MAN

1249
00:50:18,283 --> 00:50:19,717
AND IS CONTINUING TO GROW,

1250
00:50:19,750 --> 00:50:21,420
SOME LARGER THAN OTHERS,
BUT EACH ONE A DEADLY KILLER.

1251
00:50:21,453 --> 00:50:22,687
I THINK IT'LL GO
SOMETHING LIKE THIS.

1252
00:50:22,720 --> 00:50:25,323
I HOPE YOU REALIZE
WE HAVEN'T MUCH TIME.

1253
00:50:25,357 --> 00:50:27,192
YOU ARE A SCIENTIST,
MR. WAINWRIGHT.

1254
00:50:27,225 --> 00:50:28,893
YOU KNOW WHAT LOCUSTS CAN DO.

1255
00:50:28,927 --> 00:50:31,663
- I'M A SOLDIER.
I KNOW WHAT GUNS CAN DO.
- TOGETHER WE COULD...

1256
00:50:31,697 --> 00:50:33,398
I FEEL SECURE THE ILLINOIS
NATIONAL GUARD

1257
00:50:33,432 --> 00:50:34,800
CAN HANDLE THIS SITUATION.

1258
00:50:34,833 --> 00:50:36,902
JUST LIKE THEY HANDLED
THE CHICAGO CONVENTION.

1259
00:50:36,935 --> 00:50:39,570
YOU WANT TO SAY SOMETHING,
GENERAL HANSON?

1260
00:50:39,603 --> 00:50:41,640
- NO, SIR.
- I'M DEEPLY ASHAMED.

1261
00:50:41,673 --> 00:50:44,175
I WAS GREATLY IMPRESSED
WITH YOUR PRESENTATION,
WAINWRIGHT.

1262
00:50:44,208 --> 00:50:45,743
I'M SURE ALL OF US WERE.

1263
00:50:45,777 --> 00:50:47,078
THANK YOU VERY MUCH
FOR COMING.

1264
00:50:47,112 --> 00:50:48,580
GO IN PEACE AND SAY NO MORE.

1265
00:50:48,613 --> 00:50:49,815
I'M AFRAID MY PRESENTATION

1266
00:50:49,848 --> 00:50:51,215
DIDN'T IMPRESS YOU
QUITE ENOUGH, GENERAL.

1267
00:50:51,248 --> 00:50:53,218
I DON'T UNDERSTAND YOU.

1268
00:50:53,252 --> 00:50:55,353
I MEAN, THAT WHEN
THE LOCUSTS START TO MOVE
OUT OF THAT FOREST,

1269
00:50:55,387 --> 00:50:57,022
I'M NOT SURE YOU'LL BE ABLE
TO STOP THEM.

1270
00:50:57,055 --> 00:50:59,557
WHAT ARE YOU SUGGESTING WE DO,
MR. WAINWRIGHT?

1271
00:50:59,590 --> 00:51:01,593
HIT THEM WITH EVERYTHING
YOU'VE GOT NOW.

1272
00:51:01,627 --> 00:51:02,960
YOU NEED MORE MEN,
A LOT MORE MEN.

1273
00:51:02,993 --> 00:51:04,495
YOU NEED TANKS
AND HEAVY ARTILLERY.

1274
00:51:04,528 --> 00:51:07,365
AS OF NOW THE FULL STRENGTH
OF THE ILLINOIS NATIONAL GUARD

1275
00:51:07,398 --> 00:51:09,868
IS IN THE LINE, SURROUNDING
THE LUDLOW NATIONAL FOREST.

1276
00:51:09,902 --> 00:51:11,002
GO AWAY NOW.

1277
00:51:11,035 --> 00:51:12,137
AS I SAID BEFORE,
MR. WAINWRIGHT,

1278
00:51:12,170 --> 00:51:13,438
YOU ARE A SCIENTIST.

1279
00:51:13,472 --> 00:51:15,407
WHY NOT LEAVE THE FIGHTING
TO THE MILITARY?

1280
00:51:15,440 --> 00:51:18,777
DID YOU JUST CALL ME A WUSSY?

1281
00:51:18,810 --> 00:51:21,780
WELL, GUESS I'LL JUST LEAVE YOU
A FEW OF MY BROCHURES.

1282
00:51:21,813 --> 00:51:24,082
NO, THAT'S FINE.
THANK YOU.

1283
00:51:24,115 --> 00:51:27,418
URGENT CALL FROM PAXTON,
ILLINOIS, SIR.

1284
00:51:29,955 --> 00:51:31,857
HERE, YOU TALK IN THIS END,
SIR.

1285
00:51:31,890 --> 00:51:34,860
- GENERAL SHORT HERE.
- GENERAL SHORTHAIR?

1286
00:51:34,893 --> 00:51:38,197
I DON'T KNOW, STUFFING.
WHATEVER YOU MAKE.

1287
00:51:38,230 --> 00:51:41,767
[MUFFLED]
HELP US, GENERAL...

1288
00:51:41,800 --> 00:51:44,002
HELP, PLEASE.

1289
00:51:44,035 --> 00:51:46,303
YOU WILL FLY TO PAXTON
WITH MR. WAINWRIGHT.

1290
00:51:46,337 --> 00:51:47,738
YOU'LL TAKE CHARGE
OF OPERATIONS.

1291
00:51:47,772 --> 00:51:49,340
HEY, I'M VINDICATED.
HOW MANY DEAD?

1292
00:51:49,373 --> 00:51:51,877
WAINWRIGHT,
I OWE YOU AN APOLOGY.

1293
00:51:51,910 --> 00:51:54,478
THE LOCUSTS HAVE BROKEN
THROUGH OUR DEFENSE LINE.

1294
00:51:54,512 --> 00:51:56,280
THOUSANDS OF CASUALTIES.

1295
00:51:56,313 --> 00:51:57,682
OUR TROOPS ARE REORGANIZING

1296
00:51:57,715 --> 00:52:00,085
TO PREVENT PAXTON ITSELF
FROM BEING OVERRUN.

1297
00:52:00,118 --> 00:52:02,320
I'M TRYING NOT TO LAUGH, SIR.

1298
00:52:02,353 --> 00:52:04,322
♪♪ [HUMMING
RAIDERS OF THE LOST ARK THEME]

1299
00:52:05,990 --> 00:52:08,927
THE HILL POSITION
IN THE SUBURBS OF PAXTON
MUST BE HELD.

1300
00:52:08,960 --> 00:52:10,795
OTHERWISE THE 100 MILES

1301
00:52:10,828 --> 00:52:12,130
BETWEEN PAXTON AND CHICAGO
WILL LIE OPEN.

1302
00:52:12,163 --> 00:52:14,098
CAN I GET SOME NUTS?

1303
00:52:14,132 --> 00:52:17,068
[MAN ON INTERCOM]
GENERAL, WE CAN'T LAND IN
PAXTON, SIR.

1304
00:52:17,102 --> 00:52:18,203
WHY NOT?

1305
00:52:18,237 --> 00:52:20,072
IT JUST CAME OVER THE RADIO,
SIR.

1306
00:52:20,105 --> 00:52:23,875
GIANT LOCUSTS HAVE OVERRUN
PAXTON AT 1400.

1307
00:52:25,743 --> 00:52:28,313
[MUFFLED]
I TOLD YOU SO.

1308
00:52:28,347 --> 00:52:29,447
HEAD FOR CHICAGO.

1309
00:52:29,480 --> 00:52:30,915
YES, SIR.

1310
00:52:30,948 --> 00:52:33,252
WELL, NO MORE LUNCHES
AT MILDA'S CAFE, HUH?

1311
00:52:41,927 --> 00:52:44,662
"DEAR ABBY, I'M AN ELDERLY
WOMAN WHO DOESN'T ENJOY SE--"

1312
00:52:44,695 --> 00:52:46,565
OH, THIS CAME
TO THE WRONG PLACE.

1313
00:52:46,598 --> 00:52:48,233
CAPTAIN,
I WANT THESE POSITIONS HELD,

1314
00:52:48,267 --> 00:52:49,367
AND I WANT THEM HELD
AT ALL COSTS,

1315
00:52:49,400 --> 00:52:51,135
IF HUMANLY POSSIBLE.

1316
00:52:51,168 --> 00:52:54,005
CAPTAIN, HAVE YOUR MAP PEOPLE
IMMEDIATELY TURN OUT OVER
300 OVERLAYS

1317
00:52:54,038 --> 00:52:58,108
SHOWING
THE CHICAGO DEFENSE LINE...

1318
00:52:58,142 --> 00:52:59,912
YES?

1319
00:52:59,945 --> 00:53:03,582
THANK YOU,
SERGEANT WHISPER THIN.

1320
00:53:03,615 --> 00:53:06,685
YES, NOTHING GETS TOBACCO JUICE
OUT OF YOUR CLOTHES.

1321
00:53:10,788 --> 00:53:13,458
BOY, I READ SLOW.

1322
00:53:13,492 --> 00:53:14,692
MAJOR EVERETT...

1323
00:53:14,725 --> 00:53:16,995
OUR ROAD TRIP TO PEORIA
HAS BEEN CANCELLED.

1324
00:53:17,028 --> 00:53:18,830
- HOW ABOUT SQUADRON 12?
- THEY HAVEN'T REPORTED IN YET,
GENERAL.

1325
00:53:18,863 --> 00:53:19,830
LET ME KNOW
THE MOMENT YOU HEAR.

1326
00:53:19,863 --> 00:53:21,065
YES, SIR.

1327
00:53:21,098 --> 00:53:22,800
- I'LL BE WITH YOU IN A MOMENT.
- OKAY, SON.

1328
00:53:22,833 --> 00:53:24,602
BILL, YOU'LL PROCEED AT ONCE

1329
00:53:24,635 --> 00:53:27,105
TO TEMPORARY GHQ CENTRAL SECTOR
AND ASSUME COMMAND.

1330
00:53:27,138 --> 00:53:29,807
- ROBERT FROST.
- YOU WILL ORDER THE 81st
ARMORED DIVISION

1331
00:53:29,840 --> 00:53:31,208
TO PROCEED WITHOUT DELAY

1332
00:53:31,242 --> 00:53:32,577
TO FORT SHERIDAN IN CHICAGO.

1333
00:53:32,610 --> 00:53:34,145
HAVE THE CG REPORT TO ME
UPON ARRIVAL.

1334
00:53:34,178 --> 00:53:35,580
AND GET THIS MAN AN ARM.

1335
00:53:35,613 --> 00:53:37,515
...THE DEFENSE DEPARTMENT TO
ALERT THE FOLLOWING DIVISIONS--

1336
00:53:37,548 --> 00:53:41,052
THE FIRST ARMORED,
THE 40th, THE FIRST AIRBORNE,

1337
00:53:41,085 --> 00:53:43,422
THE 92nd AND THE 76th.

1338
00:53:43,455 --> 00:53:44,422
OKAY, ANY SALAD WITH THAT?

1339
00:53:44,455 --> 00:53:45,923
UH, WHAT'S YOUR PROBLEM?

1340
00:53:45,957 --> 00:53:49,227
AT THE RATE REFUGES ARE POURING
INTO CHICAGO, GENERAL,

1341
00:53:49,260 --> 00:53:51,830
OUR EMERGENCY STAFF
WON'T LAST LONG.

1342
00:53:51,863 --> 00:53:54,967
THEN WE'LL FEED THEM CRICKETS.
YEAH. THAT'S IT.

1343
00:53:55,000 --> 00:53:57,068
ECH, NOW, WHY DID I DO THAT?

1344
00:54:00,438 --> 00:54:02,373
TOXAPHENE IS ONE
WE HAVEN'T TRIED.

1345
00:54:02,407 --> 00:54:03,542
HOW GOOD IS IT?

1346
00:54:03,575 --> 00:54:04,775
ALMOST AS POWERFUL
AS CHLORDANE.

1347
00:54:04,808 --> 00:54:06,177
WITH NO AFTER TASTE.

1348
00:54:06,210 --> 00:54:08,178
ALL RIGHT, SHIP 2,000 GALLONS
OUT TO THE BASE.

1349
00:54:08,212 --> 00:54:10,448
- TAKE A PINT FOR YOURSELF.
- EXCUSE ME.

1350
00:54:10,482 --> 00:54:13,418
[PHONE RINGS]

1351
00:54:13,452 --> 00:54:14,987
- HELLO.
- BAT LAB.

1352
00:54:15,020 --> 00:54:16,020
SPEAKING.

1353
00:54:16,053 --> 00:54:18,823
SQUADRON 12 JUST REPORTED.

1354
00:54:18,857 --> 00:54:21,125
THEY SAY THEY CAME DOWN
IN THE DAY

1355
00:54:21,158 --> 00:54:23,795
AND PRACTICALLY DROWNED
THE ENEMY IN INSECTICIDE.

1356
00:54:23,828 --> 00:54:25,097
I JUST GOT A HAIRCUT,
AND IT HURTS.

1357
00:54:25,130 --> 00:54:26,563
THE CHLORDANE DIDN'T EVEN
SLOW THEM DOWN.

1358
00:54:26,597 --> 00:54:28,600
THEY THREW IT BACK AT ME
AND LAUGHED.

1359
00:54:28,633 --> 00:54:30,102
WE'LL HAVE TO COME UP
WITH SOMETHING STRONGER.

1360
00:54:30,135 --> 00:54:32,503
I'LL DO MY BEST, GENERAL.

1361
00:54:32,537 --> 00:54:34,038
GOOD-BYE.

1362
00:54:34,072 --> 00:54:36,540
HOW ABOUT CHLORDANE
WITH A TINY DROP OF RETSIN?

1363
00:54:36,573 --> 00:54:38,075
IT'S NO GOOD.
FORGET IT.

1364
00:54:38,108 --> 00:54:39,677
DOESN'T CAUSE
ENOUGH BIRTH DEFECTS.

1365
00:54:41,980 --> 00:54:43,915
WHAT ELSE
CAN I DO AROUND HERE?

1366
00:54:43,948 --> 00:54:45,250
MAKE MYSELF USEFUL.

1367
00:54:47,818 --> 00:54:49,720
AH, HERE WE GO.

1368
00:54:49,753 --> 00:54:52,290
OH, NO, NEW PETITIONS
AGAINST TAX AGAIN?

1369
00:54:52,323 --> 00:54:55,260
DEAR GOD.

1370
00:54:55,293 --> 00:54:56,293
LOOKS PRETTY BAD, DOESN'T IT?

1371
00:54:56,327 --> 00:54:57,328
NO, YOU LOOK FINE.

1372
00:54:57,362 --> 00:54:58,697
THOUGHT YOU WENT BACK
TO NEW YORK?

1373
00:54:58,730 --> 00:55:00,865
WELL, THE BIG STORY IS HERE.

1374
00:55:00,898 --> 00:55:03,802
LOOK, YOUR EDITOR CALLED
YOU BACK BECAUSE IT WAS
TOO DANGEROUS.

1375
00:55:03,835 --> 00:55:08,338
I WANTED TO BE HERE.

1376
00:55:08,372 --> 00:55:10,275
NOTHING WE'VE DONE SO FAR--

1377
00:55:10,308 --> 00:55:12,143
INSECTICIDES, FIRE BOMBS,

1378
00:55:12,177 --> 00:55:14,712
NOTHING HAS DONE ANY GOOD.

1379
00:55:14,745 --> 00:55:16,380
AND SO LITTLE TIME.

1380
00:55:16,413 --> 00:55:18,315
WELL, YOU'RE DOING
EVERYTHING YOU CAN.

1381
00:55:18,348 --> 00:55:21,518
EVERYBODY IS,
BUT IT'S NOT GOOD ENOUGH.

1382
00:55:21,552 --> 00:55:23,287
MAYBE IF I TRY TO TOSS
A QUARTER INTO THAT THING.

1383
00:55:23,320 --> 00:55:26,323
IN TIME THE BEASTS
WILL INHERIT THE EARTH.

1384
00:55:26,357 --> 00:55:28,493
THERE'S YOUR ANSWER!
A FINE PILSNER!

1385
00:55:32,597 --> 00:55:37,002
LEE MARVIN IN THE BRIDGES
OF MADISON COUNTY.

1386
00:55:37,035 --> 00:55:38,770
♪♪ [HUMMING]

1387
00:55:42,773 --> 00:55:44,708
HEY, GENERAL, WHERE YOU GOING?

1388
00:55:44,742 --> 00:55:47,945
I'M GOING TO DECATUR!
I'M GONNA SHOOT THAT
PAPER-HANGING SON OF A BITCH!

1389
00:55:50,282 --> 00:55:51,382
[DEATH RATTLES]

1390
00:55:51,415 --> 00:55:52,583
SORRY ABOUT THAT. SORRY.

1391
00:55:54,285 --> 00:55:59,290
WELL, I GUESS WAIT TILL THE
GRASSHOPPERS SHOW UP, HUH?

1392
00:55:59,323 --> 00:56:01,425
ALL QUIET
IN THE WESTERN SUBURBS.

1393
00:56:07,498 --> 00:56:09,833
THERE'S NO SIGN OF THE LOCUSTS
YET, GENERAL.

1394
00:56:09,867 --> 00:56:11,168
OUT.

1395
00:56:11,202 --> 00:56:13,772
SHOULD WE JUST CONTINUE
FIRING AT RANDOM?

1396
00:56:15,973 --> 00:56:19,810
THE JACK BENNY PROGRAM.

1397
00:56:19,843 --> 00:56:22,247
AND WITH THE LOCK
OF FIVE DIVISIONS
TO THE WESTERN SOUTH...

1398
00:56:22,280 --> 00:56:23,782
MR. MITCHELL.

1399
00:56:23,815 --> 00:56:25,117
GENERAL HANSON IS CONFIDENT

1400
00:56:25,150 --> 00:56:26,785
THAT HE CAN KEEP THE MENACE
AT BAY.

1401
00:56:26,818 --> 00:56:28,185
THAT'S DENNIS THE MENACE.

1402
00:56:28,218 --> 00:56:30,053
THE AIR FORCE AND MARINES
ARE MOVING INTO POSITION.

1403
00:56:30,087 --> 00:56:34,092
TO BACK UP THOSE FORCES
ALREADY DEPLOYED BY THE ARMY.

1404
00:56:34,125 --> 00:56:36,995
THE ONE ADVANTAGE OUR FORCES
HOLD OVER THE ENEMY...

1405
00:56:37,028 --> 00:56:38,128
DON'T SIT SO CLOSE, DEAR.

1406
00:56:38,162 --> 00:56:39,563
...ALWAYS REVEAL
THEIR INTENTION TO ATTACK.

1407
00:56:39,597 --> 00:56:40,732
WHICH IS NICE.

1408
00:56:40,765 --> 00:56:42,333
BEFORE EVERY ATTACK,

1409
00:56:42,367 --> 00:56:44,068
THE LOCUSTS SEND FORTH
THIS WARNING

1410
00:56:44,102 --> 00:56:46,337
IN THE FORM
OF A HIGH-PITCHED SCREECH.

1411
00:56:46,370 --> 00:56:49,607
LOOKS LIKE THE SUN KING'S BELL
ON TOP OF THEIR TV

1412
00:56:49,640 --> 00:56:52,077
UNTIL IT REACHES
EAR SHATTERING PROPORTIONS.

1413
00:56:52,110 --> 00:56:53,478
SOUNDS LIKE MARIAH CAREY.

1414
00:56:53,512 --> 00:56:55,480
THE SCREECH REACHES
ITS FULL INTENSITY

1415
00:56:55,513 --> 00:56:58,382
WHEN THE LOCUSTS ATTACK.

1416
00:56:58,415 --> 00:57:00,518
COPY.

1417
00:57:00,552 --> 00:57:02,887
WE'VE GOT EVERY AVAILABLE MAN
ON THE LINE, MAJOR,

1418
00:57:02,920 --> 00:57:04,955
AND I THINK THERE'S NO QUESTION
BUT WHAT WILL BE.

1419
00:57:04,988 --> 00:57:06,892
- [CHIRPING]
- HUSH NOW.

1420
00:57:06,925 --> 00:57:13,532
OH, I LOVE A SPRING RAIN.

1421
00:57:13,565 --> 00:57:15,467
I SHOULDN'T HAVE WORN
MY BUTT DRESS.

1422
00:57:18,570 --> 00:57:20,372
OH, GREAT, THEY'RE EARLY.

1423
00:57:20,405 --> 00:57:22,207
[CLAMORING]

1424
00:57:22,240 --> 00:57:27,112
THE CUBS DON'T WIN THE PENNANT!
THE CUBS DON'T WIN THE PENNANT!

1425
00:57:27,145 --> 00:57:29,913
MEANWHILE,
AT THE BOY SCOUT JAMBOREE
AT POTTAWATTOMIE PARK...

1426
00:57:32,350 --> 00:57:33,852
I WANNA DRIVE YOUR TANK.

1427
00:57:33,885 --> 00:57:35,487
I CALL THE FRONT.

1428
00:57:37,222 --> 00:57:38,590
OH, SO FAR SEEMS PRETTY--

1429
00:57:38,623 --> 00:57:40,392
OH, MY GOD, LOOK OUT!

1430
00:57:40,425 --> 00:57:41,525
HOLD YOUR FIRE, MEN.

1431
00:57:41,558 --> 00:57:42,727
WE'LL NEGOTIATE!

1432
00:57:42,760 --> 00:57:44,362
CRICKET LIGHTER.

1433
00:57:44,395 --> 00:57:46,530
JUST $1.49.

1434
00:57:51,002 --> 00:57:52,503
- WOW.
- OH, I'M HIT.

1435
00:57:52,537 --> 00:57:56,875
THEY GOT JIMINY!
GET 'EM!

1436
00:57:56,908 --> 00:57:58,275
WE WERE PINNED
DOWN NEAR ELGIN.

1437
00:57:58,308 --> 00:58:00,478
AURORA WAS PRETTY BAD.

1438
00:58:00,512 --> 00:58:02,980
BAD, IT STUNK IN THERE.

1439
00:58:03,013 --> 00:58:04,682
WHOO, SWEAT LODGE.

1440
00:58:07,018 --> 00:58:10,053
OKAY, OKAY. OKAY, GOTCHA!

1441
00:58:12,490 --> 00:58:17,395
WHOOPS. OH, I'M SORRY.
LET ME CLEAR THE SHOT.

1442
00:58:17,428 --> 00:58:19,230
THIS IS WHERE YOU STEP BACK

1443
00:58:19,263 --> 00:58:21,665
AND SAY, THANK GOD
FOR MY EXOSKELETON.

1444
00:58:23,533 --> 00:58:25,403
[MUFFLED]
THIS IS FLYING OFFICER
JIM CAVANAUGH.

1445
00:58:25,437 --> 00:58:27,405
THE DAN RYAN'S COVERED WITH
TOBACCO JUICE.

1446
00:58:27,438 --> 00:58:29,407
YOU MIGHT WANT TO TRY AN
ALTERNATE ROUTE.

1447
00:58:29,440 --> 00:58:32,210
LET'S ALL WELCOME BOB HOPE,
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN.

1448
00:58:34,978 --> 00:58:37,115
EVEN OUT BEST FOOTAGE
CAN'T STOP THEM!

1449
00:58:39,183 --> 00:58:41,052
HAVE YOU SEEN
MY MOMMY AND DADDY?

1450
00:58:41,085 --> 00:58:43,153
[CRYING]

1451
00:58:43,187 --> 00:58:47,392
DAMN NAZI GRASSHOPPERS.

1452
00:58:47,425 --> 00:58:49,560
HI, I'M GOING TO SNEAK
IN HERE TO SAY,

1453
00:58:49,593 --> 00:58:50,962
"HOPE YOU'RE ENJOYING
THE SHOW.

1454
00:58:50,995 --> 00:58:52,097
BYE FOR NOW."

1455
00:58:52,130 --> 00:58:53,832
HO, I'VE GOT A GREAT GUN.

1456
00:58:53,865 --> 00:58:55,367
NO, I DON'T NEED A BAZOOKA.

1457
00:58:58,737 --> 00:59:02,440
THE ORKIN ARMY WILL STORM
THE BEACHES OF LAKE FOREST.

1458
00:59:04,542 --> 00:59:06,277
WE'RE GOING TO HAVE TO GET
ORGANIZED.

1459
00:59:06,310 --> 00:59:08,780
WE SHOULD NOT BE LOSING
TO GRASSHOPPERS, PEOPLE.

1460
00:59:16,387 --> 00:59:20,492
SO IS THIS PROTECTING CHICAGO
AT ALL COSTS, SIR?

1461
00:59:20,525 --> 00:59:22,460
THEY KEEP COMING, GENERAL.

1462
00:59:22,493 --> 00:59:25,930
THEY'RE LOBBING APHIDS AT US!

1463
00:59:25,963 --> 00:59:27,965
THEY'RE HAMMERING AT A SINGLE
POINT IN OUR LINE.

1464
00:59:27,998 --> 00:59:29,867
I DON'T KNOW HOW,
BUT THEY'VE ARRANGED AIR COVER

1465
00:59:29,900 --> 00:59:31,235
FROM THE MEXICAN ARMY.

1466
00:59:31,268 --> 00:59:33,772
THEY CUT OFF OUR SUPPLY LINES
AND ATE THE RADIO MEN.

1467
00:59:38,042 --> 00:59:40,478
NO GRASSHOPPERS WERE HURT
IN THE MAKING OF THIS FILM,
HUH?

1468
00:59:42,713 --> 00:59:45,617
I DON'T BELIEVE IT!
THEY'RE USING HANNIBAL'S
SURPRISE!

1469
00:59:50,822 --> 00:59:53,023
THEY KEEP COMING, GENERAL.

1470
00:59:53,057 --> 00:59:55,058
THEY'RE MOVING CLOSER.

1471
00:59:55,092 --> 00:59:57,195
STILL THEY COME,
WAVE AFTER WAVE.

1472
00:59:57,228 --> 00:59:58,595
THEY'VE BROKEN OUR CODE,

1473
00:59:58,628 --> 01:00:00,565
AND THE SERGEANT
WAS A GRASSHOPPER UNDER COVER.

1474
01:00:02,167 --> 01:00:05,102
[MUMBLING]
...COMING.

1475
01:00:05,135 --> 01:00:07,372
THEY'RE POURING THROUGH
A BREACH IN OUR LINES.

1476
01:00:07,405 --> 01:00:10,775
WE'RE BEING CUT OFF!

1477
01:00:10,808 --> 01:00:12,143
OH.

1478
01:00:20,518 --> 01:00:21,552
WE INTERRUPT THIS PROGRAM

1479
01:00:21,585 --> 01:00:22,820
FOR AN IMPORTANT ANNOUNCEMENT.

1480
01:00:22,853 --> 01:00:24,622
AAH!

1481
01:00:24,655 --> 01:00:26,190
...HAVE REACHED
THE CHICAGO SOUTH SIDE

1482
01:00:26,223 --> 01:00:27,558
AND NEARBY SUBURBS.

1483
01:00:27,592 --> 01:00:29,627
I REPEAT. THE GIANT LOCUSTS

1484
01:00:29,660 --> 01:00:31,162
THE CHICAGO SOUTH SIDE

1485
01:00:31,195 --> 01:00:32,463
AND NEARBY SUBURBS.

1486
01:00:32,497 --> 01:00:34,465
THEY CONTROL
THE CEMENT BUSINESS.

1487
01:00:34,498 --> 01:00:37,735
TAKE SHELTER IN BASEMENTS.
TAKE SHELTER IN...

1488
01:00:37,768 --> 01:00:39,503
DO NOT DRESS LINE GRAIN.

1489
01:00:39,537 --> 01:00:40,705
DO NOT PANIC.

1490
01:00:40,738 --> 01:00:42,807
LOVE GRAIN.

1491
01:00:42,840 --> 01:00:44,508
ATTENTION, PLEASE.

1492
01:00:44,542 --> 01:00:47,345
KEEP MOVING.
DO NOT BLOCK THE HIGHWAY.

1493
01:00:47,378 --> 01:00:50,448
DO NOT COVET
THY NEIGHBOR'S MANSERVANT.

1494
01:00:50,482 --> 01:00:53,785
STAMP ALL FIRES DEAD OUT.

1495
01:00:53,818 --> 01:00:56,720
DO NOT PANIC.
DO NOT PANIC.

1496
01:00:59,890 --> 01:01:01,958
OH, MY GOD.
OH, JEEZ.

1497
01:01:01,992 --> 01:01:03,127
OH, YAH.

1498
01:01:05,530 --> 01:01:07,432
HEY, HEY, I WANT
A CHICAGO-STYLE HOTDOG.

1499
01:01:10,702 --> 01:01:12,803
IN GRANT PARK,
ON LAKE SHORE DRIVE.

1500
01:01:14,738 --> 01:01:19,043
♪♪ [HUMS THEME
TO THE BOB NEWHART SHOW]

1501
01:01:19,077 --> 01:01:21,812
UH, EXCUSE ME, AM I ON 24?

1502
01:01:21,845 --> 01:01:24,348
YEAH, COME ON, BABY.
COMB THAT HAIR.

1503
01:01:24,382 --> 01:01:27,352
BOY, I WISH I WAS A TUB
OF DIPPITY-DO.

1504
01:01:27,385 --> 01:01:29,620
YES, YES.

1505
01:01:29,653 --> 01:01:31,688
THIS IS A SINGLE ROOM.

1506
01:01:31,722 --> 01:01:33,690
AH, YOU WOMEN TAKE SO LONG
TO GET READY.

1507
01:01:33,723 --> 01:01:35,058
I'M KIDDING.

1508
01:01:41,332 --> 01:01:43,968
I DIDN'T SAY
THE SKIRT WAS UGLY.

1509
01:01:44,002 --> 01:01:45,737
- GENERAL.
- ED, MISS AIMES.

1510
01:01:45,770 --> 01:01:46,937
GRAB A CHAIR AND SIT DOWN.

1511
01:01:46,970 --> 01:01:48,605
THEY'VE GOT A PICTURE
OF RUSS BENDER.

1512
01:01:48,638 --> 01:01:50,442
I SENT FOR YOU BECAUSE
OF A NEW DEVELOPMENT

1513
01:01:50,475 --> 01:01:51,642
IT MAY BE FAVORABLE TO US.

1514
01:01:51,675 --> 01:01:52,877
BRUCE GELLER CALLED.

1515
01:01:52,910 --> 01:01:54,378
THE LOCUSTS HAD STOPPED
THEIR ADVANCE.

1516
01:01:54,412 --> 01:01:56,147
THEY'RE HUDDLED
IN THE ALLEYS AND BUILDINGS

1517
01:01:56,180 --> 01:01:57,315
JUST OUTSIDE THE LOOP.

1518
01:01:57,348 --> 01:01:58,715
THE LOCUSTS GET COLD.

1519
01:01:58,748 --> 01:02:01,052
WHEN THE TEMPERATURE
DROPS BELOW 68 DEGREES.

1520
01:02:01,085 --> 01:02:02,487
THEY JUST STOP MOVING.

1521
01:02:02,520 --> 01:02:05,255
MAYBE NOW'S THE TIME WE CAN
MOVE IN AND DESTROY THEM.

1522
01:02:05,288 --> 01:02:06,957
THEY AREN'T IN HIBERNATION,
SIR.

1523
01:02:06,990 --> 01:02:08,358
THEY'LL MOVE
IF THEY'RE PROVOKED,

1524
01:02:08,392 --> 01:02:09,693
AND THEY'RE JUST AS DEADLY
AS EVER.

1525
01:02:09,727 --> 01:02:10,728
JUST SHOOT ME DOWN.

1526
01:02:10,762 --> 01:02:12,230
WHEN THE SUN COMES OUT
TOMORROW,

1527
01:02:12,263 --> 01:02:13,363
THEY'LL BE ACTIVE AGAIN.

1528
01:02:13,397 --> 01:02:15,533
THE AIR FORCE IS STANDING BY

1529
01:02:15,567 --> 01:02:17,802
WITH A B52 LOADED
WITH AN ATOM BOMB.

1530
01:02:17,835 --> 01:02:19,737
OH, GOOD,
MAYBE THEY'LL GET LARGER.

1531
01:02:19,770 --> 01:02:21,738
YOU CAN'T DROP AN ATOM BOMB
ON CHICAGO.

1532
01:02:21,772 --> 01:02:23,007
SURE YOU CAN.

1533
01:02:23,040 --> 01:02:25,342
WASHINGTON HAS GIVEN ME
AUTHORITY TO DO JUST THAT,

1534
01:02:25,375 --> 01:02:27,110
AS A LAST CONTINGENCY.

1535
01:02:27,143 --> 01:02:28,947
IF THE BOMB IS DROPPED
EARLY TOMORROW,

1536
01:02:28,980 --> 01:02:30,615
THERE WILL BE NO LOSS OF LIFE.

1537
01:02:30,648 --> 01:02:32,750
THE CITY WILL BE EVACUATED
BY THEN.

1538
01:02:32,783 --> 01:02:34,085
WHAT ABOUT THE PROPERTY?

1539
01:02:34,118 --> 01:02:36,253
THERE WILL BE A BILLION DOLLARS
WORTH OF DAMAGE

1540
01:02:36,287 --> 01:02:38,755
AND A SITE THAT'S TOO
CONTAMINATED TO REBUILD ON.

1541
01:02:38,788 --> 01:02:40,858
- I REALIZE THAT.
- I JUST DON'T CARE.

1542
01:02:40,892 --> 01:02:41,958
BUT IF WE DON'T DROP THE BOMB,

1543
01:02:41,992 --> 01:02:43,627
CHICAGO WILL ALMOST CERTAINLY
FALL.

1544
01:02:43,660 --> 01:02:46,297
LOOK, WE'LL MOVE THE LOOP
TO SCHAUMBURG.

1545
01:02:46,330 --> 01:02:48,232
WE'LL DROP AT DAWN.

1546
01:02:48,265 --> 01:02:51,002
IF WE DON'T COME UP
WITH SOMETHING BY THEN,

1547
01:02:51,035 --> 01:02:52,903
I'LL MAKE A FINAL CHECK
WITH WASHINGTON

1548
01:02:52,937 --> 01:02:54,538
AND RELAY THEIR OKAY.

1549
01:02:54,572 --> 01:02:57,642
NO CHICAGO?
BUT WHY NOT?

1550
01:02:57,675 --> 01:03:00,512
ISN'T THERE A CHANCE THE LOCUSTS
COULD DIE IN THE NIGHT

1551
01:03:00,545 --> 01:03:01,712
OF THE COLD?

1552
01:03:01,745 --> 01:03:03,547
NO, NOT AT THIS TIME OF YEAR.

1553
01:03:03,580 --> 01:03:04,615
ANYWAY, THEY GOT BLANKETS.

1554
01:03:04,648 --> 01:03:06,283
TAKES 24 HOURS OF EXPOSURE

1555
01:03:06,317 --> 01:03:07,418
AT 14 DEGREES.

1556
01:03:07,452 --> 01:03:09,287
IS THAT COLD? 14?

1557
01:03:09,320 --> 01:03:11,888
ISN'T THERE SOME WAY YOU COULD
DRIVE THEM INTO THE LAKE.

1558
01:03:11,922 --> 01:03:14,725
IN WASHINGTON, YOU SAID
THE SETTLERS DID THAT.

1559
01:03:14,758 --> 01:03:17,295
- [GENERAL] SETTLERS.
- HM?

1560
01:03:17,328 --> 01:03:18,728
OH, YEAH, PEOPLE WHO SETTLE.

1561
01:03:18,762 --> 01:03:20,297
HE EARLY SETTLERS
IN MASSACHUSETTS

1562
01:03:20,330 --> 01:03:22,933
DID LITERALLY DRIVE THEM
INTO THE SEA,

1563
01:03:22,967 --> 01:03:24,502
- BUT THEY WEREN'T DEALING
WITH GIANTS.
- [RADIO WHISTLING]

1564
01:03:24,535 --> 01:03:25,637
OH, THAT'S MY DARJEELING.

1565
01:03:27,672 --> 01:03:30,507
WAIT A MINUTE.

1566
01:03:30,540 --> 01:03:31,908
WE CAN'T DRIVE THEM.

1567
01:03:31,942 --> 01:03:35,780
- WE CAN INVITE THEM TO LEAVE.
- NOT DRIVE.

1568
01:03:35,813 --> 01:03:37,382
WE COULD ATTRACT THEM.

1569
01:03:37,415 --> 01:03:38,515
ATTRACT.

1570
01:03:38,548 --> 01:03:39,750
I'LL DRESS LIKE
A SEXY GRASSHOPPER.

1571
01:03:39,783 --> 01:03:40,785
REPRODUCE THEIR CALL, GENERAL.

1572
01:03:40,818 --> 01:03:42,720
IT MIGHT WORK.
IT JUST MIGHT WORK.

1573
01:03:42,753 --> 01:03:44,022
A CALL FOR INSECTS?

1574
01:03:44,055 --> 01:03:45,455
CALL FOR INSECTS.
CALL FOR INSECTS.

1575
01:03:45,488 --> 01:03:47,492
HAVE YOU EVER BEEN DUCK HUNTING,
GENERAL?

1576
01:03:47,525 --> 01:03:48,758
A DUCK CALL.

1577
01:03:48,792 --> 01:03:50,193
YES, THERE'S ONE FOR BEES, TOO.

1578
01:03:50,227 --> 01:03:51,528
THEY USE IT IN APIARIES.

1579
01:03:51,562 --> 01:03:52,730
- BEE CALL?
- IT MIGHT WORK.

1580
01:03:52,763 --> 01:03:54,132
WHAT DO YOU NEED?

1581
01:03:54,165 --> 01:03:56,733
A TENNIS BALL, AN ACCORDION,
AND A PICTURE OF DON AMECHE.

1582
01:03:56,767 --> 01:03:59,303
I NEED AN AUDIO OSCILLATOR.

1583
01:03:59,337 --> 01:04:01,372
I NEED AN AUDIO-- TWO--
TWO AUDIO OSCILLATORS.

1584
01:04:01,405 --> 01:04:02,407
THREE-THREE-FOUR.
MAKE IT FOUR.

1585
01:04:02,440 --> 01:04:04,242
I NEED AN OSCILLOSCOPE.

1586
01:04:04,275 --> 01:04:06,843
I NEED SOME HIGH-FREQUENCY
RADIO EQUIPMENT.

1587
01:04:06,877 --> 01:04:09,713
AND A BOAT, A FAST BOAT.

1588
01:04:09,747 --> 01:04:10,915
WHATEVER YOU NEED, WE'LL GET.

1589
01:04:10,948 --> 01:04:12,550
OH, THEN A BOTTLE
OF JOHNNIE WALKER BLUE.

1590
01:04:12,583 --> 01:04:14,118
THERE'S SOMETHING
I HAVE TO GET MYSELF,

1591
01:04:14,152 --> 01:04:15,953
SOMETHING THAT'LL TELL ME
WHEN I'VE SUCCEEDED.

1592
01:04:15,987 --> 01:04:17,255
WHAT'S THAT?

1593
01:04:17,288 --> 01:04:18,822
I LIVE GIANT GRASSHOPPER.

1594
01:04:18,855 --> 01:04:20,557
GET OUT.

1595
01:04:20,590 --> 01:04:22,025
I'M NOT WITH HIM.

1596
01:04:24,828 --> 01:04:26,563
HERE, LIVE GIANT GRASSHOPPER.

1597
01:04:26,597 --> 01:04:29,667
[WHISTLES]
HERE, LIVE GIANT
GRASSHOPPER BOY.

1598
01:04:29,700 --> 01:04:32,703
ALL RIGHT, DROP YOUR SEGMENTED
THORAX AND COME OUT.

1599
01:04:32,737 --> 01:04:34,638
WE'VE GOT YOUR BLADE OF GRASS
SURROUNDED.

1600
01:04:34,672 --> 01:04:38,275
♪ I SING WHENEVER
I SING WHENEVER I SING ♪

1601
01:04:38,308 --> 01:04:41,178
♪♪ [HUMMING]

1602
01:04:41,212 --> 01:04:44,115
SIR, PLEASE.

1603
01:04:44,148 --> 01:04:47,618
SAVAGES. WORSE THAN BRITISH
SOCCER FANS.

1604
01:04:47,652 --> 01:04:50,087
THEY'VE GOT TO BE
AROUND HERE SOMEWHERE.

1605
01:04:50,120 --> 01:04:51,922
HEY, HEY, HEY,
THEY'RE STEALING THE TRUCK!

1606
01:04:51,955 --> 01:04:53,557
- HEY!
- SO LONG, SUCKERS.

1607
01:04:58,162 --> 01:05:00,798
ALL RIGHT, MEN.
OFF THE TRUCK.

1608
01:05:00,832 --> 01:05:02,367
OW. OW.

1609
01:05:03,733 --> 01:05:06,270
MAJOR, I SUGGEST THAT YOU SEND
SOME OF THEM THAT WAY

1610
01:05:06,303 --> 01:05:07,538
AND SOME DOWN THERE,

1611
01:05:07,572 --> 01:05:09,207
AND YOU AND I TRY THE ALLEY.

1612
01:05:09,240 --> 01:05:10,207
BRILLIANT!

1613
01:05:10,240 --> 01:05:11,875
NOW, YOU FOUR MEN GO THAT WAY.

1614
01:05:11,908 --> 01:05:13,110
YOU MEN THAT WAY.

1615
01:05:13,143 --> 01:05:16,180
JUST GO OUT ANYWHERE.
YOU KNOW WHAT TO DO.

1616
01:05:20,317 --> 01:05:23,620
WHAT IS THIS, A WELCOME RESPITE
FROM ALL THE ACTION?

1617
01:05:25,022 --> 01:05:26,657
YOU KNOW, MAJOR,

1618
01:05:26,690 --> 01:05:30,828
LATELY I'VE BEEN WATCHING
THE UNFOLDING OF ME.

1619
01:05:30,862 --> 01:05:32,262
AND YET I CAN'T LOVE.

1620
01:05:32,295 --> 01:05:33,663
I APPRECIATE THAT.

1621
01:05:33,697 --> 01:05:37,033
YET I DON'T THINK
IT'S APPROPRIATE RIGHT NOW.

1622
01:05:37,067 --> 01:05:40,972
SO, DOC, HOW'S THE SCIENCE GAME
WORKING OUT FOR YOU?

1623
01:05:41,005 --> 01:05:42,740
I THOUGHT ABOUT GETTING
INTO SCIENCE.

1624
01:05:42,773 --> 01:05:45,677
I GOT A C IN IT
IN JUNIOR HIGH.

1625
01:05:45,710 --> 01:05:47,745
ACTUALLY IT WAS INTERIOR DESIGN
ALWAYS THRILLED ME.

1626
01:05:47,778 --> 01:05:49,547
THAT WAS MY KNACK FOR A WHILE.

1627
01:05:49,580 --> 01:05:51,448
TEXTURES AND--

1628
01:05:51,482 --> 01:05:53,617
THEY JUST SET OFF
THE GRASSHOPPER ALARM.

1629
01:05:53,650 --> 01:05:55,753
♪ THE NIGHT CHICAGO DIED ♪

1630
01:05:55,787 --> 01:05:56,787
♪♪ [HUMMING]

1631
01:05:56,820 --> 01:05:59,123
SHUT UP.

1632
01:05:59,157 --> 01:06:03,860
- [CAN RATTLES]
- [IMITATES MACHINE GUN]

1633
01:06:03,893 --> 01:06:05,697
OH, SORRY.

1634
01:06:05,730 --> 01:06:08,498
SO IF THEY SCISSOR ME IN HALF
WITH THEIR POWERFUL JAWS,

1635
01:06:08,532 --> 01:06:11,568
PLEASE DON'T KEEP ME ALIVE.

1636
01:06:11,602 --> 01:06:14,405
SCIENCE AND THE MILITARY
WORKING SIDE BY SIDE.

1637
01:06:17,742 --> 01:06:19,810
THAT'S WHERE THE GRASSHOPPERS
GO TO SMOKE.

1638
01:06:21,045 --> 01:06:22,647
FINALLY THE MEN'S ROOM.

1639
01:06:22,680 --> 01:06:25,382
I'VE BEEN LOOKING FOR THAT.

1640
01:06:25,415 --> 01:06:27,017
I KNOW WHAT YOU'RE THINKING,
GRASSHOPPER.

1641
01:06:27,050 --> 01:06:28,985
DID I FIRE SIX SHOTS OR...

1642
01:06:29,018 --> 01:06:30,653
[GRUNTS]
OH.

1643
01:06:31,788 --> 01:06:33,723
I WASN'T SCARED.
WERE YOU SCARED?

1644
01:06:33,757 --> 01:06:35,558
[CHIRPING]

1645
01:06:36,893 --> 01:06:38,795
IT'S THAT DAMN KID
ON THE POGO STICK AGAIN.

1646
01:06:38,828 --> 01:06:40,732
LET'S GET HIM.

1647
01:06:42,900 --> 01:06:47,037
LOUIS, I THINK THIS IS GOING
TO BE THE BEGINNING
OF A BEAUTIFUL FRIENDSHIP.

1648
01:06:47,070 --> 01:06:48,538
I'M PETER GRAVES.

1649
01:06:48,572 --> 01:06:50,842
HEY. YOU KNOW,
GIANT GRASSHOPPERS--

1650
01:06:50,875 --> 01:06:52,643
YOU JUST TAKE IT FOR GRANTED
YOU CAN FIND THEM,

1651
01:06:52,677 --> 01:06:59,150
AND THEN WHEN YOU WANT THEM,
THEY DISAPPEAR.

1652
01:06:59,183 --> 01:07:04,555
YES, I JERK.
OH, GOD, LEAVE ME ALONE.

1653
01:07:04,588 --> 01:07:06,223
YOU KNOW, CHICAGO
IS A 24-HOUR TOWN.

1654
01:07:06,257 --> 01:07:07,223
YEP.

1655
01:07:07,257 --> 01:07:08,558
TRUMPY.

1656
01:07:08,592 --> 01:07:09,793
HEY.

1657
01:07:12,897 --> 01:07:14,265
[BLOWING WHISTLE]

1658
01:07:14,298 --> 01:07:16,133
THE VON TRAPPS HAVE ESCAPED!

1659
01:07:16,167 --> 01:07:17,868
COME ON! WE GOT ONE IN HERE!

1660
01:07:17,902 --> 01:07:20,170
COME ON!

1661
01:07:20,203 --> 01:07:22,205
AND KEEP QUIET.
WE JUST GOT HIM DOWN.

1662
01:07:27,110 --> 01:07:31,748
MEANWHILE, IN CASTLE WRIGLEY.

1663
01:07:31,782 --> 01:07:33,317
YOU'RE DEAD, GRAVES.

1664
01:07:33,350 --> 01:07:34,385
I'VE GOT FRIENDS.

1665
01:07:34,418 --> 01:07:37,087
THIS IS A DEAD MAN
I'M LOOKING AT.

1666
01:07:37,120 --> 01:07:40,123
WELL, IT LOOKS LIKE YOU WERE
HAVING A PRETTY GOOD TIME
FOR YOURSELF

1667
01:07:40,157 --> 01:07:43,060
OUT IN PEORIA LAST NIGHT,
EH, HOPPY?

1668
01:07:43,093 --> 01:07:45,762
IT'S LUCKY WE GOT
ONE OF THE SMALLER GUYS.

1669
01:07:45,795 --> 01:07:49,333
THIS'LL GO EASY ON YOUR IF YOU
JUST GIVE US SOME NAMES.

1670
01:07:49,367 --> 01:07:50,767
NOT TOO CLOSE, MAJOR.

1671
01:07:50,800 --> 01:07:52,035
WE PUT THAT CAGE UP
IN A HURRY,

1672
01:07:52,068 --> 01:07:53,170
AND I DON'T KNOW
HOW STRONG IT IS.

1673
01:07:53,203 --> 01:07:54,872
HOW ABOUT SOME GRASS
IN HERE?

1674
01:07:54,905 --> 01:07:57,742
A MONTH AGO I WAS TEACHING MY
ENGINEERING CLASS AT UNIVERSITY.

1675
01:07:57,775 --> 01:07:59,677
IT WAS SAFE AND SECURE.

1676
01:07:59,710 --> 01:08:01,178
BUT LOOK AT ME NOW.

1677
01:08:01,212 --> 01:08:03,280
I'M NOT SAFE AND SECURE.

1678
01:08:05,850 --> 01:08:07,685
NOW I'M 37 YEARS OLD,

1679
01:08:07,718 --> 01:08:09,820
AND ALL OF A SUDDEN I REALIZE
FOR THE FIRST TIME

1680
01:08:09,853 --> 01:08:11,122
HOW MUCH I'VE TAKEN LIFE
FOR GRANTED.

1681
01:08:11,155 --> 01:08:12,757
NOT NOW.

1682
01:08:12,790 --> 01:08:15,292
I GUESS THAT'S SOMETHING YOU
CAN'T TAKE FOR GRANTED, MAJOR.

1683
01:08:15,325 --> 01:08:17,595
ED, HOW WILL YOU KNOW WHEN
YOU'VE GOT THE RIGHT SOUND?

1684
01:08:17,628 --> 01:08:18,962
- I HAVE NO IDEA.
- HE'LL TELL US.

1685
01:08:18,995 --> 01:08:21,598
- HOW?
- HE'LL REACT TO IT.

1686
01:08:21,632 --> 01:08:24,435
AND THIS POLYGRAPH
WILL RECORD HIS REACTION.

1687
01:08:24,468 --> 01:08:26,137
HOW LONG WILL IT TAKE?

1688
01:08:26,170 --> 01:08:27,772
IT'S A MATTER
OF TRIAL AND ERROR.

1689
01:08:27,805 --> 01:08:29,407
COULD TAKE 10 MINUTES
OR 10 HOURS.

1690
01:08:29,440 --> 01:08:31,308
I THINK PETE
WAS AFFECTED BY THAT GAS.

1691
01:08:31,342 --> 01:08:32,977
- YEAH.
- WE DON'T HAVE 10 HOURS.

1692
01:08:33,010 --> 01:08:34,110
WE'VE GOT THEATER TICKETS.

1693
01:08:34,143 --> 01:08:36,480
THEY'RE DROPPING
THAT BOMB AT DAWN.

1694
01:08:36,513 --> 01:08:38,282
I HATE TO ASK YOU THIS,

1695
01:08:38,315 --> 01:08:40,650
BUT WHERE ARE YOUR NIPPLES?

1696
01:08:40,683 --> 01:08:43,520
HOW DOES THIS WORK?

1697
01:08:43,553 --> 01:08:46,523
WELL, I'VE JUST ATTACHED THESE
WIRES FROM THE POLYGRAPH

1698
01:08:46,557 --> 01:08:49,293
TO THE TWO COPPER STRIPS
AT THE BASE OF THE CAGE.

1699
01:08:49,327 --> 01:08:51,262
NOW, THE LOCUST,
LIKE EVERY OTHER LIVING THING,

1700
01:08:51,295 --> 01:08:53,197
HAS GALVANIC REFLEXES.

1701
01:08:53,230 --> 01:08:54,598
COME HERE, JUST CLOSER.
COME ON.

1702
01:08:54,632 --> 01:08:57,602
...IN DIRECT RATIO WITH ACTIVITY
OR EMOTIONAL STIMULATION.

1703
01:08:57,635 --> 01:08:58,668
NEXT TIME, FLAT FOOT,
YOU'RE MINE.

1704
01:08:58,702 --> 01:08:59,770
I DON'T UNDERSTAND.

1705
01:08:59,803 --> 01:09:01,038
IN OTHER WORDS,

1706
01:09:01,072 --> 01:09:02,807
WHEN WE HIT
THE CORRECT SOUND OR SIGNAL,

1707
01:09:02,840 --> 01:09:04,475
THE GRASSHOPPER
WILL REACT TO IT,

1708
01:09:04,508 --> 01:09:06,077
AND THE POLYGRAPH
WILL RECORD THE CHANGE.

1709
01:09:06,110 --> 01:09:07,778
MM-HM. HM.

1710
01:09:07,812 --> 01:09:10,080
YOU NOTICE HOW STEADY
AND REGULAR THE MOVEMENT
OF THE NEEDLE IS NOW?

1711
01:09:10,113 --> 01:09:11,482
OH, YES.

1712
01:09:11,515 --> 01:09:13,250
WHEN WE REPRODUCE
THE GRASSHOPPER'S CALL,

1713
01:09:13,283 --> 01:09:15,887
THE LINES WILL BECOME LONGER
AND HIGHLY IRREGULAR.

1714
01:09:15,920 --> 01:09:17,487
LIKE A LIE DETECTOR TEST.

1715
01:09:17,520 --> 01:09:18,888
SIT DOWN.

1716
01:09:18,922 --> 01:09:21,258
THIS IS THE FIRST TIME
A GRASSHOPPER EVER GOT ONE.

1717
01:09:21,292 --> 01:09:23,893
NOW, IF YOU'LL KEEP YOUR EYE
ON THE NEEDLE
FOR ANY UNUSUAL JUMPS...

1718
01:09:23,927 --> 01:09:26,930
WE'LL JUST HEAD OFF.
GOT A LITTLE SURPRISE
FOR YOU GUYS.

1719
01:09:26,963 --> 01:09:28,232
- GOODY.
- THIS IS GOING TO BE
REALLY FUN.

1720
01:09:28,265 --> 01:09:29,500
WILL YOU SET UP
THAT BIG BRICK WALL?

1721
01:09:44,815 --> 01:09:48,418
- [LAUGHING]
- OKAY, MR. TOM SERVO,
ARE YOU READY FOR THIS?

1722
01:09:48,452 --> 01:09:49,620
OH, YOU BET, MIKE.

1723
01:09:49,653 --> 01:09:50,988
THIS MOVIE'S GIVEN ME
A GREAT IDEA

1724
01:09:51,022 --> 01:09:52,155
FOR A STAND-UP ROUTINE.

1725
01:09:52,188 --> 01:09:53,723
NOW, TAKE YOUR SEAT.
GET READY.

1726
01:09:53,757 --> 01:09:56,293
OKAY, LIGHTS, CAMBOT.

1727
01:09:56,327 --> 01:09:57,393
THANK YOU,
THANK YOU, EVERYBODY.

1728
01:09:57,427 --> 01:09:59,195
WHAT A BEAUTIFUL CROWD TONIGHT,
HUH?

1729
01:09:59,228 --> 01:10:03,367
SAY, DID YOU EVER NOTICE
THE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN
GRASSHOPPERS AND LOCUSTS?

1730
01:10:03,400 --> 01:10:06,437
WELL, FOR ONE THING,
LOCUSTS HAVE SHORTER ANTENNAE
THAN GRASSHOPPERS.

1731
01:10:06,470 --> 01:10:08,305
GRASSHOPPER'S WALKING
DOWN THE STREET LIKE,

1732
01:10:08,338 --> 01:10:11,175
"HEY, LOOK AT ME.
I'VE GOT SOME BIG ANTENNAE."

1733
01:10:11,208 --> 01:10:13,143
WHERE A LOCUST IS WALKING DOWN
THE STREET, IT'S MORE LIKE,

1734
01:10:13,177 --> 01:10:16,947
"OH, NO, MY ANTENNAE
ARE SO SMALL."

1735
01:10:16,980 --> 01:10:18,848
SMALLER ANTENNAE, YOU SEE,
ON THE LOC--

1736
01:10:18,882 --> 01:10:20,250
HAVE YOU CHECKED OUT
THE OVIPOSITOR

1737
01:10:20,283 --> 01:10:21,885
IN A FEMALE GRASSHOPPER?

1738
01:10:21,918 --> 01:10:23,787
YOU SEE, THEY USE THEM
TO DRILL HOLES IN THE GRASS.

1739
01:10:23,820 --> 01:10:25,022
YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN?

1740
01:10:25,055 --> 01:10:27,423
THEY'RE LIKE,
"OH, I NEED TO DRILL A HOLE.

1741
01:10:27,457 --> 01:10:29,727
HOPE I BROUGHT MY OVIPOSITOR."

1742
01:10:29,760 --> 01:10:32,028
BUT FEMALE LOCUSTS
HAVE A SHORT OVIPOSITOR,

1743
01:10:32,062 --> 01:10:33,063
SO THEY'RE MORE LIKE,

1744
01:10:33,097 --> 01:10:36,900
"OH, NO, MY OVIPOSITORS
ARE SO SMALL."

1745
01:10:36,933 --> 01:10:39,035
WHAT ELSE CAN I TELL YOU
ABOUT MYSELF?

1746
01:10:39,068 --> 01:10:40,303
OH, LONG-HORNED GRASSHOPPERS--

1747
01:10:40,337 --> 01:10:41,672
ARE THEY SOMETHING OR WHAT?

1748
01:10:41,705 --> 01:10:43,640
YOU KNOW, THEY COME
FROM THE FAMILY TETTIGONIIDAE.

1749
01:10:43,673 --> 01:10:45,908
AM I RIGHT?
LADIES, BACK ME UP ON THIS ONE.

1750
01:10:45,942 --> 01:10:47,543
NOW, YOU SEE, LOCUSTS,

1751
01:10:47,577 --> 01:10:49,012
THEY'RE DIFFERENT
FROM THE TETTIGONIIDAE,

1752
01:10:49,045 --> 01:10:51,548
ESPECIALLY THOSE
ROCKY MOUNTAIN LOCUSTS.

1753
01:10:51,582 --> 01:10:54,352
THEY'RE KNOWN
AS MELANOPLUS SPRETUS.

1754
01:10:54,385 --> 01:10:56,420
THANK YOU.
THANK YOU VERY MUCH,
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN.

1755
01:10:56,453 --> 01:10:57,955
TIP YOUR WAITRESSES.
GOOD NIGHT.

1756
01:10:57,988 --> 01:10:59,523
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.
THANK YOU.

1757
01:10:59,557 --> 01:11:01,692
WELL, TOM, THAT--

1758
01:11:01,725 --> 01:11:02,893
THAT REALLY, REALLY--

1759
01:11:02,927 --> 01:11:04,160
SUCKED. SUCKED.

1760
01:11:04,193 --> 01:11:05,428
NO, IT WAS VERY GOOD.

1761
01:11:05,462 --> 01:11:07,063
IT WAS INFORMATIVE, TOO.

1762
01:11:07,097 --> 01:11:09,333
GEE, THANKS.
I WAS THINKING OF DOING IT ON
THE TONIGHT SHOW.

1763
01:11:09,367 --> 01:11:11,268
OH, TOM, YOU WERE GOOD,

1764
01:11:11,302 --> 01:11:12,837
BUT YOU'VE GOT TO BE
REALLY, REALLY GOOD

1765
01:11:12,870 --> 01:11:14,037
TO BE ON THE TONIGHT SHOW.

1766
01:11:14,070 --> 01:11:15,805
HOW ABOUT DAVID LETTERMAN,
THEN?

1767
01:11:15,838 --> 01:11:17,975
THEY DON'T JUST LET ANYBODY
ON LETTERMAN.

1768
01:11:18,008 --> 01:11:19,377
HOW ABOUT CHEVY CHASE?

1769
01:11:19,410 --> 01:11:21,312
HEY, THERE YOU GO.
SEND HIM A TAPE.

1770
01:11:21,345 --> 01:11:22,913
I THINK YOU'VE GOT
A REAL SHOT AT IT.

1771
01:11:22,947 --> 01:11:24,482
- WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK.
- THANK YOU.

1772
01:11:32,588 --> 01:11:36,227
VERY GOOD.
VERY BYRON ALLEN.

1773
01:11:36,260 --> 01:11:39,095
SO ARE YOU IN LOVE
WITH ME YET?

1774
01:11:40,797 --> 01:11:42,632
I HAVE MY RIGHTS.
I HAVE MY RIGHTS.

1775
01:11:45,702 --> 01:11:48,972
WELL, I'VE JUST COME TO SEE
WHAT YOU'VE DONE
WITH ALL THE GRANT MONEY.

1776
01:11:49,005 --> 01:11:50,073
OH, MY GOD!

1777
01:11:50,107 --> 01:11:51,408
WAINWRIGHT,
YOU'VE HAD YOUR CHANCE.

1778
01:11:51,442 --> 01:11:53,243
NOW IT'S THE AIR FORCE'S TURN.

1779
01:11:53,277 --> 01:11:55,678
GOD, THE STRESS
AND THE BOMB...

1780
01:11:55,712 --> 01:11:57,313
HELLO.

1781
01:11:57,347 --> 01:12:01,818
OPERATOR. OPERATOR,
THIS IS A TOP-PRIORITY CALL.

1782
01:12:01,852 --> 01:12:03,920
GET ME GENERAL WAGNER
AT THE AIR BASE.

1783
01:12:03,953 --> 01:12:05,255
YOU HEAR ME, GRAVES?

1784
01:12:05,288 --> 01:12:06,257
YOU'RE NOT GETTING
ANYTHING OUT OF ME.

1785
01:12:06,290 --> 01:12:09,058
NOTHING.

1786
01:12:09,092 --> 01:12:10,627
[MUFFLED]
ONE MOMENT.

1787
01:12:10,660 --> 01:12:12,662
♪♪ [IMITATING MUZAK]

1788
01:12:16,032 --> 01:12:17,667
I'M GETTING
THE PINA COLADA SONG.

1789
01:12:17,700 --> 01:12:18,968
LOOK, GENERAL,

1790
01:12:19,002 --> 01:12:20,470
THE LOCUSTS OUTSIDE
WILL STAY PUT

1791
01:12:20,503 --> 01:12:22,072
UNTIL THE TEMPERATURE REACHES
68 DEGREES.

1792
01:12:22,105 --> 01:12:24,408
THAT'S ABOUT AN HOUR
AND A HALF FROM NOW.

1793
01:12:24,442 --> 01:12:27,410
OH, THIS PHONE
IS SMOOTH, SLEEK--

1794
01:12:27,443 --> 01:12:28,812
HELLO.

1795
01:12:28,845 --> 01:12:32,648
WAGNER, CORRIDOR'S
BEEN EVACUATED.

1796
01:12:32,682 --> 01:12:35,085
UNLESS YOU RECEIVE INSTRUCTIONS
TO THE CONTRARY,

1797
01:12:35,118 --> 01:12:37,353
BY 06:16, THAT IS...

1798
01:12:37,387 --> 01:12:38,722
OH, CALL IT 8:00.

1799
01:12:38,755 --> 01:12:41,358
- THAT'S 90 MINUTES FROM NOW...
- THAT GOOD FOR YOU?

1800
01:12:41,392 --> 01:12:42,960
...YOU WILL ORDER
YOUR B52 CREW

1801
01:12:42,993 --> 01:12:44,862
TO DELIVER THE BOMB
ON THE DESIGNATED TARGET.

1802
01:12:44,895 --> 01:12:46,563
START WITH THE SHEDD AQUARIUM.

1803
01:12:46,597 --> 01:12:49,032
REPEAT THE INSTRUCTIONS
BACK TO ME.

1804
01:12:49,065 --> 01:12:50,467
YES, I LOVE YOU, TOO.

1805
01:12:50,500 --> 01:12:52,535
CORRECT.

1806
01:12:52,568 --> 01:12:54,805
WILL YOU STOP QUESTIONING
THE GRASSHOPPER?

1807
01:12:54,838 --> 01:12:56,640
THERE'S NO TIME TO FOOL
WITH THAT NOW.

1808
01:12:56,673 --> 01:12:58,975
MAJOR, GET A DETAIL OF MEN UP
HERE TO MOVE THIS STUFF.

1809
01:12:59,008 --> 01:13:00,577
HE'S GOT AN HOURGLASS SHAPE.

1810
01:13:00,610 --> 01:13:03,647
BRING SOME EXTRA GRENADES.
THERE'S SOME IN MY STAFF CAR.

1811
01:13:03,680 --> 01:13:04,948
THERE'S A NEW LAB SET UP
FOR YOU

1812
01:13:04,982 --> 01:13:06,583
AT MY NEW HQ
OUTSIDE THE CITY.

1813
01:13:06,617 --> 01:13:07,750
I CAN'T MOVE NOW.

1814
01:13:07,783 --> 01:13:08,918
YOU CAN'T STAY HERE,

1815
01:13:08,952 --> 01:13:10,953
NOT WITH AN ATOM BOMB
HANGING OVER YOUR HEAD.

1816
01:13:10,987 --> 01:13:12,055
DON'T HAVE ANY CHOICE.

1817
01:13:12,088 --> 01:13:13,423
I'M PETER GRAVES.

1818
01:13:13,457 --> 01:13:14,858
UP TILL NOW WE'VE BEEN USING
A FILTERED SIGNAL,

1819
01:13:14,892 --> 01:13:15,958
AND IT HASN'T WORKED,

1820
01:13:15,992 --> 01:13:17,127
BUT IT'S JUST POSSIBLE

1821
01:13:17,160 --> 01:13:18,895
THAT THE HEARING APPARATUS
OF THE LOCUST

1822
01:13:18,928 --> 01:13:20,463
CAN DETECT
HARMONIC FREQUENCIES

1823
01:13:20,497 --> 01:13:21,532
ABOVE THE HUMAN RANGE.

1824
01:13:21,565 --> 01:13:22,698
TO TEST THESE FREQUENCIES,

1825
01:13:22,732 --> 01:13:24,133
I NEED EVERY MINUTE
THAT'S LEFT.

1826
01:13:24,167 --> 01:13:26,603
IF YOU'LL JUST GIVE ME ONE MAN
TO REPLACE MISS AIMES.

1827
01:13:26,637 --> 01:13:28,272
I'M STAYING.

1828
01:13:28,305 --> 01:13:31,007
LOOK, THIS IS NO TIME TO BE
WORRYING ABOUT A BIG STORY.

1829
01:13:31,040 --> 01:13:32,175
I'M NOT WORRIED ABOUT A STORY.

1830
01:13:32,208 --> 01:13:33,477
LOOK, I JUST WANNA DROP
MY A BOMBS.

1831
01:13:33,510 --> 01:13:35,978
WILL YOU PLEASE LEAVE
BEFORE IT'S TOO LATE?

1832
01:13:36,012 --> 01:13:37,213
NO.

1833
01:13:37,247 --> 01:13:39,348
MAJOR, YOU AND A DETAIL
OF TWO MEN

1834
01:13:39,382 --> 01:13:41,485
WILL REMAIN HERE
WITH MR. WAINWRIGHT.

1835
01:13:41,518 --> 01:13:44,220
I WILL STATION MEN
AT THREE OBSERVATION POSTS--

1836
01:13:44,253 --> 01:13:46,022
ONE IN THE SUBURBS,

1837
01:13:46,055 --> 01:13:47,257
ONE NEAR THE ART INSTITUTE,

1838
01:13:47,290 --> 01:13:49,192
AND ONE ON TOP
OF THE DOWNTOWN HOTEL.

1839
01:13:49,225 --> 01:13:50,393
ONE ON TOP OF ME.

1840
01:13:50,427 --> 01:13:52,897
ALSO A HELICOPTER
WILL SPOT FROM ABOVE.

1841
01:13:52,930 --> 01:13:54,397
THERE WILL BE A GETAWAY CAR

1842
01:13:54,430 --> 01:13:56,600
PARKED DOWNSTAIRS
AT THE MAIN ENTRANCE.

1843
01:13:56,633 --> 01:13:58,068
I SUGGEST YOU USE IT BY...

1844
01:13:58,102 --> 01:13:59,202
08:00, I GUESS.

1845
01:13:59,235 --> 01:14:01,372
BY 5:45 AT THE VERY LATEST.

1846
01:14:01,405 --> 01:14:02,873
IF YOU ARE SUCCESSFUL,

1847
01:14:02,907 --> 01:14:04,742
CONTACT ME AT ONCE

1848
01:14:04,775 --> 01:14:07,510
SO I CAN STOP THE BOMB.

1849
01:14:08,878 --> 01:14:11,148
JUST A LITTLE BOWL OF WHEAT,
PLEASE.

1850
01:14:12,482 --> 01:14:14,585
IT'S 05, UM...

1851
01:14:16,253 --> 01:14:17,287
[IMITATING RADIO ANNOUNCER]
WELL, GOOD MORNING.

1852
01:14:17,320 --> 01:14:18,388
YOU'VE GOT THE LOOP HERE.

1853
01:14:18,422 --> 01:14:19,890
IT'S GOING TO BE
A NICE DAY TODAY.

1854
01:14:19,923 --> 01:14:22,058
WE'RE GOING TO GET BOMBED.
YOU PROBABLY HEARD ABOUT THAT.

1855
01:14:22,092 --> 01:14:24,928
THEY'RE SCRAPING
THE GRILLS AT THE BILLY GOAT
THIS VERY MOMENT.

1856
01:14:24,962 --> 01:14:26,062
MM.

1857
01:14:28,398 --> 01:14:29,767
I'M A BROKE GRASSHOPPER.

1858
01:14:29,800 --> 01:14:30,833
THAT'S ALL I AM, HONEST.

1859
01:14:30,867 --> 01:14:33,870
[WHIRRING]

1860
01:14:33,903 --> 01:14:35,105
SOUNDS LIKE "SWEET LORRAINE."

1861
01:14:35,138 --> 01:14:37,207
DO I REALLY HAVE TO STAY HERE
FOR THIS?

1862
01:14:40,877 --> 01:14:43,580
SO WHERE'S THE RAZZMATAZZ?
I DON'T SEE IT.

1863
01:14:43,613 --> 01:14:45,115
HM. NOPE.

1864
01:14:46,317 --> 01:14:47,717
GINO'S?

1865
01:14:47,750 --> 01:14:49,953
I'VE GOT TO HAVE
THOSE GLENGARRY LEADS.

1866
01:14:49,987 --> 01:14:52,622
HAVE YOU EVER ASSOCIATED
WITH CRICKETS?

1867
01:14:52,655 --> 01:14:54,390
HAVE YOU EVER TAKEN PART
IN A PLAGUE?

1868
01:14:54,423 --> 01:14:57,027
HAVE YOU EATEN GRASS
IN EXCESS OF $1 MILLION?

1869
01:14:59,062 --> 01:15:01,332
DAMN TANDY EQUIPMENT.

1870
01:15:07,670 --> 01:15:09,607
FOLKS, AS FOR TRAFFIC TODAY,

1871
01:15:09,640 --> 01:15:10,707
THERE'S NONE.

1872
01:15:10,740 --> 01:15:12,108
CAN'T EXPLAIN IT.

1873
01:15:12,142 --> 01:15:13,843
WHATTA YA KNOW?

1874
01:15:15,278 --> 01:15:17,413
BOY, THE CONVENTION BUSINESS

1875
01:15:17,447 --> 01:15:18,948
JUST WENT STRAIGHT DOWN HILL,
DIDN'T IT?

1876
01:15:18,982 --> 01:15:22,085
WOW.

1877
01:15:22,118 --> 01:15:23,220
LOOK AT THAT.

1878
01:15:24,320 --> 01:15:25,522
[WHIRRING]

1879
01:15:27,723 --> 01:15:29,358
WHAT THE SAM HILL IS HE DOING?

1880
01:15:31,160 --> 01:15:33,097
I'M NOT GOING TO ADMIT
MY FAILURE.

1881
01:15:35,665 --> 01:15:38,035
IT'S SHAPING UP TO BE
A PRETTY NICE DAY.

1882
01:15:38,068 --> 01:15:39,637
MAYBE GO GET SOME CHRISTMAS
SHOPPING DONE.

1883
01:15:39,670 --> 01:15:41,003
NOT A LOT OF COMPETITION.

1884
01:15:41,037 --> 01:15:42,973
[WHIRRING CONTINUES]

1885
01:15:43,007 --> 01:15:45,942
IT'S A LONG
KATHLEEN BATTLE ARIA.

1886
01:15:45,975 --> 01:15:47,177
MAYBE HE'S INNOCENT.

1887
01:15:47,210 --> 01:15:50,247
MAYBE THEY GOT
THE WRONG HOPPER.

1888
01:15:50,280 --> 01:15:52,382
DOH, I FORGOT TO TURN
THIS THING ON.

1889
01:15:54,685 --> 01:15:56,218
[IMITATES WHIRRING]

1890
01:15:59,388 --> 01:16:01,758
ED, LOOK AT THIS.

1891
01:16:01,792 --> 01:16:03,527
HE'S GOT HIGH BLOOD PRESSURE.

1892
01:16:03,560 --> 01:16:05,928
I THINK YOU'VE GOT IT.

1893
01:16:05,962 --> 01:16:09,032
THIS IS WHAT IT SOUNDS LIKE
WHEN GRASSHOPPERS CRY.

1894
01:16:09,065 --> 01:16:11,568
BY GEORGE, HIGGINS,
I THINK WE'VE GOT IT.

1895
01:16:13,070 --> 01:16:15,172
[MISS AIMES SCREAMS]

1896
01:16:15,205 --> 01:16:16,172
WHOA. HM.

1897
01:16:18,942 --> 01:16:20,243
OH, NO, NOT THE FACE.

1898
01:16:20,277 --> 01:16:22,745
YOU TOOK OUT
A COUPLE THOUSAND EYES.

1899
01:16:22,778 --> 01:16:25,582
PETE! PETE!
SHORT, CONTROLLED BURSTS!

1900
01:16:27,550 --> 01:16:31,120
HEY, I'VE GOT IT.
WE COULD JUST SHOOT THEM.

1901
01:16:31,153 --> 01:16:32,622
OH, WELL, ACCEPTABLE LOSSES.

1902
01:16:37,960 --> 01:16:41,732
I HAD TO SHOOT HIM.

1903
01:16:41,765 --> 01:16:45,768
WELL, LET'S CHOCOLATE DIP
THAT GRASSHOPPER.

1904
01:16:45,802 --> 01:16:47,370
AND GET THAT THING OUT OF HERE.

1905
01:16:47,403 --> 01:16:49,172
BUG FELL AND HIT HIS HEAD
AGAINST THE BARS

1906
01:16:49,205 --> 01:16:51,708
IF ANYONE ASKS, RIGHT?

1907
01:16:51,742 --> 01:16:52,908
BACK AT IT.

1908
01:16:52,942 --> 01:16:54,477
I WANT TO POLYGRAPH
THE DOORKNOB NOW.

1909
01:16:54,510 --> 01:16:56,145
EMERGENCY LAB TO CHICAGO GHQ.

1910
01:16:56,178 --> 01:16:59,683
EMERGENCY LAB TO CHICAGO GHQ.
COME IN, GENERAL.
ARE YOU THERE?

1911
01:16:59,717 --> 01:17:01,050
NOW, LISTEN TO ME, WAINWRIGHT.

1912
01:17:01,083 --> 01:17:02,152
WE FOUND IT, GENERAL.

1913
01:17:02,185 --> 01:17:03,653
WE FOUND THE FREQUENCY.

1914
01:17:03,687 --> 01:17:06,790
GOOD. NOW STAND BY.

1915
01:17:06,823 --> 01:17:08,625
I'VE GOT TO STOP THAT A BOMB.

1916
01:17:08,658 --> 01:17:10,727
I'LL GET RIGHT BACK TO YOU.

1917
01:17:10,760 --> 01:17:14,765
CHICAGO GHQ TO DOUBLE B.
CHICAGO GHQ TO DOUBLE B.

1918
01:17:17,367 --> 01:17:19,235
CHICAGO GHQ TO DOUBLE B.

1919
01:17:19,268 --> 01:17:20,737
THEY'RE NOT GOING TO LET US
DROP THE BOMB.

1920
01:17:20,770 --> 01:17:22,338
DON'T ANSWER IT.

1921
01:17:22,372 --> 01:17:25,608
THIS IS DOUBLE B.
COME IN, CHICAGO GHQ.
OVER.

1922
01:17:25,642 --> 01:17:27,543
HANSON HERE.

1923
01:17:27,577 --> 01:17:29,212
YOUR MISSION IS CANCELLED.

1924
01:17:29,245 --> 01:17:31,648
- REAL SORRY, BOYS.
- RETURN TO YOUR BASE.

1925
01:17:31,682 --> 01:17:34,852
REPEAT THE MESSAGE.
OVER.

1926
01:17:34,885 --> 01:17:36,185
IT'S THE COMMIES.

1927
01:17:36,218 --> 01:17:37,820
MISSION CANCELLED.
RETURN TO BASE.

1928
01:17:37,853 --> 01:17:39,055
- OVER.
- REPEAT IT AGAIN.

1929
01:17:39,088 --> 01:17:41,290
CHICAGO GHQ TO EMERGENCY LAB.

1930
01:17:41,323 --> 01:17:43,127
RIGHT HERE.

1931
01:17:43,160 --> 01:17:45,762
THE SHOW IS YOURS, WAINWRIGHT.

1932
01:17:45,795 --> 01:17:48,398
ALL RIGHT, GET THAT EQUIPMENT
ON THE LAKE IN A BOAT,

1933
01:17:48,432 --> 01:17:50,300
AND I'LL BE YOUR PIED PIPER.

1934
01:17:50,333 --> 01:17:53,103
GET ME MY LITTLE GREEN SHOES
WITH THE CURLY TOES.

1935
01:17:53,137 --> 01:17:56,407
OH, I LOVE MEN WHO USE
FAIRYTALE IMAGERY.

1936
01:18:01,110 --> 01:18:06,517
♪♪ [HUMS
McHALE'S NAVY THEME]

1937
01:18:06,550 --> 01:18:09,218
HE JUST POLYGRAPHED A SANDWICH.
HE NEEDS REAL HELP.

1938
01:18:09,252 --> 01:18:11,153
I STILL DON'T UNDERSTAND.

1939
01:18:11,187 --> 01:18:13,457
WHY DIDN'T YOU PUT
THE OSCILLATOR IN THE BOAT
IN THE FIRST PLACE

1940
01:18:13,490 --> 01:18:14,825
TO SEND OUT THE CALL?

1941
01:18:14,858 --> 01:18:16,392
WHY TRACK THEM HERE?

1942
01:18:16,425 --> 01:18:18,595
BECAUSE WE'D
NEVER GET THEM ALL.

1943
01:18:18,628 --> 01:18:19,662
HERE, LOOK.

1944
01:18:19,695 --> 01:18:20,863
DILBERT'S A SCREAM TODAY.

1945
01:18:20,897 --> 01:18:22,465
HERE WE ARE
IN DOWNTOWN CHICAGO,

1946
01:18:22,498 --> 01:18:23,800
NEAR THE LAKE.

1947
01:18:23,833 --> 01:18:25,868
AND THE LOCUSTS ARE SCATTERED
ALL THROUGH THE SUBURBS

1948
01:18:25,902 --> 01:18:27,470
AND ON THE SOUTH SIDE.

1949
01:18:27,503 --> 01:18:29,372
WE'LL SEND OUT THE CALL
FROM HERE.

1950
01:18:29,405 --> 01:18:31,708
YES, BUT THAT'S GOING
TO ATTRACT THEM TO US,
NOT INTO THE WATER.

1951
01:18:31,742 --> 01:18:33,510
- SHUT UP.
- FIRST OF ALL, IT'S IMPERATIVE

1952
01:18:33,543 --> 01:18:35,612
THAT EVERY LAST ONE OF
THE LOCUSTS HEAR THE CALL.

1953
01:18:35,645 --> 01:18:36,747
IN ORDER TO DO THAT,

1954
01:18:36,780 --> 01:18:38,382
WE'VE GOT TO GET
OUR AMPLIFIER SPEAKER

1955
01:18:38,415 --> 01:18:39,648
AT THE HIGHEST POSSIBLE POINT

1956
01:18:39,682 --> 01:18:41,083
TO GET MAXIMUM RANGE.

1957
01:18:41,117 --> 01:18:43,120
NOW, WE'VE GOT OURS
ON THE ROOF OF THIS BUILDING,

1958
01:18:43,153 --> 01:18:45,122
WHICH IS ONE OF THE TALLEST
IN CHICAGO.

1959
01:18:45,155 --> 01:18:46,623
ONCE WE GET THEM HERE,

1960
01:18:46,657 --> 01:18:48,558
I SEE. THEN THE BOAT
WILL TAKE OVER.

1961
01:18:48,592 --> 01:18:51,695
EXACTLY. ONCE WE HAVE THEM
IN THE HEART OF THE LOOP,
NEAR OUR LOCATION,

1962
01:18:51,728 --> 01:18:54,363
THEY'LL BE WITHIN RANGE
OF THE AMPLIFIER ON THE BOAT.

1963
01:18:54,397 --> 01:18:57,833
NOW, WE'LL THEN RADIO OUR
OSCILLATOR SIGNAL
OUT TO THE BOAT,

1964
01:18:57,867 --> 01:19:01,303
AND THEY IN TURN
WILL REBROADCAST IT
OVER THEIR AMPLIFIER,

1965
01:19:01,337 --> 01:19:03,173
DIRECTING THE LOCUSTS TO THEM

1966
01:19:03,207 --> 01:19:06,008
AND INTO THE LAKE.

1967
01:19:06,042 --> 01:19:07,310
WE HOPE.

1968
01:19:07,343 --> 01:19:10,580
SEE, THAT'S WHAT YOU DO SO WELL.
YOU CUT ME DOWN.

1969
01:19:10,613 --> 01:19:13,350
WILL YOU CHECK AND SEE
ABOUT THE TEMPERATURE?

1970
01:19:13,383 --> 01:19:15,518
I KNOW A SCIENTIST
THAT NEEDS A BACK RUB.

1971
01:19:15,552 --> 01:19:16,987
HOW CAN WE BE SURE, SURE?

1972
01:19:17,020 --> 01:19:18,422
HM? WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

1973
01:19:18,455 --> 01:19:20,457
HOW CAN YOU KNOW
THAT WE'LL GET THEM ALL?

1974
01:19:20,490 --> 01:19:24,360
THAT'S WHERE OUR OBSERVATION
POSTS AND THE HELICOPTER
COME IN.

1975
01:19:24,393 --> 01:19:26,497
FROM THEIR REPORTS
WE'LL KNOW THE EXACT LOCATION

1976
01:19:26,530 --> 01:19:28,598
OF THE LOCUSTS AT ALL TIMES

1977
01:19:28,632 --> 01:19:30,200
AND IF IT'S WORKING.

1978
01:19:31,500 --> 01:19:32,935
IT'S 70 DEGREES, ED.

1979
01:19:32,968 --> 01:19:34,037
COOLER NEAR THE LAKE.

1980
01:19:34,070 --> 01:19:35,838
THEY'RE PROBABLY
STARTING TO MOVE.

1981
01:19:35,872 --> 01:19:38,608
EMERGENCY LAB
TO ALL OBSERVATION POSTS.

1982
01:19:38,642 --> 01:19:43,180
EMERGENCY LAB TO ALL
OBSERVATION POSTS, REPORT IN.

1983
01:19:43,213 --> 01:19:44,948
I'M HIDING FROM A LION.

1984
01:19:44,982 --> 01:19:46,482
...TO EMERGENCY LAB, OVER.

1985
01:19:46,515 --> 01:19:47,917
IT'S GOT THESE WOMEN
SCARED STIFF.

1986
01:19:47,950 --> 01:19:49,252
WHAT IS YOUR LOCATION?
OVER.

1987
01:19:49,285 --> 01:19:50,720
I AM SITUATED IN A STORE

1988
01:19:50,753 --> 01:19:52,055
ACROSS FROM THE ART INSTITUTE

1989
01:19:52,088 --> 01:19:53,055
ON MICHIGAN BOULEVARD.

1990
01:19:53,088 --> 01:19:54,790
OLGA BRAS ARE ON SALE.

1991
01:19:54,823 --> 01:19:56,893
NOTHING IN SIGHT.
OUT.

1992
01:19:56,927 --> 01:20:00,030
OBSERVATION POST NUMBER THREE
TO EMERGENCY LAB.

1993
01:20:00,063 --> 01:20:01,832
I'M ON THE ROOF
OF THE DRAYTON HOTEL.

1994
01:20:01,865 --> 01:20:03,098
I SEE
A HUGE SWIRLY CROWN ROAST.

1995
01:20:03,132 --> 01:20:04,767
I DON'T SEE ANY GRASSHOPPERS
IN THIS AREA.

1996
01:20:04,800 --> 01:20:06,637
BUT THE SOUTH SIDE'S
GETTING SOME ACTION.

1997
01:20:06,670 --> 01:20:08,103
- WOW.
- OUT.

1998
01:20:16,412 --> 01:20:18,615
EMERGENCY LAB TO OBSERVATION
POST ONE.

1999
01:20:18,648 --> 01:20:21,350
EMERGENCY LAB
TO OBSERVATION POST ONE.

2000
01:20:21,383 --> 01:20:23,152
YOU DID NOT REPORT IN.

2001
01:20:23,185 --> 01:20:24,620
WHAT'S YOUR LOCATION...

2002
01:20:24,653 --> 01:20:25,922
NOTHING GOING ON HERE.

2003
01:20:25,955 --> 01:20:27,523
OBSERVATION POST NUMBER ONE.

2004
01:20:27,557 --> 01:20:29,358
I'M RIGHT
IN THE MIDDLE OF THEM.

2005
01:20:29,392 --> 01:20:32,662
I'M JUST SOUTH OF 73rd
AND SOUTH SHORE DRIVE.
OUT.

2006
01:20:32,695 --> 01:20:35,032
AND JIMMY FERLICK'S MOM SAYS
I CAN STAY FOR DINNER.

2007
01:20:35,065 --> 01:20:37,733
EMERGENCY LAB TO HELICOPTER.
OVER.

2008
01:20:37,767 --> 01:20:41,972
THE NAME'S JEFFREY.
I HAPPEN TO BE IN A HELICOPTER.

2009
01:20:42,005 --> 01:20:44,840
THE LOCUSTS ARE ACTIVE
ON THE SOUTH SIDE OF CHICAGO.

2010
01:20:44,873 --> 01:20:47,677
AS YET THERE ARE NONE
IN THE DOWNTOWN AREA.
OUT.

2011
01:20:47,710 --> 01:20:51,013
CAN YOU READ ME,
EMERGENCY LAB?
OVER.

2012
01:20:51,047 --> 01:20:52,482
YES, WE CAN READ YOU FINE,
GENERAL.

2013
01:20:52,515 --> 01:20:54,317
ARE YOU ALL SET?
OVER.

2014
01:20:54,350 --> 01:20:57,220
WE'RE NOT QUITE READY YET.

2015
01:20:57,253 --> 01:20:59,022
DUMMY HERE CAN'T FIX
THE RADIO.

2016
01:20:59,055 --> 01:21:00,190
A FEW MORE MINUTES.

2017
01:21:00,223 --> 01:21:01,992
OVER.

2018
01:21:02,025 --> 01:21:03,827
I THINK WE BETTER START NOW,
GENERAL.

2019
01:21:03,860 --> 01:21:05,328
IF THEY SHOULD CHANGE
THEIR DIRECTION

2020
01:21:05,362 --> 01:21:06,730
AND START MOVING AWAY
FROM CHICAGO,

2021
01:21:06,763 --> 01:21:09,065
WE MAY NOT GET THEM ALL.
OVER.

2022
01:21:09,098 --> 01:21:10,400
I DON'T LIKE YOUR STARTING

2023
01:21:10,433 --> 01:21:11,802
UNTIL WE'RE COMPLETELY READY.

2024
01:21:11,835 --> 01:21:13,903
THIS BOAT HAS TO DRAW THEM
AWAY FROM YOU

2025
01:21:13,937 --> 01:21:15,338
AT A SPLIT SECOND'S NOTICE.

2026
01:21:15,372 --> 01:21:16,572
UH, RIGHTY TIGHTY.

2027
01:21:16,605 --> 01:21:17,607
OVER.

2028
01:21:17,640 --> 01:21:19,108
I'D LIKE TO START, SIR.

2029
01:21:21,077 --> 01:21:23,847
- THEN GO AHEAD.
- BABY.

2030
01:21:23,880 --> 01:21:25,915
I SAY GO, THAT GUY JUMPS.

2031
01:21:28,685 --> 01:21:30,553
I'M GOING TO POLYGRAPH MY TIE.

2032
01:21:30,587 --> 01:21:31,988
YES, SIR?

2033
01:21:32,022 --> 01:21:33,990
IS THAT THE WIRE THAT LEADS
TO THE SPEAKER ON THE ROOF?

2034
01:21:34,023 --> 01:21:35,258
SURE.

2035
01:21:35,292 --> 01:21:38,428
PLUG IT INTO THE AMPLIFIER,
WILL YOU?

2036
01:21:38,462 --> 01:21:39,428
[IMITATES ELECTRICAL BUZZING]

2037
01:21:39,462 --> 01:21:40,530
[IMITATES SCREAM]

2038
01:21:40,563 --> 01:21:42,565
[AMPLIFIER WHIRRING]

2039
01:21:42,598 --> 01:21:44,867
[LOUDER WHIRRING]

2040
01:21:44,900 --> 01:21:48,705
ALL RIGHT, PLAYING TULL
OUT THE WINDOW, MAN. WHOO!

2041
01:21:48,738 --> 01:21:52,975
WHEN BRIAN ENO RULED CHICAGO.

2042
01:21:53,008 --> 01:21:54,643
I DON'T REMEMBER THAT.

2043
01:21:54,677 --> 01:21:56,612
POST NUMBER ONE
TO EMERGENCY LAB,

2044
01:21:56,645 --> 01:21:58,113
THE LOCUSTS ARE LEAVING
THIS SECTION.

2045
01:21:58,147 --> 01:21:59,782
THEY'RE HEADING
TOWARD CHICAGO'S DOWNTOWN.

2046
01:21:59,815 --> 01:22:01,550
IF THEY WANTED TO REV UP
THE GRASSHOPPERS,

2047
01:22:01,583 --> 01:22:02,852
THEY JUST SHOULD'VE PLAYED
SOME MARVIN GAYE.

2048
01:22:02,885 --> 01:22:04,587
HELICOPTER TO EMERGENCY LAB...

2049
01:22:04,620 --> 01:22:06,222
I'M STILL PAUL FREES.

2050
01:22:06,255 --> 01:22:07,823
THEY'RE MOVING
ON THE DOWNTOWN AREA.

2051
01:22:07,857 --> 01:22:10,627
THEY ARE RADICALLY ALTERING
THEIR SIZE

2052
01:22:10,660 --> 01:22:12,395
DEPENDING ON YOUR PERSPECTIVE.

2053
01:22:15,032 --> 01:22:17,667
SO DOES THIS BUS GO
ALL THE WAY TO...

2054
01:22:17,700 --> 01:22:20,037
JUST GET ON THE BUS.

2055
01:22:23,373 --> 01:22:25,242
WE'VE GOT TO GET ORGANIZED.

2056
01:22:25,275 --> 01:22:29,412
HOPPY.

2057
01:22:29,445 --> 01:22:31,748
OBSERVATION POST NUMBER THREE
TO EMERGENCY LAB.

2058
01:22:31,782 --> 01:22:34,450
THE LOCUSTS ARE EVERYWHERE.

2059
01:22:34,483 --> 01:22:36,418
YEP, OVER THERE, TOO.
EVERYWHERE PRETTY MUCH.

2060
01:22:36,452 --> 01:22:38,320
THEY'RE MOVING
TOWARDS YOUR LOCATION.

2061
01:22:38,353 --> 01:22:41,557
I REPEAT. THE LOCUSTS ARE MOVING
TOWARDS THE EMERGENCY LAB.

2062
01:22:41,590 --> 01:22:45,128
THEY'VE GOTTEN HOLD
OF FIRE ARMS AND THEY'RE DRUNK.

2063
01:22:45,162 --> 01:22:46,595
MICHIGAN BOULEVARD
IS FILLED WITH THEM.

2064
01:22:46,628 --> 01:22:47,630
THEY'RE EVERYWHERE!

2065
01:22:47,663 --> 01:22:48,998
THEY'RE ON A SHOPPING RAMPAGE!

2066
01:22:49,032 --> 01:22:51,768
EMERGENCY LAB TO BOAT.
EMERGENCY LAB TO BOAT.

2067
01:22:51,802 --> 01:22:53,135
IT'S WORKING, GENERAL.
IT'S WORKING.

2068
01:22:53,168 --> 01:22:54,470
YOU NEVER TAKE ME ANYWHERE.

2069
01:22:54,503 --> 01:22:55,772
I HEARD THE REPORTS.

2070
01:23:03,513 --> 01:23:06,348
WOW, WOULD YOU LOOK AT THAT?
THEY DYED THE RIVER GREEN.

2071
01:23:06,382 --> 01:23:09,385
THAT DICK DALEY.

2072
01:23:09,418 --> 01:23:11,788
WE'RE IN THE FAMOUS LOOP NOW,
HARRY.

2073
01:23:11,822 --> 01:23:15,258
WONDER WHY THEY CALL IT THAT.

2074
01:23:15,292 --> 01:23:17,793
[CHUCKLES]
WACKER.

2075
01:23:17,827 --> 01:23:19,428
- WACKER.
- WACKER.

2076
01:23:22,532 --> 01:23:24,533
I'M BLOWING THE LIFE.
THIS IS BOGUS.

2077
01:23:29,305 --> 01:23:30,407
YEP.

2078
01:23:30,440 --> 01:23:34,477
I'M RIGHT BEHIND YOU, OKAY?

2079
01:23:35,845 --> 01:23:37,480
[LAUGHING]

2080
01:23:37,513 --> 01:23:38,715
OH, MAN.

2081
01:23:38,748 --> 01:23:41,550
LOOKS GOOD.
EVERYBODY, I THINK WE'RE OKAY.

2082
01:23:41,583 --> 01:23:43,853
PRETTY GOOD SHAPE.
NOTHING TO WORRY ABOUT.

2083
01:23:43,887 --> 01:23:46,588
INTELLIGENCE, SOPHISTICATED
EQUIPMENT. I THINK--
[SCREAMS]

2084
01:23:46,622 --> 01:23:48,992
- [MAN SCREAMING]
- THAT'S WHAT I SAID.

2085
01:23:49,025 --> 01:23:52,928
YOU WANNA TAKE OVER
THAT WATCH POST, HONEY?

2086
01:23:52,962 --> 01:23:56,332
ARE YOU AS TURNED ON AS I AM?

2087
01:23:56,365 --> 01:23:58,868
HERE THEY COME.
THEY'RE COMING DOWN THE STREET.

2088
01:23:58,902 --> 01:24:02,938
GET THE FUNNIEST LOOKS
FROM EVERYONE THEY MEET.

2089
01:24:02,972 --> 01:24:07,110
WHAT DO YOU WANT?

2090
01:24:07,143 --> 01:24:08,712
THEY'RE CLIMBING THE BUILDING.

2091
01:24:08,745 --> 01:24:10,413
AND THEIR FEET ARE DIRTY.

2092
01:24:13,082 --> 01:24:14,650
THAT'S A POSTCARD.

2093
01:24:21,623 --> 01:24:24,093
BOY, WATCH IT.
YOU'RE STEPPING
OFF THE BUILDING THERE.

2094
01:24:31,000 --> 01:24:32,668
[MUTTERS]

2095
01:24:36,172 --> 01:24:37,807
WAINWRIGHT TO BOAT.
WAINWRIGHT TO BOAT.

2096
01:24:37,840 --> 01:24:38,842
COME IN, PLEASE.
COME IN.

2097
01:24:38,875 --> 01:24:40,477
COME IN, WAINWRIGHT.

2098
01:24:40,510 --> 01:24:41,777
HOW SOON ARE YOU READY?

2099
01:24:41,810 --> 01:24:43,713
WE'RE READY AS SOON
AS WE GET CLEARANCE

2100
01:24:43,747 --> 01:24:45,482
FROM OBSERVATION POSTS.

2101
01:24:45,515 --> 01:24:48,250
I'LL CHECK THEM IMMEDIATELY.
OUT.

2102
01:24:48,283 --> 01:24:49,985
YEAH, AS SOON AS MARCONI HERE
IS READY.

2103
01:24:50,018 --> 01:24:51,420
BOAT TO HELICOPTER.

2104
01:24:52,988 --> 01:24:54,157
THEY'RE STILL GOING IN, SIR,

2105
01:24:54,190 --> 01:24:55,525
BUT IT'LL BE A WHILE

2106
01:24:55,558 --> 01:24:57,927
BEFORE THEY ALL REACH
THE DOWNTOWN SECTION.

2107
01:24:57,960 --> 01:25:01,130
WAINWRIGHT,
YOU'LL HAVE TO HOLD OUT
A BIT LONGER.

2108
01:25:01,163 --> 01:25:04,733
ALL THE LOCUSTS HAVEN'T REACHED
THE DOWNTOWN AREA YET.

2109
01:25:04,767 --> 01:25:07,437
EXCUSE ME.
I'M ON THE PHONE HERE.

2110
01:25:07,470 --> 01:25:09,138
ALL RIGHT, WE'LL TRY.

2111
01:25:14,543 --> 01:25:16,312
WANT SOME?
HAH!

2112
01:25:16,345 --> 01:25:18,447
NOT AGAIN.
WHAT A DAY.

2113
01:25:19,515 --> 01:25:21,283
SAFE YOURSELF, TONY!

2114
01:25:23,285 --> 01:25:25,120
TOP OF THE WRIGLEY BUILDING, MA.

2115
01:25:25,153 --> 01:25:26,155
NOT QUITE THE TOP.

2116
01:25:26,188 --> 01:25:28,390
WE CAN'T HOLD OUT MUCH LONGER.

2117
01:25:28,423 --> 01:25:30,393
LOOK, I WANNA TALK.
I WANNA LIVE.

2118
01:25:30,427 --> 01:25:33,530
I WANNA--
[SCREAMS]

2119
01:25:33,563 --> 01:25:35,163
WATCH IT, CAL.

2120
01:25:35,197 --> 01:25:37,133
BOAT TO OBSERVATION POST.

2121
01:25:37,167 --> 01:25:38,968
WELL, WE'RE NOT GOING TO GET
THIS GOING.

2122
01:25:39,002 --> 01:25:39,968
OVER.

2123
01:25:40,002 --> 01:25:41,303
POST NUMBER ONE,

2124
01:25:41,337 --> 01:25:43,640
JIMMY'S MOM SERVING MEATLOAF.

2125
01:25:43,673 --> 01:25:45,475
POST NUMBER TWO.

2126
01:25:45,508 --> 01:25:46,877
ALL CLEAR, SIR.

2127
01:25:46,910 --> 01:25:49,178
HELICOPTER REPORTING.

2128
01:25:49,212 --> 01:25:50,547
ALL CLEAR, SIR.

2129
01:25:53,950 --> 01:25:55,452
THIS GUY'S CRAZY UP THERE.

2130
01:25:56,987 --> 01:25:59,922
OH, THE THIRD TIME.
HOW STUPID AM I?

2131
01:26:01,857 --> 01:26:03,993
THINK ABOUT OUR 10,000 KIDS?

2132
01:26:09,432 --> 01:26:12,068
HEY, I'M JUST GOING
TO THE OBSERVATION DECK.
[SCREAMS]

2133
01:26:12,102 --> 01:26:13,970
BUST MY CHOPS.

2134
01:26:14,003 --> 01:26:15,170
WHENEVER YOU'RE READY, GENERAL.

2135
01:26:15,203 --> 01:26:17,173
THEN LET'S HAVE IT.

2136
01:26:17,207 --> 01:26:19,642
OKAY, GO AHEAD, AUDREY.

2137
01:26:19,675 --> 01:26:21,710
[WHIRRING STOPS]

2138
01:26:21,743 --> 01:26:23,045
THROW THE SWITCH.

2139
01:26:23,078 --> 01:26:25,948
- [LOUD WHIRRING]
- OH, JIMINY, SHUT THAT OFF!

2140
01:26:31,988 --> 01:26:33,255
GEEZ, I'M OUT OF HERE.

2141
01:26:33,288 --> 01:26:35,223
I KNOW WHEN I'M NOT WANTED.
DON'T SHOOT.

2142
01:26:35,257 --> 01:26:37,127
GOOD-BYE. I'M OUT OF HERE.

2143
01:26:39,328 --> 01:26:41,530
YOU GUYS FEEL
AS SILLY AS I DO?

2144
01:26:42,865 --> 01:26:44,900
STREET BEEF.

2145
01:26:44,933 --> 01:26:48,070
GET OFF THE POSTCARD.
THEY'RE GOING TO BLOW
THE POSTCARD.

2146
01:26:48,103 --> 01:26:50,240
- YOU'VE BEEN DISTANT LATELY.
- NOT NOW.

2147
01:26:55,545 --> 01:26:56,980
LET'S SPIT ON THEM.

2148
01:26:59,248 --> 01:27:00,248
HELICOPTER TO BOAT.

2149
01:27:00,282 --> 01:27:01,850
GENERAL, THEY'RE RESPONDING.

2150
01:27:01,883 --> 01:27:02,952
THEY'RE RESPONDING.

2151
01:27:02,985 --> 01:27:04,487
THEY'RE SWARMING
TOWARD THE WATER.

2152
01:27:04,520 --> 01:27:07,423
DON'T LINGER ON THAT SHOT.

2153
01:27:07,457 --> 01:27:08,490
THEY'RE GOING INTO THE WATER.

2154
01:27:08,523 --> 01:27:09,725
IT'S A TRICK.

2155
01:27:09,758 --> 01:27:11,427
IT'S GOTTA BE A TRICK.

2156
01:27:11,460 --> 01:27:14,497
THERE CAN'T BE
THAT MANY LADY GRASSHOPPERS
IN LAKE MICHIGAN.

2157
01:27:18,668 --> 01:27:21,137
WOW, CHICAGO THOUGHT
THE ALEWIVES SMELLED BAD.

2158
01:27:21,170 --> 01:27:22,405
WHOO.

2159
01:27:22,438 --> 01:27:24,140
WELL, LET'S SEE
WHAT THIS BABY CAN DO.

2160
01:27:24,173 --> 01:27:25,240
LET 'ER RIP, PRIVATE.

2161
01:27:25,273 --> 01:27:26,842
HIT IT!

2162
01:27:26,875 --> 01:27:29,645
HEAD FOR SHORE.

2163
01:27:29,678 --> 01:27:31,880
WE'LL, WE'VE JUST SPENT
THE GOOFIEST WEEK

2164
01:27:31,913 --> 01:27:33,382
OF OUR ENTIRE LIVES.

2165
01:27:35,818 --> 01:27:37,453
IT'S GOING TO BE TOUGH
FOR THEM.

2166
01:27:37,487 --> 01:27:39,788
ALL THEY EVER REALLY SHARED
WERE THE GRASSHOPPERS.

2167
01:27:39,822 --> 01:27:41,923
YEAH.

2168
01:27:41,957 --> 01:27:43,425
DIDN'T THIS GUY CAUSE
THE WHOLE THING?

2169
01:27:43,458 --> 01:27:45,795
HE'S GOTTA BE DOING HARD TIME
IN JOLIET RIGHT NOW.

2170
01:27:45,828 --> 01:27:47,263
NO, THE GRASSHOPPERS
ATE JOLIET.

2171
01:27:48,430 --> 01:27:50,433
HEY, SLOW DOWN THERE, ROMEO.

2172
01:27:50,467 --> 01:27:52,835
WHERE'S YOUR OTHER HAND?

2173
01:27:52,868 --> 01:27:58,040
♪ HEY, MR. ARNSTEIN,
HERE I AM! ♪

2174
01:28:14,657 --> 01:28:15,958
HEY, TOM.

2175
01:28:15,992 --> 01:28:17,127
EEEEYEEESSSS?

2176
01:28:17,160 --> 01:28:19,562
IS THIS THE FIRST MOVIE
WITH GRASSHOPPERS?

2177
01:28:19,595 --> 01:28:21,197
YOU KNOW, I THINK IT IS.

2178
01:28:21,230 --> 01:28:24,100
I CAN'T REMEMBER EVER SEEING
A SINGLE GRASSHOPPER.

2179
01:28:24,133 --> 01:28:27,537
AND THEN TODAY,
NOTHING BUT GRASSHOPPERS.
WEIRD.

2180
01:28:27,570 --> 01:28:28,938
NOW, COME ON.

2181
01:28:28,972 --> 01:28:30,407
THERE HAD TO HAVE BEEN ONE
OR TWO GRASSHOPPERS.

2182
01:28:30,440 --> 01:28:31,740
- NOPE.
- NO, SIREE.

2183
01:28:31,773 --> 01:28:33,508
THAT IS WEIRD.
THAT IS WEIRD.

2184
01:28:33,542 --> 01:28:35,812
YOU KNOW, MAYBE WE SHOULD READ
A POSTCARD HERE.

2185
01:28:35,845 --> 01:28:38,882
OKAY, WE'VE GOT THIS ONE
HERE FROM CANTON, AMY HIKAIDA.

2186
01:28:38,915 --> 01:28:41,317
PUT THAT UP ON STILL STORE,
THERE, CAMBOT.

2187
01:28:41,350 --> 01:28:44,487
THEY SAY, AS MEMBERS
OF THE KIM CATTRALL FAN CLUB...

2188
01:28:44,520 --> 01:28:46,555
- CROW.
- KIM CATTRALL.

2189
01:28:46,588 --> 01:28:50,158
WE WONDERED
IF YOU WERE GOING TO VIEW
OLIVER STONE'S WILD PALMS.

2190
01:28:50,192 --> 01:28:51,860
- NO. I DON'T THINK OF IT.
- NO.

2191
01:28:51,893 --> 01:28:53,362
WELL, GOTTA GO.

2192
01:28:53,395 --> 01:28:55,698
THE FATHERS AND FRIENDS
ARE GOING AT IT
IN THE SWIMMING POOL--

2193
01:28:55,732 --> 01:28:57,367
- WOW. WOO-HOO.
- WUH-HO.

2194
01:28:57,400 --> 01:28:59,635
- YOWZA.
- THAT IS SALTY.

2195
01:28:59,668 --> 01:29:02,072
THE GREAT THING
ABOUT THESE POST CARDS
PEOPLE SEND IN, THOUGH,

2196
01:29:02,105 --> 01:29:05,040
THEY DOUBLE
AS GREAT BERT I. GORDON
SPECIAL EFFECTS.

2197
01:29:05,073 --> 01:29:07,777
CHECK THIS OUT.

2198
01:29:07,810 --> 01:29:09,178
OH, NO!
OH, NO!

2199
01:29:09,212 --> 01:29:12,615
GRASSHOPPERS ARE ATTACKING
THE BEACH IN ARUBA.

2200
01:29:12,648 --> 01:29:15,083
[IMITATING SCREAMS]

2201
01:29:15,117 --> 01:29:16,252
[CHUCKLING]

2202
01:29:16,285 --> 01:29:17,953
I GOT ONE.
I GOT ONE HERE.

2203
01:29:17,987 --> 01:29:20,155
THE GRASSHOPPERS-- AAH,
THEY'RE ATTACKING THE BEATLES.

2204
01:29:20,188 --> 01:29:22,023
[IMITATING SCREAMS]

2205
01:29:22,057 --> 01:29:23,492
[LIVERPOOL ACCENT]
DEFEND RINGO AT ALL COSTS.

2206
01:29:23,525 --> 01:29:24,660
OH, THEY'RE ATTACKING ME.

2207
01:29:24,693 --> 01:29:26,895
[LAUGHING]

2208
01:29:26,928 --> 01:29:28,097
OH, LOOK AT THIS.

2209
01:29:28,130 --> 01:29:30,032
OH, GRASSHOPPERS--
THEY DON'T CARE.

2210
01:29:30,065 --> 01:29:33,668
NOW THEY'RE GOING
FOR THE VILLAGE OF SPIRES
IN OLDENBURG, INDIANA.

2211
01:29:33,702 --> 01:29:37,207
HAVE YOU NO DECENCY?

2212
01:29:37,240 --> 01:29:40,342
OH, NO, GRASSHOPPERS
HAVE SCALED TO THE VERY TOP

2213
01:29:40,375 --> 01:29:41,643
OF OLD EARL "FATHA" HINES.

2214
01:29:41,677 --> 01:29:43,345
[IMITATING SCREAMS]

2215
01:29:44,747 --> 01:29:46,182
WE ARE WITNESSING A TIME

2216
01:29:46,215 --> 01:29:48,852
WHEN THE BEASTS HAVE RECLAIMED
EARL "FATHA" HINES.

2217
01:29:48,885 --> 01:29:50,620
- CROW.
- I'M PETER GRAVES.

2218
01:29:50,653 --> 01:29:51,953
- CROW!
- I'M DONE.

2219
01:29:51,987 --> 01:29:53,088
I'D SAY.

2220
01:29:53,122 --> 01:29:54,890
BACK TO YOU.

2221
01:29:54,923 --> 01:29:58,027
OH, MAYBE WE SHOULD GO
BACK DOWN THERE.

2222
01:29:58,060 --> 01:29:59,628
REMEMBER WHAT HAPPENED
LAST TIME.

2223
01:29:59,662 --> 01:30:00,663
BACK TO YOU, SIRS.

2224
01:30:01,863 --> 01:30:03,967
KEEP YOUR HANDS UP, FRANK.

2225
01:30:04,000 --> 01:30:06,702
KEEP YOUR HANDS UP,
FRANK.

2226
01:30:06,735 --> 01:30:10,438
AH, MIKE, CAUGHT US
IN THE MIDDLE
OF OUR DAILY ROUTINE.

2227
01:30:10,472 --> 01:30:12,408
WHAT'S THAT THEY SAY
ABOUT BOXING, FRANK?

2228
01:30:12,442 --> 01:30:13,708
IT'S THE ONLY REAL SPORT.

2229
01:30:13,742 --> 01:30:15,077
IT'S THE ONLY HONEST SPORT.

2230
01:30:15,110 --> 01:30:16,645
IT'S THE SPORT OF MEN.

2231
01:30:16,678 --> 01:30:17,813
ABSOLUTELY RIGHT.

2232
01:30:17,847 --> 01:30:19,315
GRAB YOURSELF A BEER

2233
01:30:19,348 --> 01:30:21,783
AND GRAB ME ONE, TOO,
FELLOW FIGHTER.

2234
01:30:21,817 --> 01:30:23,218
OKAY, BECAUSE WE'RE MEN.

2235
01:30:23,252 --> 01:30:24,820
WE ARE MEN!

2236
01:30:24,853 --> 01:30:26,122
YES, YOU'VE MADE YOUR POINT,
FRANK.

2237
01:30:26,155 --> 01:30:27,357
- WE'RE MEN!
- YES, FRANK.

2238
01:30:27,390 --> 01:30:29,158
OH!

2239
01:30:29,192 --> 01:30:31,760
YOU WANT A PIECE OF ME?
COME ON, COME ON.
HUH?

2240
01:30:37,867 --> 01:30:39,202
OH, OH, FRANK.

2241
01:30:39,235 --> 01:30:40,770
FRANK, PLEASE.

2242
01:30:40,803 --> 01:30:42,070
PLEASE, ENOUGH.

2243
01:30:42,103 --> 01:30:45,273
I HAVE TO GET THE BUTTON.

2244
01:30:47,008 --> 01:30:48,343
[CHUCKLING]

2245
01:31:57,780 --> 01:32:00,082
ALL RIGHT, MEN,
INTO THE WOODS.

2246
01:32:04,920 --> 01:32:08,323
THIS HAS BEEN A PRESENTATION
FROM COMEDY CENTRAL.
